est.ts\nroom.ts\n2: * @file The engine in a page (PLAN.md §6.4, §6.9, §8.3, WP 2.7): `createEngine({ canvas, scenes, levels })` registers\n37: * // const engine = await createEngine({ canvas, scenes: ['box:room'] }); // labs/box/main.ts\n109:  /** The page's scenes, by id (registered with defineScene); `?scene` picks one, the first by default. */\n110:  scenes: readonly string[];\n112:   * The levels the page's scenes load, by id: their text (Vite's `?raw` import), file and material swaps (the level\n122:  /** Where scenes, levels, components, settings and materials are declared (the shared registry). */\n277:    routes = parseRoutes(search, { scenes: options.scenes, registry, hash: options.hash ?? location.hash, log });\n281:      if (scene && !new URLSearchParams(search).has('scene') && options.scenes.includes(scene)) {","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Ktph99zqjMqm6cm1uDeZRG","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgj99e56jAdLQj1xkqszY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DygUxqdTcbeUVYBJLi4jQE","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211947__x8ab6bc/work/.research/my-3dge/engine/app/engine.ts"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1535,"cache_read_input_tokens":130176,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1535},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b0d0401-1a79-4c2f-8a33-ba9239fdbfed","uuid":"2a7eb31d-b4fb-475e-b99d-1d278f123001","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:21:43.944Z","request_id":"req_011Cgj99dpibvpSxE9UeANtF","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01DygUxqdTcbeUVYBJLi4jQE":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211947__x8ab6bc/work/.research/my-3dge/engine/app/engine.ts"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DygUxqdTcbeUVYBJLi4jQE","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t/**\n2\t * @file The engine in a page (PLAN.md §6.4, §6.9, §8.3, WP 2.7): `createEngine({ canvas, scenes, levels })` registers\n3\t * the levels the page imported as text, reads the page's routes (engine/app/routes.ts: `?scene ?seed ?cam ?replay`,\n4\t * settings by path, a gallery link `#gallery/<kind>/<id>` with its driver, engine/dev/galleryShoot.ts), starts the\n5\t * scene as a recorded run with its view (engine/app/headless.ts, engine/app/view.ts), publishes the run's inspector\n6\t * as `window.__engine`, starts the renderer (WebGPU or nothing, engine/gfx/renderer.ts) and the post-processing chain\n7\t * every frame and shot is drawn through (engine/gfx/post/chain.ts: the view settings `post.look`, `post.filters` and\n8\t * `post.show`; the look's sky and style, engine/app/look.ts), warms up every pipeline the view needs (`gfx.warmUp`,\n9\t * engine/gfx/warmup.ts), draws the first frame, then runs the frame loop (engine/app/loop.ts): the devices sampled\n10\t * into intents (engine/input/input.ts; `__engine.input` drives the same session), fixed steps from the clock, the\n11\t * view drawn at the clock's alpha; the map follows the camera, the look the view settings `input.*`, the aim the\n12\t * view, and a click takes the pointer lock where the map's mouse looks (WP 13.9).\n13\t *\n14\t * Ready or error (§8.3): `__engine.ready` turns true once the first frame is done on the GPU, never after a startup\n15\t * error; every failure (a frame that throws stops the loop) is one record in `__engine.errors` (the log's), shown as\n16\t * page text by the error overlay (engine/dev/overlay.ts), so a startup crash is one line, never a hang. Without WebGPU\n17\t * (`GFX_NO_WEBGPU`) the sim still runs, and `__engine` still steps it; only `render` and `shot` throw.\n18\t *\n19\t * Every frame drawn is timed by the run's stats meter, which reads the renderer's counts (`__engine.stats()`,\n20\t * engine/dev/stats.ts), and feeds the performance governor (engine/dev/governor.ts: `auto`'s tier by frame rate). The\n21\t * rendering members (engine/app/viewMembers.ts) draw through the page's drawing (engine/app/drawing.ts: `render(n)`,\n22\t * `shot`, and `replay(text)` drawing a frame after every step, §6.7). `?replay=<name>` plays one of `options.replays`\n23\t * in real time from step 0 (without `?scene`, in its own scene if the page has it), then hands back to the devices.\n24\t * The overlay (engine/ui/overlay.ts, `engine.ui`, WP 6.7) shows the sim's hits as damage numbers\n25\t * (engine/app/damageNumbers.ts); `onFrame` runs a page's own presentation (`EngineFrame`). A page's front end (WP\n26\t * 13.25): `store` keeps the bindings across sessions; while `modal()` holds the page (a menu, a photo mode) the devices\n27\t * still read the system layer, but no intent reaches the run; `cameraInput()` is laid over each frame's camera input.\n28\t *\n29\t * Touch (WP 3.12, ADR-0021: built, not tested): the app wires the touch device (engine/input/devices/touch.ts), the\n30\t * page's chrome, the touch layer from `touchLayout` and swiping (engine/ui/), the quality budget's pixel caps\n31\t * (engine/gfx/quality.ts) and, in touch mode, the loop's 60 fps cap; the menu button pauses, then calls `onMenu`.\n32\t *\n33\t * Invariants: rendering never writes the sim (doctrine: WebGPU only): the loop steps the session only with intents and\n34\t * recorded settings; cameras and view settings never reach the hash; time comes from the frames, never a wall clock.\n35\t *\n36\t * @example\n37\t * // const engine = await createEngine({ canvas, scenes: ['box:room'] }); // labs/box/main.ts\n38\t * // engine.ready; // true once the first frame is drawn\n39\t * @see tests/e2e/box.spec.ts\n40\t */\n41\timport '../dev/members'; // declares the kind inspectorMember before input/devices/inspector registers its members\n42\timport {\n43\t  codeError,\n44\t  codeInfo,\n45\t  defineCodes,\n46\t  log as sharedLog,\n47\t  type CodeValues,\n48\t  type ErrorRecord,\n49\t  type Log,\n50\t} from '../core/log';\n51\timport { registry as sharedRegistry, type Registry } from '../core/registry';\n52\timport type { Settings } from '../core/settings';\n53\timport { createGalleryDriver, type GalleryDriver } from '../dev/galleryShoot';\n54\timport { createOverlay } from '../dev/overlay';\n55\timport { createMaterialLibrary } from '../gfx/materials/library';\n56\timport { createStyleSet } from '../gfx/materials/styles';\n57\timport type { QualitySetting } from '../gfx/quality';\n58\timport { createPost } from '../gfx/post/chain';\n59\timport { definePostSettings } from '../gfx/post/settings';\n60\timport { createRenderer } from '../gfx/renderer';\n61\timport { warmsAsked } from '../gfx/warmup';\n62\timport type { CameraInput } from '../gfx/cameras/pose';\n63\timport { connectVirtualDevice } from '../input/devices/inspector';\n64\timport { createInput, type CameraLike, type Input } from '../input/input';\n65\timport { lookOptions } from '../input/look';\n66\timport type { TouchSetting } from '../input/devices/touch';\n67\timport { createChrome } from '../ui/chrome';\n68\timport { attachSwipes } from '../ui/swipe';\n69\timport { createTouchLayer, getTouchLayout, type TouchLayout } from '../ui/touch';\n70\timport type { Inspector } from '../dev/inspector';\n71\timport { createOverlay as createUi, type Overlay } from '../ui/overlay';\n72\timport { createDamageNumbers } from './damageNumbers';\n73\timport { createPageDrawing, type EngineFrame, type PageParts } from './drawing';\n74\timport { createPageLook } from './look';\n75\timport { createAppHost, type AppRun } from './headless';\n76\timport { createLoop, type Loop } from './loop';\n77\timport { textStorage, type Store } from './store';\n78\timport { createPlayback, type Playback } from './playback';\n79\timport { defineLevel } from '../world/level/level';\n80\timport { parseRoutes, type Routes } from './routes';\n81\timport { createGovernor, governorMemory } from '../dev/governor';\n82\t\n83\t/** The codes this module raises, with their fixes. */\n84\texport const ENGINE_CODES = defineCodes('app', {\n85\t  APP_START: {\n86\t    template: 'the page failed to start: {message}',\n87\t    fix: 'the console names the cause; node x shot <page> reports it headless',\n88\t  },\n89\t  APP_FRAME: {\n90\t    template: 'a frame threw, so the loop stopped: {message}',\n91\t    fix: 'the console names the cause; reload the page to start again, or read __engine.state() to see where the run stands',\n92\t  },\n93\t  APP_NO_REPLAY: {\n94\t    template: 'the page has no replay {name}',\n95\t    fix: 'use one of: {names}',\n96\t  },\n97\t  APP_NO_FRAME: {\n98\t    template: 'no frame was drawn in {tries} tries: the warm-up never finished',\n99\t    fix: 'read __engine.errors for GFX_WARMUP_FAILED; node x shot <page> reports it headless',\n100\t  },\n101\t});\n102\t\n103\texport type { EngineFrame, FrameWorld } from './drawing';\n104\t\n105\t/** How a page starts the engine. */\n106\texport interface EngineOptions {\n107\t  /** The canvas it draws into; the page sizes it with CSS. */\n108\t  canvas: HTMLCanvasElement;\n109\t  /** The page's scenes, by id (registered with defineScene); `?scene` picks one, the first by default. */\n110\t  scenes: readonly string[];\n111\t  /**\n112\t   * The levels the page's scenes load, by id: their text (Vite's `?raw` import), file and material swaps (the level\n113\t   * entry's `materials`); registered unless already.\n114\t   */\n115\t  levels?: Readonly<Record<string, { text: string; file?: string; materials?: Readonly<Record<string, string>> }>>;\n116\t  /** Replays the page offers by name (`?replay=<name>`): name → its text, loaded when asked for. */\n117\t  replays?: Readonly<Record<string, () => Promise<string>>>;\n118\t  /** The query to read (`location.search`). */\n119\t  search?: string;\n120\t  /** The hash to read (`location.hash`): a gallery deep link, `#gallery/<kind>/<id>` (engine/app/routes.ts). */\n121\t  hash?: string;\n122\t  /** Where scenes, levels, components, settings and materials are declared (the shared registry). */\n123\t  registry?: Registry;\n124\t  /** Where errors and advice go (the shared log). */\n125\t  log?: Log;\n126\t  /** The page's touch buttons, a `touchlayout` id (engine/ui/touch.ts); without it, only the touch stick shows. */\n127\t  touchLayout?: string;\n128\t  /**\n129\t   * The action map the devices read (`actionMap:thirdPerson` by default): its actions are the intents' buttons. A\n130\t   * function gives the map for the camera now (its code, `cam3=first,…`), so each camera mode has its own (WP 13.9).\n131\t   */\n132\t  actionMap?: string | ((camera: string) => string);\n133\t  /** A view action of the map pressed (its `view`: a camera switch, a view's turn), as it happens (WP 13.9). */\n134\t  onView?: (action: string) => void;\n135\t  /** Opens the page's menu, called after the touch menu button has paused the game. */\n136\t  onMenu?: () => void;\n137\t  /** The page's own presentation (its sound): called once per drawn frame, after the draw, with the run to read. */\n138\t  onFrame?: (frame: EngineFrame) => void;\n139\t  /** Where the bindings are kept across sessions (`createStore`, engine/app/store.ts); in memory without it. */\n140\t  store?: Store;\n141\t  /** True while the page's front end holds the devices (a menu, a photo mode): no intent reaches the run. */\n142\t  modal?: () => boolean;\n143\t  /** Camera input laid over the devices' each drawn frame, field by field (a photo mode's fly keys and drag look). */\n144\t  cameraInput?: () => CameraInput | undefined;\n145\t}\n146\t\n147\t/** A started engine. */\n148\texport interface Engine {\n149\t  /** The inspector, also `window.__engine`; null when the scene could not start. */\n150\t  readonly inspector: Inspector | null;\n151\t  /** True once the first frame is drawn; never after a startup error. */\n152\t  readonly ready: boolean;\n153\t  /** What the query asked for; null when it could not be read. */\n154\t  readonly routes: Routes | null;\n155\t  /** The game's HTML/CSS overlay over the canvas (engine/ui/overlay.ts); null until the renderer started. */\n156\t  readonly ui: Overlay | null;\n157\t  /** The devices (engine/input/input.ts): prompts, rebinding, the map in use; null when the scene could not start. */\n158\t  readonly input: Input | null;\n159\t  /** Stops the frame loop. */\n160\t  stop(): void;\n161\t}\n162\t\n163\t/** What `?replay=<name>` asked for: the replay, ready to play, or why there is none (raised once the page is up). */\n164\tinterface Asked {\n165\t  playback?: Playback;\n166\t  error?: unknown;\n167\t}\n168\t\n169\t/** Reads the replay `name` of `replays` before the run starts, so its scene can start (see the file comment). */\n170\tasync function readReplay(name: string, replays: EngineOptions['replays']): Promise<Asked> {\n171\t  const load = replays?.[name];\n172\t  if (!load) {\n173\t    const names = Object.keys(replays ?? {}).sort();\n174\t    return { error: codeError('APP_NO_REPLAY', { name, names: names.join(', ') || 'none' }) };\n175\t  }\n176\t  try {\n177\t    return { playback: createPlayback(JSON.parse(await load())) };\n178\t  } catch (error) {\n179\t    return { error };\n180\t  }\n181\t}\n182\t\n183\t/** A store that reads and writes whichever run's settings are current, for the renderer made once. */\n184\tfunction currentSettings(run: () => AppRun): Settings {\n185\t  return new Proxy({} as Settings, {\n186\t    get(_, key: keyof Settings) {\n187\t      const store = run().session.settings;\n188\t      const value = store[key];\n189\t      return typeof value === 'function' ? (value as (...args: unknown[]) => unknown).bind(store) : value;\n190\t    },\n191\t  });\n192\t}\n193\t\n194\t/**\n195\t * The log record for a thrown value: its own code and values when it is a coded error (a `GfxError` carries only its\n196\t * message, so the values are read back from it through the code's template), else `code` with the message.\n197\t */\n198\texport function recordOf(error: unknown, code: string): [string, CodeValues] {\n199\t  const coded = error as { code?: unknown; values?: CodeValues; message?: unknown };\n200\t  const message = String(coded?.message ?? error);\n201\t  const info = typeof coded?.code === 'string' ? codeInfo(coded.code) : undefined;\n202\t  if (!info) return [code, { message }];\n203\t  if (coded.values) return [info.code, coded.values];\n204\t  const names: string[] = [];\n205\t  const pattern = info.template\n206\t    .split(/\\{(\\w+)\\}/)\n207\t    .map((part, i) => (i % 2 ? (names.push(part), '(.*)') : part.replace(/[.*+?^${}()|[\\]\\\\]/g, '\\\\$&')))\n208\t    .join('');\n209\t  const found = new RegExp(`^${pattern}$`, 's').exec(message);\n210\t  return [info.code, Object.fromEntries(names.map((name, i) => [name, found?.[i + 1] ?? '?']))];\n211\t}\n212\t\n213\t/** Starts the engine in a page (see the file comment); resolves once it is up or has failed. */\n214\texport async function createEngine(options: EngineOptions): Promise<Engine> {\n215\t  const log = options.log ?? sharedLog;\n216\t  const registry = options.registry ?? sharedRegistry;\n217\t  const overlay = createOverlay(document);\n218\t  overlay.status('Loading…');\n219\t  let routes: Routes | null = null;\n220\t  let loop: Loop | null = null;\n221\t  const parts: PageParts = { run: null, gfx: null, post: null, look: null, input: null, layer: null, ui: null, numbers: null, governor: createGovernor({ log, memory: governorMemory(options.store, () => routes?.scene) }), cameraInput: options.cameraInput, ready: false }; // prettier-ignore\n222\t  const fail = (error: unknown, code = 'APP_START'): ErrorRecord => {\n223\t    const record = log.error(...recordOf(error, code), error);\n224\t    overlay.error(record);\n225\t    return record;\n226\t  };\n227\t  const signals = {\n228\t    get ready() {\n229\t      return false;\n230\t    },\n231\t    get errors() {\n232\t      return log.errors.map((record) => ({ ...record }));\n233\t    },\n234\t    info: () => ({ page: location.pathname, headless: true }),\n235\t  };\n236\t  Object.assign(window, { __engine: signals });\n237\t  const engine: Engine = {\n238\t    get inspector() {\n239\t      return parts.run?.inspector ?? null;\n240\t    },\n241\t    get ready() {\n242\t      return parts.ready;\n243\t    },\n244\t    get routes() {\n245\t      return routes;\n246\t    },\n247\t    get ui() {\n248\t      return parts.ui;\n249\t    },\n250\t    get input() {\n251\t      return parts.input;\n252\t    },\n253\t    stop: () => loop?.stop(),\n254\t  };\n255\t\n256\t  let layout: TouchLayout | null = null;\n257\t  let playback: Playback | null = null;\n258\t  const viewNow = () => parts.run!.view!;\n259\t  const settingsNow = currentSettings(() => parts.run!);\n260\t  const chrome = createChrome(document);\n261\t  let gallery: GalleryDriver | null = null; // a gallery deep link's, fitting its camera and bursting its emitter\n262\t  const onFrame = (shown: EngineFrame) => {\n263\t    gallery?.frame(shown.dt);\n264\t    options.onFrame?.(shown);\n265\t  };\n266\t  const { drawing, frame, settle, warmCameras } = createPageDrawing(parts, { chrome, settings: settingsNow, onFrame }); // prettier-ignore\n267\t  let warming: Promise<void> | null = null;\n268\t  let asked: Asked | null = null;\n269\t  let materials: ReturnType<typeof createMaterialLibrary> | null = null;\n270\t\n271\t  try {\n272\t    definePostSettings(registry);\n273\t    for (const [id, level] of Object.entries(options.levels ?? {})) {\n274\t      if (!registry.has('level', id)) defineLevel(id, level, registry);\n275\t    }\n276\t    const search = options.search ?? location.search;\n277\t    routes = parseRoutes(search, { scenes: options.scenes, registry, hash: options.hash ?? location.hash, log });\n278\t    if (routes.replay !== undefined) {\n279\t      asked = await readReplay(routes.replay, options.replays);\n280\t      const scene = asked.playback?.replay.scene;\n281\t      if (scene && !new URLSearchParams(search).has('scene') && options.scenes.includes(scene)) {\n282\t        routes = { ...routes, scene };\n283\t      }\n284\t    }\n285\t    if (options.touchLayout !== undefined) layout = getTouchLayout(options.touchLayout, registry);\n286\t    materials = createMaterialLibrary({ registry });\n287\t    const { scene, seed, settings, cam } = routes;\n288\t    parts.run = createAppHost({ scene, seed, settings, cam, registry, log, drawing, materials });\n289\t    if (routes.gallery) gallery = createGalleryDriver(routes.gallery, () => parts.run!, registry);\n290\t  } catch (error) {\n291\t    fail(error);\n292\t    return engine;\n293\t  }\n294\t  const started = parts.run;\n295\t  Object.assign(window, { __engine: started.inspector });\n296\t  const onTap = (name: string) => {\n297\t    if (name === 'game') chrome.closeTopPanel();\n298\t    if (name !== 'menu') return;\n299\t    started.clock.pause();\n300\t    options.onMenu?.();\n301\t  };\n302\t  const touchMode = () => settingsNow.get<TouchSetting>('touch');\n303\t  const mapFor = () => {\n304\t    const asked = options.actionMap;\n305\t    return (typeof asked === 'function' ? asked(viewNow().camera.code()) : asked) ?? 'actionMap:thirdPerson';\n306\t  };\n307\t  const declared = (path: string) => registry.kinds().includes('setting') && registry.has('setting', path);\n308\t  const look = () => lookOptions((path) => (declared(path) ? settingsNow.get(path) : undefined));\n309\t  const input = (parts.input = createInput({ window, document, element: options.canvas, registry, log, touchMode, onTap, map: mapFor(), look, onView: options.onView, storage: options.store && textStorage(options.store) })); // prettier-ignore\n310\t  /** The camera the devices read: its heading, its look, and the aim from the view (engine/input/aim.ts). */\n311\t  const camera: CameraLike = {\n312\t    yaw: () => viewNow().camera.yaw(),\n313\t    pose: () => viewNow().camera.pose(),\n314\t    aim: (rule, devices) => viewNow().aim(rule, devices),\n315\t  };\n316\t  /** The map for the camera now, and the pointer lock: a click takes it where the map's mouse looks; pause gives it back. */ // prettier-ignore\n317\t  const sample = (now: number) => {\n318\t    const id = mapFor();\n319\t    if (id !== input.bindings.map.id) input.use(id);\n320\t    if (input.mouse?.locked && (!input.bindings.map.lock || started.clock.paused)) input.mouse.unlock();\n321\t    const intents = input.sample(camera, now);\n322\t    return options.modal?.() ? {} : intents;\n323\t  };\n324\t  options.canvas.addEventListener('click', () => {\n325\t    if (input.bindings.map.lock && !started.clock.paused && !input.mouse?.locked) input.mouse?.lock();\n326\t  });\n327\t  parts.layer = createTouchLayer(document, layout);\n328\t  attachSwipes(document);\n329\t  connectVirtualDevice(started.host, input.virtual);\n330\t  try {\n331\t    parts.gfx = await createRenderer(options.canvas, { settings: currentSettings(() => started), registry, log });\n332\t  } catch (error) {\n333\t    fail(error);\n334\t    return engine;\n335\t  }\n336\t  const gfx = parts.gfx;\n337\t  parts.numbers = createDamageNumbers((parts.ui = createUi({ canvas: options.canvas })));\n338\t  try {\n339\t    gfx.renderer.shadowMap.enabled = true;\n340\t    const styles = createStyleSet({ library: materials!, registry });\n341\t    const post = (parts.post = createPost(gfx, { settings: currentSettings(() => started), registry, log, styles }));\n342\t    const budget = () => parts.governor!.budget(settingsNow.get<QualitySetting>('quality'), input.touch?.active ?? false); // prettier-ignore\n343\t    parts.look = createPageLook({ post, styles, warmup: gfx.warmup, resolution: gfx.resolution, library: materials!, quality: budget, asked: () => warmsAsked(settingsNow) }); // prettier-ignore\n344\t    post.attach(gfx.warmup);\n345\t    viewNow().stage.register(gfx.warmup, gfx.features);\n346\t    await warmCameras();\n347\t    await settle(1, 0);\n348\t  } catch (error) {\n349\t    fail(error);\n350\t    return engine;\n351\t  }\n352\t  const step = (intents: Record<string, unknown>) => {\n353\t    if (playback && !playback.done) {\n354\t      playback.step(started.session);\n355\t      started.stepped(); // its hit-stops reach the clock as in live play\n356\t    } else {\n357\t      playback = null;\n358\t      started.stepOnce(intents);\n359\t    }\n360\t  };\n361\t  loop = createLoop({\n362\t    clock: () => started.clock,\n363\t    sample,\n364\t    step,\n365\t    draw: ({ alpha, dt }) => {\n366\t      // frozen in a reproducible run: a replay playing, or the governor turned off (engine/dev/governor.ts)\n367\t      parts.governor!.freeze((playback !== null && !playback.done) || !settingsNow.get<boolean>('gfx.governor'));\n368\t      if (warming) return;\n369\t      const report = frame(alpha, dt);\n370\t      if (!report.drawn && report.warming) warming = warmCameras().finally(() => (warming = null));\n371\t    },\n372\t    hold: () => started.playing,\n373\t    cap: () => input.touch?.active ?? false,\n374\t    onError: (error) => fail(error, 'APP_FRAME'),\n375\t  });\n376\t  parts.ready = true;\n377\t  overlay.hide();\n378\t  loop.start();\n379\t  const replay = asked?.playback;\n380\t  if (asked && !replay) fail(asked.error);\n381\t  else if (replay) {\n382\t    try {\n383\t      started.begin(replay.replay);\n384\t      playback = replay;\n385\t    } catch (error) {\n386\t      fail(error);\n387\t    }\n388\t  }\n389\t  return engine;\n390\t}\n391\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b0d0401-1a79-4c2f-8a33-ba9239fdbfed","uuid":"9e61593e-a865-4d1e-bb08-b3d019d366b7","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:21:43.965Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211947__x8ab6bc/work/.research/my-3dge/engine/app/engine.ts","content":"/**\n * @file The engine in a page (PLAN.md §6.4, §6.9, §8.3, WP 2.7): `createEngine({ canvas, scenes, levels })` registers\n * the levels the page imported as text, reads the page's routes (engine/app/routes.ts: `?scene ?seed ?cam ?replay`,\n * settings by path, a gallery link `#gallery/<kind>/<id>` with its driver, engine/dev/galleryShoot.ts), starts the\n * scene as a recorded run with its view (engine/app/headless.ts, engine/app/view.ts), publishes the run's inspector\n * as `window.__engine`, starts the renderer (WebGPU or nothing, engine/gfx/renderer.ts) and the post-processing chain\n * every frame and shot is drawn through (engine/gfx/post/chain.ts: the view settings `post.look`, `post.filters` and\n * `post.show`; the look's sky and style, engine/app/look.ts), warms up every pipeline the view needs (`gfx.warmUp`,\n * engine/gfx/warmup.ts), draws the first frame, then runs the frame loop (engine/app/loop.ts): the devices sampled\n * into intents (engine/input/input.ts; `__engine.input` drives the same session), fixed steps from the clock, the\n * view drawn at the clock's alpha; the map follows the camera, the look the view settings `input.*`, the aim the\n * view, and a click takes the pointer lock where the map's mouse looks (WP 13.9).\n *\n * Ready or error (§8.3): `__engine.ready` turns true once the first frame is done on the GPU, never after a startup\n * error; every failure (a frame that throws stops the loop) is one record in `__engine.errors` (the log's), shown as\n * page text by the error overlay (engine/dev/overlay.ts), so a startup crash is one line, never a hang. Without WebGPU\n * (`GFX_NO_WEBGPU`) the sim still runs, and `__engine` still steps it; only `render` and `shot` throw.\n *\n * Every frame drawn is timed by the run's stats meter, which reads the renderer's counts (`__engine.stats()`,\n * engine/dev/stats.ts), and feeds the performance governor (engine/dev/governor.ts: `auto`'s tier by frame rate). The\n * rendering members (engine/app/viewMembers.ts) draw through the page's drawing (engine/app/drawing.ts: `render(n)`,\n * `shot`, and `replay(text)` drawing a frame after every step, §6.7). `?replay=<name>` plays one of `options.replays`\n * in real time from step 0 (without `?scene`, in its own scene if the page has it), then hands back to the devices.\n * The overlay (engine/ui/overlay.ts, `engine.ui`, WP 6.7) shows the sim's hits as damage numbers\n * (engine/app/damageNumbers.ts); `onFrame` runs a page's own presentation (`EngineFrame`). A page's front end (WP\n * 13.25): `store` keeps the bindings across sessions; while `modal()` holds the page (a menu, a photo mode) the devices\n * still read the system layer, but no intent reaches the run; `cameraInput()` is laid over each frame's camera input.\n *\n * Touch (WP 3.12, ADR-0021: built, not tested): the app wires the touch device (engine/input/devices/touch.ts), the\n * page's chrome, the touch layer from `touchLayout` and swiping (engine/ui/), the quality budget's pixel caps\n * (engine/gfx/quality.ts) and, in touch mode, the loop's 60 fps cap; the menu button pauses, then calls `onMenu`.\n *\n * Invariants: rendering never writes the sim (doctrine: WebGPU only): the loop steps the session only with intents and\n * recorded settings; cameras and view settings never reach the hash; time comes from the frames, never a wall clock.\n *\n * @example\n * // const engine = await createEngine({ canvas, scenes: ['box:room'] }); // labs/box/main.ts\n * // engine.ready; // true once the first frame is drawn\n * @see tests/e2e/box.spec.ts\n */\nimport '../dev/members'; // declares the kind inspectorMember before input/devices/inspector registers its members\nimport {\n  codeError,\n  codeInfo,\n  defineCodes,\n  log as sharedLog,\n  type CodeValues,\n  type ErrorRecord,\n  type Log,\n} from '../core/log';\nimport { registry as sharedRegistry, type Registry } from '../core/registry';\nimport type { Settings } from '../core/settings';\nimport { createGalleryDriver, type GalleryDriver } from '../dev/galleryShoot';\nimport { createOverlay } from '../dev/overlay';\nimport { createMaterialLibrary } from '../gfx/materials/library';\nimport { createStyleSet } from '../gfx/materials/styles';\nimport type { QualitySetting } from '../gfx/quality';\nimport { createPost } from '../gfx/post/chain';\nimport { definePostSettings } from '../gfx/post/settings';\nimport { createRenderer } from '../gfx/renderer';\nimport { warmsAsked } from '../gfx/warmup';\nimport type { CameraInput } from '../gfx/cameras/pose';\nimport { connectVirtualDevice } from '../input/devices/inspector';\nimport { createInput, type CameraLike, type Input } from '../input/input';\nimport { lookOptions } from '../input/look';\nimport type { TouchSetting } from '../input/devices/touch';\nimport { createChrome } from '../ui/chrome';\nimport { attachSwipes } from '../ui/swipe';\nimport { createTouchLayer, getTouchLayout, type TouchLayout } from '../ui/touch';\nimport type { Inspector } from '../dev/inspector';\nimport { createOverlay as createUi, type Overlay } from '../ui/overlay';\nimport { createDamageNumbers } from './damageNumbers';\nimport { createPageDrawing, type EngineFrame, type PageParts } from './drawing';\nimport { createPageLook } from './look';\nimport { createAppHost, type AppRun } from './headless';\nimport { createLoop, type Loop } from './loop';\nimport { textStorage, type Store } from './store';\nimport { createPlayback, type Playback } from './playback';\nimport { defineLevel } from '../world/level/level';\nimport { parseRoutes, type Routes } from './routes';\nimport { createGovernor, governorMemory } from '../dev/governor';\n\n/** The codes this module raises, with their fixes. */\nexport const ENGINE_CODES = defineCodes('app', {\n  APP_START: {\n    template: 'the page failed to start: {message}',\n    fix: 'the console names the cause; node x shot <page> reports it headless',\n  },\n  APP_FRAME: {\n    template: 'a frame threw, so the loop stopped: {message}',\n    fix: 'the console names the cause; reload the page to start again, or read __engine.state() to see where the run stands',\n  },\n  APP_NO_REPLAY: {\n    template: 'the page has no replay {name}',\n    fix: 'use one of: {names}',\n  },\n  APP_NO_FRAME: {\n    template: 'no frame was drawn in {tries} tries: the warm-up never finished',\n    fix: 'read __engine.errors for GFX_WARMUP_FAILED; node x shot <page> reports it headless',\n  },\n});\n\nexport type { EngineFrame, FrameWorld } from './drawing';\n\n/** How a page starts the engine. */\nexport interface EngineOptions {\n  /** The canvas it draws into; the page sizes it with CSS. */\n  canvas: HTMLCanvasElement;\n  /** The page's scenes, by id (registered with defineScene); `?scene` picks one, the first by default. */\n  scenes: readonly string[];\n  /**\n   * The levels the page's scenes load, by id: their text (Vite's `?raw` import), file and material swaps (the level\n   * entry's `materials`); registered unless already.\n   */\n  levels?: Readonly<Record<string, { text: string; file?: string; materials?: Readonly<Record<string, string>> }>>;\n  /** Replays the page offers by name (`?replay=<name>`): name → its text, loaded when asked for. */\n  replays?: Readonly<Record<string, () => Promise<string>>>;\n  /** The query to read (`location.search`). */\n  search?: string;\n  /** The hash to read (`location.hash`): a gallery deep link, `#gallery/<kind>/<id>` (engine/app/routes.ts). */\n  hash?: string;\n  /** Where scenes, levels, components, settings and materials are declared (the shared registry). */\n  registry?: Registry;\n  /** Where errors and advice go (the shared log). */\n  log?: Log;\n  /** The page's touch buttons, a `touchlayout` id (engine/ui/touch.ts); without it, only the touch stick shows. */\n  touchLayout?: string;\n  /**\n   * The action map the devices read (`actionMap:thirdPerson` by default): its actions are the intents' buttons. A\n   * function gives the map for the camera now (its code, `cam3=first,…`), so each camera mode has its own (WP 13.9).\n   */\n  actionMap?: string | ((camera: string) => string);\n  /** A view action of the map pressed (its `view`: a camera switch, a view's turn), as it happens (WP 13.9). */\n  onView?: (action: string) => void;\n  /** Opens the page's menu, called after the touch menu button has paused the game. */\n  onMenu?: () => void;\n  /** The page's own presentation (its sound): called once per drawn frame, after the draw, with the run to read. */\n  onFrame?: (frame: EngineFrame) => void;\n  /** Where the bindings are kept across sessions (`createStore`, engine/app/store.ts); in memory without it. */\n  store?: Store;\n  /** True while the page's front end holds the devices (a menu, a photo mode): no intent reaches the run. */\n  modal?: () => boolean;\n  /** Camera input laid over the devices' each drawn frame, field by field (a photo mode's fly keys and drag look). */\n  cameraInput?: () => CameraInput | undefined;\n}\n\n/** A started engine. */\nexport interface Engine {\n  /** The inspector, also `window.__engine`; null when the scene could not start. */\n  readonly inspector: Inspector | null;\n  /** True once the first frame is drawn; never after a startup error. */\n  readonly ready: boolean;\n  /** What the query asked for; null when it could not be read. */\n  readonly routes: Routes | null;\n  /** The game's HTML/CSS overlay over the canvas (engine/ui/overlay.ts); null until the renderer started. */\n  readonly ui: Overlay | null;\n  /** The devices (engine/input/input.ts): prompts, rebinding, the map in use; null when the scene could not start. */\n  readonly input: Input | null;\n  /** Stops the frame loop. */\n  stop(): void;\n}\n\n/** What `?replay=<name>` asked for: the replay, ready to play, or why there is none (raised once the page is up). */\ninterface Asked {\n  playback?: Playback;\n  error?: unknown;\n}\n\n/** Reads the replay `name` of `replays` before the run starts, so its scene can start (see the file comment). */\nasync function readReplay(name: string, replays: EngineOptions['replays']): Promise<Asked> {\n  const load = replays?.[name];\n  if (!load) {\n    const names = Object.keys(replays ?? {}).sort();\n    return { error: codeError('APP_NO_REPLAY', { name, names: names.join(', ') || 'none' }) };\n  }\n  try {\n    return { playback: createPlayback(JSON.parse(await load())) };\n  } catch (error) {\n    return { error };\n  }\n}\n\n/** A store that reads and writes whichever run's settings are current, for the renderer made once. */\nfunction currentSettings(run: () => AppRun): Settings {\n  return new Proxy({} as Settings, {\n    get(_, key: keyof Settings) {\n      const store = run().session.settings;\n      const value = store[key];\n      return typeof value === 'function' ? (value as (...args: unknown[]) => unknown).bind(store) : value;\n    },\n  });\n}\n\n/**\n * The log record for a thrown value: its own code and values when it is a coded error (a `GfxError` carries only its\n * message, so the values are read back from it through the code's template), else `code` with the message.\n */\nexport function recordOf(error: unknown, code: string): [string, CodeValues] {\n  const coded = error as { code?: unknown; values?: CodeValues; message?: unknown };\n  const message = String(coded?.message ?? error);\n  const info = typeof coded?.code === 'string' ? codeInfo(coded.code) : undefined;\n  if (!info) return [code, { message }];\n  if (coded.values) return [info.code, coded.values];\n  const names: string[] = [];\n  const pattern = info.template\n    .split(/\\{(\\w+)\\}/)\n    .map((part, i) => (i % 2 ? (names.push(part), '(.*)') : part.replace(/[.*+?^${}()|[\\]\\\\]/g, '\\\\$&')))\n    .join('');\n  const found = new RegExp(`^${pattern}$`, 's').exec(message);\n  return [info.code, Object.fromEntries(names.map((name, i) => [name, found?.[i + 1] ?? '?']))];\n}\n\n/** Starts the engine in a page (see the file comment); resolves once it is up or has failed. */\nexport async function createEngine(options: EngineOptions): Promise<Engine> {\n  const log = options.log ?? sharedLog;\n  const registry = options.registry ?? sharedRegistry;\n  const overlay = createOverlay(document);\n  overlay.status('Loading…');\n  let routes: Routes | null = null;\n  let loop: Loop | null = null;\n  const parts: PageParts = { run: null, gfx: null, post: null, look: null, input: null, layer: null, ui: null, numbers: null, governor: createGovernor({ log, memory: governorMemory(options.store, () => routes?.scene) }), cameraInput: options.cameraInput, ready: false }; // prettier-ignore\n  const fail = (error: unknown, code = 'APP_START'): ErrorRecord => {\n    const record = log.error(...recordOf(error, code), error);\n    overlay.error(record);\n    return record;\n  };\n  const signals = {\n    get ready() {\n      return false;\n    },\n    get errors() {\n      return log.errors.map((record) => ({ ...record }));\n    },\n    info: () => ({ page: location.pathname, headless: true }),\n  };\n  Object.assign(window, { __engine: signals });\n  const engine: Engine = {\n    get inspector() {\n      return parts.run?.inspector ?? null;\n    },\n    get ready() {\n      return parts.ready;\n    },\n    get routes() {\n      return routes;\n    },\n    get ui() {\n      return parts.ui;\n    },\n    get input() {\n      return parts.input;\n    },\n    stop: () => loop?.stop(),\n  };\n\n  let layout: TouchLayout | null = null;\n  let playback: Playback | null = null;\n  const viewNow = () => parts.run!.view!;\n  const settingsNow = currentSettings(() => parts.run!);\n  const chrome = createChrome(document);\n  let gallery: GalleryDriver | null = null; // a gallery deep link's, fitting its camera and bursting its emitter\n  const onFrame = (shown: EngineFrame) => {\n    gallery?.frame(shown.dt);\n    options.onFrame?.(shown);\n  };\n  const { drawing, frame, settle, warmCameras } = createPageDrawing(parts, { chrome, settings: settingsNow, onFrame }); // prettier-ignore\n  let warming: Promise<void> | null = null;\n  let asked: Asked | null = null;\n  let materials: ReturnType<typeof createMaterialLibrary> | null = null;\n\n  try {\n    definePostSettings(registry);\n    for (const [id, level] of Object.entries(options.levels ?? {})) {\n      if (!registry.has('level', id)) defineLevel(id, level, registry);\n    }\n    const search = options.search ?? location.search;\n    routes = parseRoutes(search, { scenes: options.scenes, registry, hash: options.hash ?? location.hash, log });\n    if (routes.replay !== undefined) {\n      asked = await readReplay(routes.replay, options.replays);\n      const scene = asked.playback?.replay.scene;\n      if (scene && !new URLSearchParams(search).has('scene') && options.scenes.includes(scene)) {\n        routes = { ...routes, scene };\n      }\n    }\n    if (options.touchLayout !== undefined) layout = getTouchLayout(options.touchLayout, registry);\n    materials = createMaterialLibrary({ registry });\n    const { scene, seed, settings, cam } = routes;\n    parts.run = createAppHost({ scene, seed, settings, cam, registry, log, drawing, materials });\n    if (routes.gallery) gallery = createGalleryDriver(routes.gallery, () => parts.run!, registry);\n  } catch (error) {\n    fail(error);\n    return engine;\n  }\n  const started = parts.run;\n  Object.assign(window, { __engine: started.inspector });\n  const onTap = (name: string) => {\n    if (name === 'game') chrome.closeTopPanel();\n    if (name !== 'menu') return;\n    started.clock.pause();\n    options.onMenu?.();\n  };\n  const touchMode = () => settingsNow.get<TouchSetting>('touch');\n  const mapFor = () => {\n    const asked = options.actionMap;\n    return (typeof asked === 'function' ? asked(viewNow().camera.code()) : asked) ?? 'actionMap:thirdPerson';\n  };\n  const declared = (path: string) => registry.kinds().includes('setting') && registry.has('setting', path);\n  const look = () => lookOptions((path) => (declared(path) ? settingsNow.get(path) : undefined));\n  const input = (parts.input = createInput({ window, document, element: options.canvas, registry, log, touchMode, onTap, map: mapFor(), look, onView: options.onView, storage: options.store && textStorage(options.store) })); // prettier-ignore\n  /** The camera the devices read: its heading, its look, and the aim from the view (engine/input/aim.ts). */\n  const camera: CameraLike = {\n    yaw: () => viewNow().camera.yaw(),\n    pose: () => viewNow().camera.pose(),\n    aim: (rule, devices) => viewNow().aim(rule, devices),\n  };\n  /** The map for the camera now, and the pointer lock: a click takes it where the map's mouse looks; pause gives it back. */ // prettier-ignore\n  const sample = (now: number) => {\n    const id = mapFor();\n    if (id !== input.bindings.map.id) input.use(id);\n    if (input.mouse?.locked && (!input.bindings.map.lock || started.clock.paused)) input.mouse.unlock();\n    const intents = input.sample(camera, now);\n    return options.modal?.() ? {} : intents;\n  };\n  options.canvas.addEventListener('click', () => {\n    if (input.bindings.map.lock && !started.clock.paused && !input.mouse?.locked) input.mouse?.lock();\n  });\n  parts.layer = createTouchLayer(document, layout);\n  attachSwipes(document);\n  connectVirtualDevice(started.host, input.virtual);\n  try {\n    parts.gfx = await createRenderer(options.canvas, { settings: currentSettings(() => started), registry, log });\n  } catch (error) {\n    fail(error);\n    return engine;\n  }\n  const gfx = parts.gfx;\n  parts.numbers = createDamageNumbers((parts.ui = createUi({ canvas: options.canvas })));\n  try {\n    gfx.renderer.shadowMap.enabled = true;\n    const styles = createStyleSet({ library: materials!, registry });\n    const post = (parts.post = createPost(gfx, { settings: currentSettings(() => started), registry, log, styles }));\n    const budget = () => parts.governor!.budget(settingsNow.get<QualitySetting>('quality'), input.touch?.active ?? false); // prettier-ignore\n    parts.look = createPageLook({ post, styles, warmup: gfx.warmup, resolution: gfx.resolution, library: materials!, quality: budget, asked: () => warmsAsked(settingsNow) }); // prettier-ignore\n    post.attach(gfx.warmup);\n    viewNow().stage.register(gfx.warmup, gfx.features);\n    await warmCameras();\n    await settle(1, 0);\n  } catch (error) {\n    fail(error);\n    return engine;\n  }\n  const step = (intents: Record<string, unknown>) => {\n    if (playback && !playback.done) {\n      playback.step(started.session);\n      started.stepped(); // its hit-stops reach the clock as in live play\n    } else {\n      playback = null;\n      started.stepOnce(intents);\n    }\n  };\n  loop = createLoop({\n    clock: () => started.clock,\n    sample,\n    step,\n    draw: ({ alpha, dt }) => {\n      // frozen in a reproducible run: a replay playing, or the governor turned off (engine/dev/governor.ts)\n      parts.governor!.freeze((playback !== null && !playback.done) || !settingsNow.get<boolean>('gfx.governor'));\n      if (warming) return;\n      const report = frame(alpha, dt);\n      if (!report.drawn && report.warming) warming = warmCameras().finally(() => (warming = null));\n    },\n    hold: () => started.playing,\n    cap: () => input.touch?.active ?? false,\n    onError: (error) => fail(error, 'APP_FRAME'),\n  });\n  parts.ready = true;\n  overlay.hide();\n  loop.start();\n  const replay = asked?.playback;\n  if (asked && !replay) fail(asked.error);\n  else if (replay) {\n    try {\n      started.begin(replay.replay);\n      playback = replay;\n    } catch (error) {\n      fail(error);\n    }\n  }\n  return engine;\n}\n","numLines":391,"startLine":1,"totalLines":391}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01DygUxqdTcbeUVYBJLi4jQE","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgj99e56jAdLQj1xkqszY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FbaePisf48TpkzdCA85C2L","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211947__x8ab6bc/work/.research/my-3dge/engine/app/view.ts"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1535,"cache_read_input_tokens":130176,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1535},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b0d0401-1a79-4c2f-8a33-ba9239fdbfed","uuid":"4709b8e0-2fa4-401c-b761-e0f8adec5c0c","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:21:44.808Z","request_id":"req_011Cgj99dpibvpSxE9UeANtF","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01FbaePisf48TpkzdCA85C2L":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211947__x8ab6bc/work/.research/my-3dge/engine/app/view.ts"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FbaePisf48TpkzdCA85C2L","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t/**\n2\t * @file The view of a run (PLAN.md §6.4's `view.update`, §8.3, WP 2.7): what a running scene looks like, built\n3\t * without a GPU, so a page draws it and `createHeadless({ view: true })` dumps it in Node. `createRunView` makes the\n4\t * stage of the scene (engine/gfx/stage.ts: lights, the level's meshes, actors as puppets, a stand-in per other placed\n5\t * entity) and its camera (engine/gfx/cameras: a camera code, `cam=iso` by default), and keeps both in step with the\n6\t * run: `stepped()` after every sim step reads where the entities are, `frame({ alpha, dt, aspect })` puts every\n7\t * puppet and stand-in `alpha` of the way between its last two steps and moves the camera by a rendered frame, then\n8\t * draws the crowd bodies as that camera sees them (engine/gfx/stageCrowd.ts: its level of detail and culling; after\n9\t * steps with no frame, `dump` draws them first), then moves the stage's effects on by the frame (engine/gfx/stageFx.ts:\n10\t * the world's new events burst, its bolts, telegraphs and trails drawn, unless the view setting `gfx.effects` is off;\n11\t * the page shakes its camera by them while it draws), returning what to draw (`{ scene, camera, alpha }`,\n12\t * engine/gfx/renderer.ts's `FrameView`). A frame that finds `gfx.effects` switched since the last read reads the\n13\t * entities again first, so a flying bolt is the effects' or its stand-in from that frame, with or without a step.\n14\t *\n15\t * The camera is a rig (engine/gfx/cameras/rig.ts: a code's camera, blends, the view effects, the settings `cam.*`) that\n16\t * follows the player (WP 3.10): the first player actor's feet as the frame draws them, else the level's middle; so does\n17\t * the stage's sky (engine/gfx/stageSky.ts, flickering at the frames' time, WP 7.8), and the level entry's looks (its\n18\t * swaps, rooms' floors and recipes: `levelLooks`) reach the stage. The rig also gets the sim's read-only `QueryView` in\n19\t * a physics scene (the follow cameras keep out of the walls and the doors standing shut), the player's eye (the shooter model's height, else his\n20\t * head socket) and what he does each step (`cameraPlayer`); first person draws his arms by their own lens and hides his\n21\t * body, its shadow kept (engine/gfx/viewmodel/, WP 13.12; `cameraInfo().culled`, `.arms`); hard landings shake the\n22\t * screen. Following a player, the cutaways run (the stage's `frame`); `aim(rule, devices)` is his aim from the camera\n23\t * drawn last (WP 13.9, engine/input/aim.ts: the centre's ray through the sim's queries, his body skipped, or the\n24\t * pointer's onto his floor), which the page's input records. `restarted()` after the run starts again (a new seed, a\n25\t * replay) or its world changes between steps (a restore, a dev action) reads the entities afresh: the stand-ins and\n26\t * bolts snap to them, so no dump, shot or frame shows the places they had before. The effects forget what ran only for\n27\t * a new world, read from its first event; the same world keeps its trace read, so no event plays twice.\n28\t *\n29\t * The level comes from the scene's `level` id (engine/world/level/level.ts), registered before the view starts\n30\t * (`APP_NO_LEVEL`), the terrain from its `terrain` id (WP 10.5), the site from its `site` id (WP 13.15). Cameras are\n31\t * view state: switching one (`setCamera(code)`, `__engine.camera.set`; `{ blend: true }` blends it in), moving it on\n32\t * headless (`advance`) or at a replay's step drawing no frame (`carry`) never reaches the sim. Invariants: presentation\n33\t * only: it reads the run, never writes it (its `QueryView` has no way in); one stage per view, a camera per projection.\n34\t *\n35\t * @example\n36\t * // const view = createRunView({ run: () => session, registry, materials: createMaterialLibrary() });\n37\t * // view.stepped(); // after each sim step; then gfx.frame(view.frame({ alpha, dt, aspect }))\n38\t * // view.setCamera('cam=topdown').describe; // what the camera now shows, in words\n39\t * @see engine/app/view.test.ts\n40\t */\n41\timport { codeError, defineCodes, type Log } from '../core/log';\n42\timport type { Registry } from '../core/registry';\n43\timport type { BoostedOrthographicCamera, BoostedPerspectiveCamera } from '../gfx/cameras/boost';\n44\timport { cameraPlayer, type CameraPlayer } from '../gfx/cameras/effects';\n45\timport { createCameraPair, type AnyCamera } from '../gfx/cameras/place';\n46\timport type { CameraInput, CameraPose, Vec3 } from '../gfx/cameras/pose';\n47\timport { createCameraRig, rigOptions } from '../gfx/cameras/rig';\n48\timport type { MaterialLibrary } from '../gfx/materials/library';\n49\timport type { FrameView } from '../gfx/renderer';\n50\timport { aimPoint, type AimDevices, type AimRule } from '../input/aim';\n51\timport { dumpScene, type DumpOptions } from '../gfx/sceneDump';\n52\timport { levelLooks } from '../gfx/level/runs';\n53\timport { createStage, type Stage } from '../gfx/stage';\n54\timport type { FirstPersonParts } from '../gfx/viewmodel/body';\n55\timport { armsLens } from '../gfx/viewmodel/lens';\n56\timport { queryViewOf, type QueryView } from '../sim/queryView';\n57\timport { shutDoors } from '../sim/doors';\n58\timport { daytimeOf } from '../sim/lights';\n59\timport { CHEST } from '../sim/weapons';\n60\timport type { Session } from '../sim/session';\n61\timport type { EntityData } from '../sim/state';\n62\timport { getLevel } from '../world/level/level';\n63\timport { getSite } from '../world/site';\n64\timport { getTerrain } from '../world/terrain';\n65\t\n66\t/** The codes this module raises, with their fixes. */\n67\texport const VIEW_CODES = defineCodes('app', {\n68\t  APP_NO_LEVEL: {\n69\t    template: 'the scene {scene} loads the level {level}, which is not registered, so its view cannot be built',\n70\t    fix: \"register the level's text before the view starts: in a page, import text from './levels/<name>.txt?raw' and call defineLevel('{level}', { text, file }); in Node, read the file and do the same\",\n71\t  },\n72\t  APP_NO_VIEW: {\n73\t    template: '{member} needs the scene drawn as a view, and this engine has none',\n74\t    fix: 'start it with createHeadless({ scene, view: true }) in Node; a page always has one',\n75\t  },\n76\t});\n77\t\n78\t/** The camera code a view starts with when none is given. */\n79\texport const DEFAULT_CAMERA = 'cam=iso';\n80\t\n81\t/** The aspect a view frames for when nothing draws it (headless): 16:9, the e2e viewport's. */\n82\texport const HEADLESS_ASPECT = 16 / 9;\n83\t\n84\t/** A frame `advance` moves the camera on by, real seconds: a 60 Hz page's. */\n85\texport const ADVANCE_FRAME = 1 / 60;\n86\t\n87\t/** What `camera.get()` and `camera.set(code)` return: the camera as a code, in words, and its pose. */\n88\texport interface CameraInfo {\n89\t  code: string;\n90\t  describe: string;\n91\t  type: string;\n92\t  /** The heading it looks along, rad: the intents' `cam`. */\n93\t  yaw: number;\n94\t  pose: CameraPose;\n95\t  /** First person: the player's joints whose body parts it hides from itself, and the ones his arms show. */\n96\t  culled?: string[];\n97\t  arms?: string[];\n98\t}\n99\t\n100\t/** What a view is made from. */\n101\texport interface RunViewOptions {\n102\t  /** The run it shows: the live session, read again after every restart. */\n103\t  run: () => Session;\n104\t  /** Where the scene's level and the component kinds are declared. */\n105\t  registry: Registry;\n106\t  /** The page's material library. */\n107\t  materials: MaterialLibrary;\n108\t  /** The camera code to start with (`DEFAULT_CAMERA`). Throws `GFX_BAD_CAMERA_CODE` or `GFX_UNKNOWN_CAMERA`. */\n109\t  cam?: string;\n110\t  log?: Log;\n111\t}\n112\t\n113\t/** One rendered frame's view inputs: the clock's alpha, real seconds since the last frame, the picture's aspect. */\n114\texport interface ViewFrame {\n115\t  alpha: number;\n116\t  dt: number;\n117\t  aspect: number;\n118\t  /** What the devices give the camera this frame (mouse look, wheel). */\n119\t  input?: CameraInput;\n120\t}\n121\t\n122\t/** The view of a run (see the file comment). */\n123\texport interface RunView {\n124\t  readonly stage: Stage;\n125\t  /** The camera's state (what codes and the devices change). */\n126\t  readonly camera: AnyCamera;\n127\t  /** Both three.js cameras, perspective then orthographic: what a warm-up compiles for. */\n128\t  readonly cameras: readonly [BoostedPerspectiveCamera, BoostedOrthographicCamera];\n129\t  /** The three.js camera the last frame placed. */\n130\t  readonly drawn: BoostedPerspectiveCamera | BoostedOrthographicCamera;\n131\t  /** Reads where the entities are after a sim step. */\n132\t  stepped(): void;\n133\t  /** The run started again, or its world changed between steps: forget the old places and snap to the new ones. */\n134\t  restarted(): void;\n135\t  /**\n136\t   * Moves the camera by one rendered frame and the stand-ins to `alpha`; returns what to draw. The stage's sky follows,\n137\t   * lit by the hour of the scene's clock (engine/sim/lights.ts) and lighting the props' lamps that are on (WP 13.23).\n138\t   */\n139\t  frame(frame: ViewFrame): FrameView;\n140\t  /** The camera now. */\n141\t  cameraInfo(): CameraInfo;\n142\t  /**\n143\t   * The point `rule` aims at from the camera drawn last (see the file comment), without the burst's climb, which the\n144\t   * sim adds to his shots (the rig's `aimPose`, WP 13.20); undefined without a player.\n145\t   */\n146\t  aim(rule: AimRule, devices?: AimDevices): Vec3 | undefined;\n147\t  /** Switches to the camera `code` names, from the current one (blending with `blend`); returns it. Throws for a bad code. */\n148\t  setCamera(code: string, options?: { blend?: boolean }): CameraInfo;\n149\t  /** Moves the camera on by `frames` frames of `ADVANCE_FRAME`, drawing nothing, as a page's frames move it; returns it. */\n150\t  advance(frames: number): CameraInfo;\n151\t  /** Moves the camera on by one frame of `ADVANCE_FRAME`, as `advance(1)`, leaving the crowd to the next frame or dump. */\n152\t  carry(): void;\n153\t  /** The stage as text (engine/gfx/sceneDump.ts). */\n154\t  dump(options?: DumpOptions): string;\n155\t  /** The sim's read-only queries, or undefined without physics: what the agent eye casts through (WP 12.3). */\n156\t  queries(): QueryView | undefined;\n157\t  /** Frees the stage. */\n158\t  dispose(): void;\n159\t}\n160\t\n161\t/** The entities that a stage can place, each once, in id order. */\n162\tfunction placed(session: Session, kinds: readonly string[]): EntityData[] {\n163\t  const byId = new Map<number, EntityData>();\n164\t  for (const kind of kinds) for (const entity of session.world.query(kind)) byId.set(entity.id, entity);\n165\t  return [...byId.values()].sort((a, b) => a.id - b.id);\n166\t}\n167\t\n168\t/** Builds the view of a run (see the file comment). */\n169\texport function createRunView(options: RunViewOptions): RunView {\n170\t  const { registry } = options;\n171\t  const scene = options.run().scene;\n172\t  const known = (id: string) => registry.kinds().includes('level') && registry.has('level', id);\n173\t  if (scene.level !== undefined && !known(scene.level)) {\n174\t    throw codeError('APP_NO_LEVEL', { scene: scene.id, level: scene.level });\n175\t  }\n176\t  const level = scene.level === undefined ? null : getLevel(scene.level, registry);\n177\t  const looks = scene.level === undefined ? {} : levelLooks(registry, scene.level);\n178\t  const terrain = scene.terrain === undefined ? null : getTerrain(scene.terrain, registry);\n179\t  const site = scene.site === undefined ? null : getSite(scene.site, registry);\n180\t  const fxRng = (...keys: readonly (string | number)[]) => options.run().world.fxRng(...keys);\n181\t  const stage = createStage({ level, terrain, site, materials: options.materials, registry, log: options.log, fxRng, ...looks }); // prettier-ignore\n182\t  /**\n183\t   * Turns the effects on or off by the view setting `gfx.effects` (a registry without it: on), before they read;\n184\t   * returns whether that changed them.\n185\t   */\n186\t  const syncEffects = (): boolean => {\n187\t    const run = options.run();\n188\t    const declared = registry.kinds().includes('setting') && registry.has('setting', 'gfx.effects');\n189\t    const enabled = !declared || run.settings.get<boolean>('gfx.effects') !== false;\n190\t    const changed = stage.fx.effects.enabled !== enabled;\n191\t    stage.fx.effects.enabled = enabled;\n192\t    return changed;\n193\t  };\n194\t  /** Reads the entities afresh from the run's last step: every stand-in, puppet and bolt snaps to it. */\n195\t  const reread = () => {\n196\t    const run = options.run();\n197\t    stage.capture([]);\n198\t    stage.capture(placed(run, stage.kinds), run.world.dt, queries());\n199\t  };\n200\t  /** The world whose trace the effects read: only a new one is read from its first event. */\n201\t  let fxWorld: object | null = null;\n202\t  const pair = createCameraPair();\n203\t  const rig = createCameraRig(options.cam ?? DEFAULT_CAMERA);\n204\t  let drawn: BoostedPerspectiveCamera | BoostedOrthographicCamera = pair.perspective;\n205\t  let aspect = HEADLESS_ASPECT;\n206\t  let parts: FirstPersonParts = { hidden: [], arms: [] };\n207\t  let alpha = 1;\n208\t  let crowdStale = false;\n209\t  /** Seconds of frames drawn: the lights' flicker clock (presentation only). */\n210\t  let time = 0;\n211\t  /** Poses and draws the crowd bodies as the camera now placed sees them. */\n212\t  const drawCrowd = () => {\n213\t    stage.crowd.draw(alpha, drawn);\n214\t    crowdStale = false;\n215\t  };\n216\t  const views = new WeakMap<object, QueryView>();\n217\t  /** The sim's read-only queries, for the follow cameras' walls and the puppets' ground; none without physics. */\n218\t  const queries = (): QueryView | undefined => {\n219\t    const run = options.run();\n220\t    if (!run.scene.physics) return undefined;\n221\t    const world = run.world;\n222\t    if (!views.has(world)) views.set(world, queryViewOf(world));\n223\t    return views.get(world);\n224\t  };\n225\t  /** What the player did last step, for the rig (`cameraPlayer`); null without one. */\n226\t  let doing: CameraPlayer | null = null;\n227\t  /** The player's body, which his aim's ray skips; -1 without one. */\n228\t  let body = -1;\n229\t  /** The doors standing shut after the last step, which stop the follow cameras as walls do (engine/sim/doors.ts). */\n230\t  let shut: readonly number[] = [];\n231\t  /** Reads the player after a step (`fresh`: after a restart, so nothing he did before counts as a landing), and the\n232\t   * looks of the other actors' AIs (their heads along them). */\n233\t  const readPlayer = (fresh = false) => {\n234\t    const run = options.run();\n235\t    if (fresh) rig.step(null);\n236\t    const entity = run.world.query('actor').find((e) => (e.actor as { player?: boolean }).player === true);\n237\t    const aiming = (run.intents.b ?? []).includes('aim');\n238\t    doing = entity ? cameraPlayer(entity, aiming) : null;\n239\t    body = entity ? Number((entity.actor as { body?: number }).body ?? -1) : -1;\n240\t    shut = run.scene.physics ? shutDoors(run.world, registry) : [];\n241\t    const look = run.intents.look; // his head, and his gun, along it (WP 13.11); the sights only with one out (WP 13.20)\n242\t    if (entity) stage.actors.look(entity.id, look ? { yaw: look[0], pitch: look[1], aiming: doing?.aiming ?? aiming } : null); // prettier-ignore\n243\t    for (const other of run.world.query('actor')) {\n244\t      const actor = other.actor as { player?: boolean; intents?: { look?: readonly [number, number] } };\n245\t      if (actor.player === true) continue;\n246\t      const along = actor.intents?.look; // an AI's head along the look it gives its actor (WP 13.21: the neighbours)\n247\t      stage.actors.look(other.id, along ? { yaw: along[0], pitch: along[1], aiming: false } : null);\n248\t    }\n249\t    rig.step(doing);\n250\t  };\n251\t  /** Whether the run's registry declares the view setting `path`. */\n252\t  const declared = (path: string) => registry.kinds().includes('setting') && registry.has('setting', path);\n253\t  /** What the camera takes from the run this frame: whom it follows, his eye and what he does, the walls. */\n254\t  const follow = (): {\n255\t    follow: Vec3;\n256\t    eye?: Vec3;\n257\t    queries?: QueryView;\n258\t    also: readonly number[];\n259\t    player: CameraPlayer | null;\n260\t  } => {\n261\t    // prettier-ignore\n262\t    const player = stage.actors.player();\n263\t    const feet = player?.feet ?? stage.centre;\n264\t    const eye: Vec3 | undefined = doing?.eye !== undefined ? [feet[0], feet[1] + doing.eye, feet[2]] : player?.posed?.eye; // prettier-ignore\n265\t    return { follow: feet, eye, queries: queries(), also: shut, player: doing };\n266\t  };\n267\t  /** Steps the camera by `dt` with `input`, then draws the player for a first-person camera: his arms, his body hidden. */\n268\t  const move = (input: CameraInput | undefined, dt: number): CameraPose => {\n269\t    const run = options.run();\n270\t    const setting = (path: string) => (declared(path) ? run.settings.get(path) : undefined);\n271\t    rig.configure(rigOptions(setting));\n272\t    const pose = rig.update({ ...follow(), ...input }, dt);\n273\t    stage.fx.effects.shake.add(rig.shake());\n274\t    const lens = { fov: armsLens(setting('cam.armsFov')), fullBody: setting('cam.fullBody') === true };\n275\t    const first = rig.firstShare() > 0.5 ? { pose, dt, aspect, player: doing, effects: rig.effects(), ...lens } : null;\n276\t    parts = stage.actors.firstPerson(first);\n277\t    const player = stage.actors.player();\n278\t    const fade = (rig.camera as { fade?: boolean }).fade === true; // a camera that may stand behind a wall\n279\t    if (player) stage.frame(pose, player.feet, { fade, view: rig.camera.type === 'view' });\n280\t    return pose;\n281\t  };\n282\t  const info = (): CameraInfo => ({\n283\t    code: rig.camera.code(),\n284\t    describe: rig.camera.describe(),\n285\t    type: rig.camera.type,\n286\t    yaw: rig.camera.yaw(),\n287\t    pose: rig.pose(),\n288\t    ...(rig.camera.type === 'first' ? { culled: [...parts.hidden], arms: [...parts.arms] } : {}),\n289\t  });\n290\t  const view: RunView = {\n291\t    stage,\n292\t    get camera() {\n293\t      return rig.camera;\n294\t    },\n295\t    cameras: [pair.perspective, pair.orthographic],\n296\t    get drawn() {\n297\t      return drawn;\n298\t    },\n299\t    stepped() {\n300\t      const run = options.run();\n301\t      syncEffects(); // off, the bolts this step reads draw as stand-ins at once\n302\t      stage.capture(placed(run, stage.kinds), run.world.dt, queries());\n303\t      stage.draw((alpha = 1)); // the latest state until a frame interpolates: what a headless dump shows\n304\t      crowdStale = true; // posed by the next frame or dump, not every step\n305\t      readPlayer();\n306\t    },\n307\t    restarted() {\n308\t      const run = options.run();\n309\t      // A new world is read from its first event. The same one (a restore, a dev action) keeps its trace read: the\n310\t      // trace is history, never restored, so reading it again would play its events twice. Bolts snap either way.\n311\t      if (run.world !== fxWorld) {\n312\t        stage.fx.reset();\n313\t        fxWorld = run.world;\n314\t      }\n315\t      syncEffects();\n316\t      reread();\n317\t      stage.draw((alpha = 1));\n318\t      crowdStale = true;\n319\t      readPlayer(true);\n320\t    },\n321\t    frame(frame) {\n322\t      aspect = frame.aspect;\n323\t      // Turned on or off since the last read (a paused page, a hit-stop, a shot): read the world again first, so a\n324\t      // flying bolt changes hands at once between the effects and its stand-in, and no frame draws it by neither.\n325\t      if (syncEffects()) reread();\n326\t      stage.draw((alpha = frame.alpha));\n327\t      drawn = pair.place(move(frame.input, frame.dt), aspect);\n328\t      time += frame.dt;\n329\t      const [hour, lamps] = [daytimeOf(options.run().world), stage.props.lights()]; // WP 13.23\n330\t      stage.sky.update({ camera: drawn, focus: stage.actors.player()?.feet ?? stage.centre, time, hour, lamps });\n331\t      drawCrowd();\n332\t      stage.fx.frame(frame.dt, drawn, options.run().world.events.trace());\n333\t      return { scene: stage.scene, camera: drawn, alpha: frame.alpha, ...(stage.fx.gpuParticles ? { particles: stage.fx.gpuParticles } : {}) }; // prettier-ignore\n334\t    },\n335\t    cameraInfo: info,\n336\t    queries,\n337\t    aim(rule, devices = {}) {\n338\t      if (!stage.actors.player()) return undefined;\n339\t      const { follow: feet, eye, queries: walls } = follow();\n340\t      const lens = 'isPerspectiveCamera' in drawn && drawn.isPerspectiveCamera ? { fov: drawn.fov } : {}; // as the page widened it\n341\t      const skip = body >= 0 ? { exclude: body } : {};\n342\t      const cast = (origin: Vec3, direction: Vec3, max: number) =>\n343\t        walls?.raycast(origin, direction, { maxDistance: max, ...skip })?.distance ?? null;\n344\t      const motion = (options.run().world.get(stage.actors.player()!.id) as { motion?: { stance?: string } } | undefined)?.motion; // prettier-ignore\n345\t      const height = motion?.stance === 'crouch' ? CHEST.crouch : CHEST.stand; // where a level shot leaves\n346\t      return aimPoint(rule, { pose: { ...rig.aimPose(), ...lens }, aspect, feet, eye, height, ...devices, cast }); // the climb aside: the sim adds it\n347\t    },\n348\t    setCamera(code, setOptions = {}) {\n349\t      rig.set(code, { blend: setOptions.blend === true });\n350\t      drawn = pair.place(move(undefined, 0), aspect);\n351\t      drawCrowd();\n352\t      return info();\n353\t    },\n354\t    advance(frames) {\n355\t      for (let i = 0; i < frames; i++) drawn = pair.place(move(undefined, ADVANCE_FRAME), aspect);\n356\t      drawCrowd();\n357\t      return info();\n358\t    },\n359\t    carry() {\n360\t      drawn = pair.place(move(undefined, ADVANCE_FRAME), aspect);\n361\t      crowdStale = true; // posed by the next frame or dump, as after a step\n362\t    },\n363\t    dump: (dumpOptions) => {\n364\t      if (crowdStale) drawCrowd();\n365\t      return dumpScene(stage.scene, dumpOptions);\n366\t    },\n367\t    dispose: () => stage.dispose(),\n368\t  };\n369\t  view.restarted();\n370\t  view.frame({ alpha: 1, dt: 0, aspect });\n371\t  return view;\n372\t}\n373\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b0d0401-1a79-4c2f-8a33-ba9239fdbfed","uuid":"a50a8826-2a08-4e64-993b-fc048155b7b9","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:21:44.823Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211947__x8ab6bc/work/.research/my-3dge/engine/app/view.ts","content":"/**\n * @file The view of a run (PLAN.md §6.4's `view.update`, §8.3, WP 2.7): what a running scene looks like, built\n * without a GPU, so a page draws it and `createHeadless({ view: true })` dumps it in Node. `createRunView` makes the\n * stage of the scene (engine/gfx/stage.ts: lights, the level's meshes, actors as puppets, a stand-in per other placed\n * entity) and its camera (engine/gfx/cameras: a camera code, `cam=iso` by default), and keeps both in step with the\n * run: `stepped()` after every sim step reads where the entities are, `frame({ alpha, dt, aspect })` puts every\n * puppet and stand-in `alpha` of the way between its last two steps and moves the camera by a rendered frame, then\n * draws the crowd bodies as that camera sees them (engine/gfx/stageCrowd.ts: its level of detail and culling; after\n * steps with no frame, `dump` draws them first), then moves the stage's effects on by the frame (engine/gfx/stageFx.ts:\n * the world's new events burst, its bolts, telegraphs and trails drawn, unless the view setting `gfx.effects` is off;\n * the page shakes its camera by them while it draws), returning what to draw (`{ scene, camera, alpha }`,\n * engine/gfx/renderer.ts's `FrameView`). A frame that finds `gfx.effects` switched since the last read reads the\n * entities again first, so a flying bolt is the effects' or its stand-in from that frame, with or without a step.\n *\n * The camera is a rig (engine/gfx/cameras/rig.ts: a code's camera, blends, the view effects, the settings `cam.*`) that\n * follows the player (WP 3.10): the first player actor's feet as the frame draws them, else the level's middle; so does\n * the stage's sky (engine/gfx/stageSky.ts, flickering at the frames' time, WP 7.8), and the level entry's looks (its\n * swaps, rooms' floors and recipes: `levelLooks`) reach the stage. The rig also gets the sim's read-only `QueryView` in\n * a physics scene (the follow cameras keep out of the walls and the doors standing shut), the player's eye (the shooter model's height, else his\n * head socket) and what he does each step (`cameraPlayer`); first person draws his arms by their own lens and hides his\n * body, its shadow kept (engine/gfx/viewmodel/, WP 13.12; `cameraInfo().culled`, `.arms`); hard landings shake the\n * screen. Following a player, the cutaways run (the stage's `frame`); `aim(rule, devices)` is his aim from the camera\n * drawn last (WP 13.9, engine/input/aim.ts: the centre's ray through the sim's queries, his body skipped, or the\n * pointer's onto his floor), which the page's input records. `restarted()` after the run starts again (a new seed, a\n * replay) or its world changes between steps (a restore, a dev action) reads the entities afresh: the stand-ins and\n * bolts snap to them, so no dump, shot or frame shows the places they had before. The effects forget what ran only for\n * a new world, read from its first event; the same world keeps its trace read, so no event plays twice.\n *\n * The level comes from the scene's `level` id (engine/world/level/level.ts), registered before the view starts\n * (`APP_NO_LEVEL`), the terrain from its `terrain` id (WP 10.5), the site from its `site` id (WP 13.15). Cameras are\n * view state: switching one (`setCamera(code)`, `__engine.camera.set`; `{ blend: true }` blends it in), moving it on\n * headless (`advance`) or at a replay's step drawing no frame (`carry`) never reaches the sim. Invariants: presentation\n * only: it reads the run, never writes it (its `QueryView` has no way in); one stage per view, a camera per projection.\n *\n * @example\n * // const view = createRunView({ run: () => session, registry, materials: createMaterialLibrary() });\n * // view.stepped(); // after each sim step; then gfx.frame(view.frame({ alpha, dt, aspect }))\n * // view.setCamera('cam=topdown').describe; // what the camera now shows, in words\n * @see engine/app/view.test.ts\n */\nimport { codeError, defineCodes, type Log } from '../core/log';\nimport type { Registry } from '../core/registry';\nimport type { BoostedOrthographicCamera, BoostedPerspectiveCamera } from '../gfx/cameras/boost';\nimport { cameraPlayer, type CameraPlayer } from '../gfx/cameras/effects';\nimport { createCameraPair, type AnyCamera } from '../gfx/cameras/place';\nimport type { CameraInput, CameraPose, Vec3 } from '../gfx/cameras/pose';\nimport { createCameraRig, rigOptions } from '../gfx/cameras/rig';\nimport type { MaterialLibrary } from '../gfx/materials/library';\nimport type { FrameView } from '../gfx/renderer';\nimport { aimPoint, type AimDevices, type AimRule } from '../input/aim';\nimport { dumpScene, type DumpOptions } from '../gfx/sceneDump';\nimport { levelLooks } from '../gfx/level/runs';\nimport { createStage, type Stage } from '../gfx/stage';\nimport type { FirstPersonParts } from '../gfx/viewmodel/body';\nimport { armsLens } from '../gfx/viewmodel/lens';\nimport { queryViewOf, type QueryView } from '../sim/queryView';\nimport { shutDoors } from '../sim/doors';\nimport { daytimeOf } from '../sim/lights';\nimport { CHEST } from '../sim/weapons';\nimport type { Session } from '../sim/session';\nimport type { EntityData } from '../sim/state';\nimport { getLevel } from '../world/level/level';\nimport { getSite } from '../world/site';\nimport { getTerrain } from '../world/terrain';\n\n/** The codes this module raises, with their fixes. */\nexport const VIEW_CODES = defineCodes('app', {\n  APP_NO_LEVEL: {\n    template: 'the scene {scene} loads the level {level}, which is not registered, so its view cannot be built',\n    fix: \"register the level's text before the view starts: in a page, import text from './levels/<name>.txt?raw' and call defineLevel('{level}', { text, file }); in Node, read the file and do the same\",\n  },\n  APP_NO_VIEW: {\n    template: '{member} needs the scene drawn as a view, and this engine has none',\n    fix: 'start it with createHeadless({ scene, view: true }) in Node; a page always has one',\n  },\n});\n\n/** The camera code a view starts with when none is given. */\nexport const DEFAULT_CAMERA = 'cam=iso';\n\n/** The aspect a view frames for when nothing draws it (headless): 16:9, the e2e viewport's. */\nexport const HEADLESS_ASPECT = 16 / 9;\n\n/** A frame `advance` moves the camera on by, real seconds: a 60 Hz page's. */\nexport const ADVANCE_FRAME = 1 / 60;\n\n/** What `camera.get()` and `camera.set(code)` return: the camera as a code, in words, and its pose. */\nexport interface CameraInfo {\n  code: string;\n  describe: string;\n  type: string;\n  /** The heading it looks along, rad: the intents' `cam`. */\n  yaw: number;\n  pose: CameraPose;\n  /** First person: the player's joints whose body parts it hides from itself, and the ones his arms show. */\n  culled?: string[];\n  arms?: string[];\n}\n\n/** What a view is made from. */\nexport interface RunViewOptions {\n  /** The run it shows: the live session, read again after every restart. */\n  run: () => Session;\n  /** Where the scene's level and the component kinds are declared. */\n  registry: Registry;\n  /** The page's material library. */\n  materials: MaterialLibrary;\n  /** The camera code to start with (`DEFAULT_CAMERA`). Throws `GFX_BAD_CAMERA_CODE` or `GFX_UNKNOWN_CAMERA`. */\n  cam?: string;\n  log?: Log;\n}\n\n/** One rendered frame's view inputs: the clock's alpha, real seconds since the last frame, the picture's aspect. */\nexport interface ViewFrame {\n  alpha: number;\n  dt: number;\n  aspect: number;\n  /** What the devices give the camera this frame (mouse look, wheel). */\n  input?: CameraInput;\n}\n\n/** The view of a run (see the file comment). */\nexport interface RunView {\n  readonly stage: Stage;\n  /** The camera's state (what codes and the devices change). */\n  readonly camera: AnyCamera;\n  /** Both three.js cameras, perspective then orthographic: what a warm-up compiles for. */\n  readonly cameras: readonly [BoostedPerspectiveCamera, BoostedOrthographicCamera];\n  /** The three.js camera the last frame placed. */\n  readonly drawn: BoostedPerspectiveCamera | BoostedOrthographicCamera;\n  /** Reads where the entities are after a sim step. */\n  stepped(): void;\n  /** The run started again, or its world changed between steps: forget the old places and snap to the new ones. */\n  restarted(): void;\n  /**\n   * Moves the camera by one rendered frame and the stand-ins to `alpha`; returns what to draw. The stage's sky follows,\n   * lit by the hour of the scene's clock (engine/sim/lights.ts) and lighting the props' lamps that are on (WP 13.23).\n   */\n  frame(frame: ViewFrame): FrameView;\n  /** The camera now. */\n  cameraInfo(): CameraInfo;\n  /**\n   * The point `rule` aims at from the camera drawn last (see the file comment), without the burst's climb, which the\n   * sim adds to his shots (the rig's `aimPose`, WP 13.20); undefined without a player.\n   */\n  aim(rule: AimRule, devices?: AimDevices): Vec3 | undefined;\n  /** Switches to the camera `code` names, from the current one (blending with `blend`); returns it. Throws for a bad code. */\n  setCamera(code: string, options?: { blend?: boolean }): CameraInfo;\n  /** Moves the camera on by `frames` frames of `ADVANCE_FRAME`, drawing nothing, as a page's frames move it; returns it. */\n  advance(frames: number): CameraInfo;\n  /** Moves the camera on by one frame of `ADVANCE_FRAME`, as `advance(1)`, leaving the crowd to the next frame or dump. */\n  carry(): void;\n  /** The stage as text (engine/gfx/sceneDump.ts). */\n  dump(options?: DumpOptions): string;\n  /** The sim's read-only queries, or undefined without physics: what the agent eye casts through (WP 12.3). */\n  queries(): QueryView | undefined;\n  /** Frees the stage. */\n  dispose(): void;\n}\n\n/** The entities that a stage can place, each once, in id order. */\nfunction placed(session: Session, kinds: readonly string[]): EntityData[] {\n  const byId = new Map<number, EntityData>();\n  for (const kind of kinds) for (const entity of session.world.query(kind)) byId.set(entity.id, entity);\n  return [...byId.values()].sort((a, b) => a.id - b.id);\n}\n\n/** Builds the view of a run (see the file comment). */\nexport function createRunView(options: RunViewOptions): RunView {\n  const { registry } = options;\n  const scene = options.run().scene;\n  const known = (id: string) => registry.kinds().includes('level') && registry.has('level', id);\n  if (scene.level !== undefined && !known(scene.level)) {\n    throw codeError('APP_NO_LEVEL', { scene: scene.id, level: scene.level });\n  }\n  const level = scene.level === undefined ? null : getLevel(scene.level, registry);\n  const looks = scene.level === undefined ? {} : levelLooks(registry, scene.level);\n  const terrain = scene.terrain === undefined ? null : getTerrain(scene.terrain, registry);\n  const site = scene.site === undefined ? null : getSite(scene.site, registry);\n  const fxRng = (...keys: readonly (string | number)[]) => options.run().world.fxRng(...keys);\n  const stage = createStage({ level, terrain, site, materials: options.materials, registry, log: options.log, fxRng, ...looks }); // prettier-ignore\n  /**\n   * Turns the effects on or off by the view setting `gfx.effects` (a registry without it: on), before they read;\n   * returns whether that changed them.\n   */\n  const syncEffects = (): boolean => {\n    const run = options.run();\n    const declared = registry.kinds().includes('setting') && registry.has('setting', 'gfx.effects');\n    const enabled = !declared || run.settings.get<boolean>('gfx.effects') !== false;\n    const changed = stage.fx.effects.enabled !== enabled;\n    stage.fx.effects.enabled = enabled;\n    return changed;\n  };\n  /** Reads the entities afresh from the run's last step: every stand-in, puppet and bolt snaps to it. */\n  const reread = () => {\n    const run = options.run();\n    stage.capture([]);\n    stage.capture(placed(run, stage.kinds), run.world.dt, queries());\n  };\n  /** The world whose trace the effects read: only a new one is read from its first event. */\n  let fxWorld: object | null = null;\n  const pair = createCameraPair();\n  const rig = createCameraRig(options.cam ?? DEFAULT_CAMERA);\n  let drawn: BoostedPerspectiveCamera | BoostedOrthographicCamera = pair.perspective;\n  let aspect = HEADLESS_ASPECT;\n  let parts: FirstPersonParts = { hidden: [], arms: [] };\n  let alpha = 1;\n  let crowdStale = false;\n  /** Seconds of frames drawn: the lights' flicker clock (presentation only). */\n  let time = 0;\n  /** Poses and draws the crowd bodies as the camera now placed sees them. */\n  const drawCrowd = () => {\n    stage.crowd.draw(alpha, drawn);\n    crowdStale = false;\n  };\n  const views = new WeakMap<object, QueryView>();\n  /** The sim's read-only queries, for the follow cameras' walls and the puppets' ground; none without physics. */\n  const queries = (): QueryView | undefined => {\n    const run = options.run();\n    if (!run.scene.physics) return undefined;\n    const world = run.world;\n    if (!views.has(world)) views.set(world, queryViewOf(world));\n    return views.get(world);\n  };\n  /** What the player did last step, for the rig (`cameraPlayer`); null without one. */\n  let doing: CameraPlayer | null = null;\n  /** The player's body, which his aim's ray skips; -1 without one. */\n  let body = -1;\n  /** The doors standing shut after the last step, which stop the follow cameras as walls do (engine/sim/doors.ts). */\n  let shut: readonly number[] = [];\n  /** Reads the player after a step (`fresh`: after a restart, so nothing he did before counts as a landing), and the\n   * looks of the other actors' AIs (their heads along them). */\n  const readPlayer = (fresh = false) => {\n    const run = options.run();\n    if (fresh) rig.step(null);\n    const entity = run.world.query('actor').find((e) => (e.actor as { player?: boolean }).player === true);\n    const aiming = (run.intents.b ?? []).includes('aim');\n    doing = entity ? cameraPlayer(entity, aiming) : null;\n    body = entity ? Number((entity.actor as { body?: number }).body ?? -1) : -1;\n    shut = run.scene.physics ? shutDoors(run.world, registry) : [];\n    const look = run.intents.look; // his head, and his gun, along it (WP 13.11); the sights only with one out (WP 13.20)\n    if (entity) stage.actors.look(entity.id, look ? { yaw: look[0], pitch: look[1], aiming: doing?.aiming ?? aiming } : null); // prettier-ignore\n    for (const other of run.world.query('actor')) {\n      const actor = other.actor as { player?: boolean; intents?: { look?: readonly [number, number] } };\n      if (actor.player === true) continue;\n      const along = actor.intents?.look; // an AI's head along the look it gives its actor (WP 13.21: the neighbours)\n      stage.actors.look(other.id, along ? { yaw: along[0], pitch: along[1], aiming: false } : null);\n    }\n    rig.step(doing);\n  };\n  /** Whether the run's registry declares the view setting `path`. */\n  const declared = (path: string) => registry.kinds().includes('setting') && registry.has('setting', path);\n  /** What the camera takes from the run this frame: whom it follows, his eye and what he does, the walls. */\n  const follow = (): {\n    follow: Vec3;\n    eye?: Vec3;\n    queries?: QueryView;\n    also: readonly number[];\n    player: CameraPlayer | null;\n  } => {\n    // prettier-ignore\n    const player = stage.actors.player();\n    const feet = player?.feet ?? stage.centre;\n    const eye: Vec3 | undefined = doing?.eye !== undefined ? [feet[0], feet[1] + doing.eye, feet[2]] : player?.posed?.eye; // prettier-ignore\n    return { follow: feet, eye, queries: queries(), also: shut, player: doing };\n  };\n  /** Steps the camera by `dt` with `input`, then draws the player for a first-person camera: his arms, his body hidden. */\n  const move = (input: CameraInput | undefined, dt: number): CameraPose => {\n    const run = options.run();\n    const setting = (path: string) => (declared(path) ? run.settings.get(path) : undefined);\n    rig.configure(rigOptions(setting));\n    const pose = rig.update({ ...follow(), ...input }, dt);\n    stage.fx.effects.shake.add(rig.shake());\n    const lens = { fov: armsLens(setting('cam.armsFov')), fullBody: setting('cam.fullBody') === true };\n    const first = rig.firstShare() > 0.5 ? { pose, dt, aspect, player: doing, effects: rig.effects(), ...lens } : null;\n    parts = stage.actors.firstPerson(first);\n    const player = stage.actors.player();\n    const fade = (rig.camera as { fade?: boolean }).fade === true; // a camera that may stand behind a wall\n    if (player) stage.frame(pose, player.feet, { fade, view: rig.camera.type === 'view' });\n    return pose;\n  };\n  const info = (): CameraInfo => ({\n    code: rig.camera.code(),\n    describe: rig.camera.describe(),\n    type: rig.camera.type,\n    yaw: rig.camera.yaw(),\n    pose: rig.pose(),\n    ...(rig.camera.type === 'first' ? { culled: [...parts.hidden], arms: [...parts.arms] } : {}),\n  });\n  const view: RunView = {\n    stage,\n    get camera() {\n      return rig.camera;\n    },\n    cameras: [pair.perspective, pair.orthographic],\n    get drawn() {\n      return drawn;\n    },\n    stepped() {\n      const run = options.run();\n      syncEffects(); // off, the bolts this step reads draw as stand-ins at once\n      stage.capture(placed(run, stage.kinds), run.world.dt, queries());\n      stage.draw((alpha = 1)); // the latest state until a frame interpolates: what a headless dump shows\n      crowdStale = true; // posed by the next frame or dump, not every step\n      readPlayer();\n    },\n    restarted() {\n      const run = options.run();\n      // A new world is read from its first event. The same one (a restore, a dev action) keeps its trace read: the\n      // trace is history, never restored, so reading it again would play its events twice. Bolts snap either way.\n      if (run.world !== fxWorld) {\n        stage.fx.reset();\n        fxWorld = run.world;\n      }\n      syncEffects();\n      reread();\n      stage.draw((alpha = 1));\n      crowdStale = true;\n      readPlayer(true);\n    },\n    frame(frame) {\n      aspect = frame.aspect;\n      // Turned on or off since the last read (a paused page, a hit-stop, a shot): read the world again first, so a\n      // flying bolt changes hands at once between the effects and its stand-in, and no frame draws it by neither.\n      if (syncEffects()) reread();\n      stage.draw((alpha = frame.alpha));\n      drawn = pair.place(move(frame.input, frame.dt), aspect);\n      time += frame.dt;\n      const [hour, lamps] = [daytimeOf(options.run().world), stage.props.lights()]; // WP 13.23\n      stage.sky.update({ camera: drawn, focus: stage.actors.player()?.feet ?? stage.centre, time, hour, lamps });\n      drawCrowd();\n      stage.fx.frame(frame.dt, drawn, options.run().world.events.trace());\n      return { scene: stage.scene, camera: drawn, alpha: frame.alpha, ...(stage.fx.gpuParticles ? { particles: stage.fx.gpuParticles } : {}) }; // prettier-ignore\n    },\n    cameraInfo: info,\n    queries,\n    aim(rule, devices = {}) {\n      if (!stage.actors.player()) return undefined;\n      const { follow: feet, eye, queries: walls } = follow();\n      const lens = 'isPerspectiveCamera' in drawn && drawn.isPerspectiveCamera ? { fov: drawn.fov } : {}; // as the page widened it\n      const skip = body >= 0 ? { exclude: body } : {};\n      const cast = (origin: Vec3, direction: Vec3, max: number) =>\n        walls?.raycast(origin, direction, { maxDistance: max, ...skip })?.distance ?? null;\n      const motion = (options.run().world.get(stage.actors.player()!.id) as { motion?: { stance?: string } } | undefined)?.motion; // prettier-ignore\n      const height = motion?.stance === 'crouch' ? CHEST.crouch : CHEST.stand; // where a level shot leaves\n      return aimPoint(rule, { pose: { ...rig.aimPose(), ...lens }, aspect, feet, eye, height, ...devices, cast }); // the climb aside: the sim adds it\n    },\n    setCamera(code, setOptions = {}) {\n      rig.set(code, { blend: setOptions.blend === true });\n      drawn = pair.place(move(undefined, 0), aspect);\n      drawCrowd();\n      return info();\n    },\n    advance(frames) {\n      for (let i = 0; i < frames; i++) drawn = pair.place(move(undefined, ADVANCE_FRAME), aspect);\n      drawCrowd();\n      return info();\n    },\n    carry() {\n      drawn = pair.place(move(undefined, ADVANCE_FRAME), aspect);\n      crowdStale = true; // posed by the next frame or dump, as after a step\n    },\n    dump: (dumpOptions) => {\n      if (crowdStale) drawCrowd();\n      return dumpScene(stage.scene, dumpOptions);\n    },\n    dispose: () => stage.dispose(),\n  };\n  view.restarted();\n  view.frame({ alpha: 1, dt: 0, aspect });\n  return view;\n}\n","numLines":373,"startLine":1,"totalLines":373}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01FbaePisf48TpkzdCA85C2L","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgj99e56jAdLQj1xkqszY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FRprxazoHRb8YG8JSkrzdd","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211947__x8ab6bc/work/.research/my-3dge/engine/app/headless.ts","limit":150},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1535,"cache_read_input_tokens":130176,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1535},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b0d0401-1a79-4c2f-8a33-ba9239fdbfed","uuid":"f6f14516-b8ab-4deb-93fe-5431a16fd650","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:21:45.719Z","request_id":"req_011Cgj99dpibvpSxE9UeANtF","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01FRprxazoHRb8YG8JSkrzdd":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211947__x8ab6bc/work/.research/my-3dge/engine/app/headless.ts","limit":150}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FRprxazoHRb8YG8JSkrzdd","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t/**\n2\t * @file The engine without a page (PLAN.md §8.3, §6.9, WPs 1.6 and 2.7; doctrine: Verifiable): `createHeadless({\n3\t * scene, seed, settings, view })` starts a scene as a recorded session (engine/sim/scene.ts) and returns its\n4\t * inspector, the same object a page publishes as `window.__engine` minus a renderer: `render` and `shot` throw\n5\t * `DEV_NO_RENDERER`. With `view: true` it also builds the scene's presentation graph in Node (engine/app/view.ts: the\n6\t * stage and its camera, no GPU), so `scene.dump()` and `camera` work headless and view logic is tested in T1; the\n7\t * scene's level must be registered first (`APP_NO_LEVEL`). `x sim` runs scenes through it, and tests drive the sim\n8\t * with the same calls an agent makes in a page.\n9\t *\n10\t * Time: a headless engine has a frame clock over the run's settings, like a page, but no frames. `step(n, intents)`\n11\t * runs n steps at once, inside the session, so the steps are recorded and `headlessHost(h).session.record()` is the run\n12\t * as a replay. `pause`, `resume` and `timeScale` set the clock's settings as in a page (no real time passes headless,\n13\t * so only `step` runs steps). After each step the run hands the hit-stop its rules asked for (engine/sim/damage.ts\n14\t * `takeHitStop`) to its clock, whose budget shrinks stops that follow closely, so a page's frames stop and a crowd hit\n15\t * stutters once; a page's real-time `?replay=` playback hands them over the same way (`stepped`), and a dev action's\n16\t * goes with the next step, as in that playback. `seed(n)` starts the scene again with seed n, a new session and clock,\n17\t * keeping every setting that differs from what a fresh start gives; `replay(text)` starts the replay's run (its\n18\t * scene, seed and settings, keeping the view settings that differ, which never change play: a page's look stays) and\n19\t * plays it, with a page's loop held, so it drops the stops it asks for (none is left to freeze a later frame). The\n20\t * run's stats meter (engine/dev/stats.ts, `__engine.stats()`) times every step it runs, and the world's systems\n21\t * through the world's probe; a page times its frames through it and gives it the renderer's counts (`Drawing.counts`).\n22\t *\n23\t * `createAppHost` is the run behind both engines: engine/app/engine.ts adds a page's drawing to it. Invariants:\n24\t * everything runs synchronously after the promise resolves (the fdlibm swap holds only through synchronous entry\n25\t * points); runs share nothing but the registry; the inspector holds only its members, so the run behind it is reached\n26\t * through `headlessHost(h)` (tools only), whose `session` is what members get: the recorded operations and the world\n27\t * read-only (engine/dev/members.ts). Its `restore` and `act` move entities between steps, so they snap the view to the\n28\t * world (no interpolation from stale places), as a restart does. A seed is a whole number from 0 (`SIM_BAD_SEED`).\n29\t *\n30\t * @example\n31\t * import { createRegistry } from '../core/registry';\n32\t * import { defineScene } from '../sim/scene';\n33\t * const demo = defineScene('demo', { setup: (w) => void w.spawn() }, createRegistry());\n34\t * const h = await createHeadless({ scene: demo, seed: 3 });\n35\t * h.step(60); // 60: the tick after the steps\n36\t * h.entities(); // [{ id: 1, components: [] }]\n37\t * @see engine/app/headless.test.ts\n38\t */\n39\timport type { EventMap } from '../core/events';\n40\timport { codeError, defineCodes, log as sharedLog, type Log } from '../core/log';\n41\timport { registry as sharedRegistry, sameValue, type Registry } from '../core/registry';\n42\timport { isPlainObject } from '../core/schema';\n43\timport { createSettings, defineSettings, type SettingValue } from '../core/settings';\n44\timport { createClock, TIME_SETTINGS, type Clock } from '../core/time';\n45\timport '../dev/actions'; // registers `__engine.actions` and `__engine.bot`\n46\timport { createInspector, type Inspector } from '../dev/inspector';\n47\timport { recordedRun, type InspectorHost, type RecordedRun } from '../dev/members';\n48\timport { createStatsMeter, type RenderCounts, type StatsMeter } from '../dev/stats';\n49\timport { createMaterialLibrary, type MaterialLibrary } from '../gfx/materials/library';\n50\timport type { FrameReport } from '../gfx/renderer';\n51\timport type { ShotJson, ShotOptions } from '../gfx/shot';\n52\timport { virtualDeviceOf } from '../input/devices/inspector'; // registers `__engine.input` too\n53\timport { virtualIntents } from '../input/devices/virtual';\n54\timport { takeHitStop } from '../sim/damage';\n55\timport type { Replay } from '../sim/replay';\n56\timport { checkSeed, getScene, type Scene } from '../sim/scene';\n57\timport { createSession, type Session } from '../sim/session';\n58\timport type { AnyComponents } from '../sim/state';\n59\timport { playInto, type PlayIntoOptions, type PlayResult } from './playback';\n60\timport { createRunView, type RunView } from './view';\n61\timport type { AppHost } from './viewMembers';\n62\timport './animMember';\n63\timport './feelMember';\n64\timport './lookMember';\n65\timport './viewMembers';\n66\timport '../dev/eye'; // the agent eye's member: __engine.eye in a page and headless alike\n67\timport '../dev/galleryShoot'; // the gallery's members: __engine.gallery in a page and headless alike\n68\t\n69\t/** The codes this module raises, with their fixes. */\n70\texport const HEADLESS_CODES = defineCodes('app', {\n71\t  APP_NOT_HEADLESS: {\n72\t    template: 'headlessHost was given {value}, not a headless engine',\n73\t    fix: 'pass the object createHeadless resolved to',\n74\t  },\n75\t  APP_OTHER_SCENE: {\n76\t    template: 'this engine draws {shown}, so it cannot start {scene}',\n77\t    fix: \"play {scene} in its own page (labs/<name>/?scene=<name>), or headless: createHeadless({ scene: '{scene}' })\",\n78\t  },\n79\t});\n80\t\n81\t/** How a headless engine starts. */\n82\texport interface HeadlessOptions<C extends object = AnyComponents, E extends EventMap = EventMap> {\n83\t  /** The scene: an id on the registry, or the scene `defineScene` returned. */\n84\t  scene: string | Scene<C, E>;\n85\t  /** The seed every sim RNG stream derives from (1). */\n86\t  seed?: number;\n87\t  /** Setting values over the scene's, path → value (`x sim --set`). */\n88\t  settings?: Readonly<Record<string, unknown>>;\n89\t  /** Also build the scene's presentation graph (no GPU), for `scene.dump()` and `camera` (false). */\n90\t  view?: boolean;\n91\t  /** The camera code the view starts with (`cam=iso`). */\n92\t  cam?: string;\n93\t  /** Where scenes, components and settings are declared (the shared registry). */\n94\t  registry?: Registry;\n95\t  /** Where errors and advice are recorded (the shared log). */\n96\t  log?: Log;\n97\t}\n98\t\n99\t/** A headless engine: `__engine`'s members, over a scene running in this process. */\n100\texport type Headless = Inspector;\n101\t\n102\t/** What a page adds to the run's host (engine/app/engine.ts): its GPU and how it draws. */\n103\texport interface Drawing {\n104\t  /** Whether a renderer draws: false until it started, or when WebGPU refused (members that need one throw). */\n105\t  active(): boolean;\n106\t  readonly adapter: Readonly<Record<string, unknown>> | null;\n107\t  readonly features: readonly string[];\n108\t  readonly downgrades: readonly string[];\n109\t  /** Whether the page is up: its first frame drawn. */\n110\t  ready(): boolean;\n111\t  render(frames: number): Promise<FrameReport>;\n112\t  shot(options: ShotOptions): Promise<ShotJson>;\n113\t  /** Draws one frame of the run now, while a replay plays. */\n114\t  draw(): Promise<void>;\n115\t  /** Sets a view setting (it never changes play). */\n116\t  setView(path: string, value: SettingValue): void;\n117\t  /** The renderer's counts for `__engine.stats()`, null before it started. */\n118\t  counts(): RenderCounts | null;\n119\t}\n120\t\n121\t/** The run behind an engine: the inspector, its host, and the live session (app code only, never members). */\n122\texport interface AppRun {\n123\t  readonly inspector: Inspector;\n124\t  readonly host: AppHost;\n125\t  /** The live session: what the page's loop steps. */\n126\t  readonly session: Session;\n127\t  /** The frame clock over the run's settings. */\n128\t  readonly clock: Clock;\n129\t  /** The view, or null. */\n130\t  readonly view: RunView | null;\n131\t  /** Runs one step with `intents` through the session, hands its hit-stop to the clock, and lets the view read it. */\n132\t  stepOnce(intents: unknown): void;\n133\t  /**\n134\t   * After a step played outside `stepOnce` (a page's real-time `?replay=` playback): hands the step's hit-stop to the\n135\t   * clock and lets the view read the world, as `stepOnce` does.\n136\t   */\n137\t  stepped(): void;\n138\t  /** True while a replay plays: the page's loop steps nothing then. */\n139\t  readonly playing: boolean;\n140\t  /** Starts a replay's run (its scene, seed and settings), for playing it step by step; returns its session. */\n141\t  begin(replay: Replay): Session;\n142\t  /** The stats meter (engine/dev/stats.ts): it times every step and phase; a page times its frames through it. */\n143\t  readonly meter: StatsMeter;\n144\t}\n145\t\n146\t/** How `createAppHost` makes a run: `createHeadless`'s options, plus a page's drawing and material library. */\n147\texport interface AppHostOptions<\n148\t  C extends object = AnyComponents,\n149\t  E extends EventMap = EventMap,\n150\t> extends HeadlessOptions<C, E> {"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b0d0401-1a79-4c2f-8a33-ba9239fdbfed","uuid":"de8bd6ad-b979-4194-bad6-16a478d1788d","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:21:45.737Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211947__x8ab6bc/work/.research/my-3dge/engine/app/headless.ts","content":"/**\n * @file The engine without a page (PLAN.md §8.3, §6.9, WPs 1.6 and 2.7; doctrine: Verifiable): `createHeadless({\n * scene, seed, settings, view })` starts a scene as a recorded session (engine/sim/scene.ts) and returns its\n * inspector, the same object a page publishes as `window.__engine` minus a renderer: `render` and `shot` throw\n * `DEV_NO_RENDERER`. With `view: true` it also builds the scene's presentation graph in Node (engine/app/view.ts: the\n * stage and its camera, no GPU), so `scene.dump()` and `camera` work headless and view logic is tested in T1; the\n * scene's level must be registered first (`APP_NO_LEVEL`). `x sim` runs scenes through it, and tests drive the sim\n * with the same calls an agent makes in a page.\n *\n * Time: a headless engine has a frame clock over the run's settings, like a page, but no frames. `step(n, intents)`\n * runs n steps at once, inside the session, so the steps are recorded and `headlessHost(h).session.record()` is the run\n * as a replay. `pause`, `resume` and `timeScale` set the clock's settings as in a page (no real time passes headless,\n * so only `step` runs steps). After each step the run hands the hit-stop its rules asked for (engine/sim/damage.ts\n * `takeHitStop`) to its clock, whose budget shrinks stops that follow closely, so a page's frames stop and a crowd hit\n * stutters once; a page's real-time `?replay=` playback hands them over the same way (`stepped`), and a dev action's\n * goes with the next step, as in that playback. `seed(n)` starts the scene again with seed n, a new session and clock,\n * keeping every setting that differs from what a fresh start gives; `replay(text)` starts the replay's run (its\n * scene, seed and settings, keeping the view settings that differ, which never change play: a page's look stays) and\n * plays it, with a page's loop held, so it drops the stops it asks for (none is left to freeze a later frame). The\n * run's stats meter (engine/dev/stats.ts, `__engine.stats()`) times every step it runs, and the world's systems\n * through the world's probe; a page times its frames through it and gives it the renderer's counts (`Drawing.counts`).\n *\n * `createAppHost` is the run behind both engines: engine/app/engine.ts adds a page's drawing to it. Invariants:\n * everything runs synchronously after the promise resolves (the fdlibm swap holds only through synchronous entry\n * points); runs share nothing but the registry; the inspector holds only its members, so the run behind it is reached\n * through `headlessHost(h)` (tools only), whose `session` is what members get: the recorded operations and the world\n * read-only (engine/dev/members.ts). Its `restore` and `act` move entities between steps, so they snap the view to the\n * world (no interpolation from stale places), as a restart does. A seed is a whole number from 0 (`SIM_BAD_SEED`).\n *\n * @example\n * import { createRegistry } from '../core/registry';\n * import { defineScene } from '../sim/scene';\n * const demo = defineScene('demo', { setup: (w) => void w.spawn() }, createRegistry());\n * const h = await createHeadless({ scene: demo, seed: 3 });\n * h.step(60); // 60: the tick after the steps\n * h.entities(); // [{ id: 1, components: [] }]\n * @see engine/app/headless.test.ts\n */\nimport type { EventMap } from '../core/events';\nimport { codeError, defineCodes, log as sharedLog, type Log } from '../core/log';\nimport { registry as sharedRegistry, sameValue, type Registry } from '../core/registry';\nimport { isPlainObject } from '../core/schema';\nimport { createSettings, defineSettings, type SettingValue } from '../core/settings';\nimport { createClock, TIME_SETTINGS, type Clock } from '../core/time';\nimport '../dev/actions'; // registers `__engine.actions` and `__engine.bot`\nimport { createInspector, type Inspector } from '../dev/inspector';\nimport { recordedRun, type InspectorHost, type RecordedRun } from '../dev/members';\nimport { createStatsMeter, type RenderCounts, type StatsMeter } from '../dev/stats';\nimport { createMaterialLibrary, type MaterialLibrary } from '../gfx/materials/library';\nimport type { FrameReport } from '../gfx/renderer';\nimport type { ShotJson, ShotOptions } from '../gfx/shot';\nimport { virtualDeviceOf } from '../input/devices/inspector'; // registers `__engine.input` too\nimport { virtualIntents } from '../input/devices/virtual';\nimport { takeHitStop } from '../sim/damage';\nimport type { Replay } from '../sim/replay';\nimport { checkSeed, getScene, type Scene } from '../sim/scene';\nimport { createSession, type Session } from '../sim/session';\nimport type { AnyComponents } from '../sim/state';\nimport { playInto, type PlayIntoOptions, type PlayResult } from './playback';\nimport { createRunView, type RunView } from './view';\nimport type { AppHost } from './viewMembers';\nimport './animMember';\nimport './feelMember';\nimport './lookMember';\nimport './viewMembers';\nimport '../dev/eye'; // the agent eye's member: __engine.eye in a page and headless alike\nimport '../dev/galleryShoot'; // the gallery's members: __engine.gallery in a page and headless alike\n\n/** The codes this module raises, with their fixes. */\nexport const HEADLESS_CODES = defineCodes('app', {\n  APP_NOT_HEADLESS: {\n    template: 'headlessHost was given {value}, not a headless engine',\n    fix: 'pass the object createHeadless resolved to',\n  },\n  APP_OTHER_SCENE: {\n    template: 'this engine draws {shown}, so it cannot start {scene}',\n    fix: \"play {scene} in its own page (labs/<name>/?scene=<name>), or headless: createHeadless({ scene: '{scene}' })\",\n  },\n});\n\n/** How a headless engine starts. */\nexport interface HeadlessOptions<C extends object = AnyComponents, E extends EventMap = EventMap> {\n  /** The scene: an id on the registry, or the scene `defineScene` returned. */\n  scene: string | Scene<C, E>;\n  /** The seed every sim RNG stream derives from (1). */\n  seed?: number;\n  /** Setting values over the scene's, path → value (`x sim --set`). */\n  settings?: Readonly<Record<string, unknown>>;\n  /** Also build the scene's presentation graph (no GPU), for `scene.dump()` and `camera` (false). */\n  view?: boolean;\n  /** The camera code the view starts with (`cam=iso`). */\n  cam?: string;\n  /** Where scenes, components and settings are declared (the shared registry). */\n  registry?: Registry;\n  /** Where errors and advice are recorded (the shared log). */\n  log?: Log;\n}\n\n/** A headless engine: `__engine`'s members, over a scene running in this process. */\nexport type Headless = Inspector;\n\n/** What a page adds to the run's host (engine/app/engine.ts): its GPU and how it draws. */\nexport interface Drawing {\n  /** Whether a renderer draws: false until it started, or when WebGPU refused (members that need one throw). */\n  active(): boolean;\n  readonly adapter: Readonly<Record<string, unknown>> | null;\n  readonly features: readonly string[];\n  readonly downgrades: readonly string[];\n  /** Whether the page is up: its first frame drawn. */\n  ready(): boolean;\n  render(frames: number): Promise<FrameReport>;\n  shot(options: ShotOptions): Promise<ShotJson>;\n  /** Draws one frame of the run now, while a replay plays. */\n  draw(): Promise<void>;\n  /** Sets a view setting (it never changes play). */\n  setView(path: string, value: SettingValue): void;\n  /** The renderer's counts for `__engine.stats()`, null before it started. */\n  counts(): RenderCounts | null;\n}\n\n/** The run behind an engine: the inspector, its host, and the live session (app code only, never members). */\nexport interface AppRun {\n  readonly inspector: Inspector;\n  readonly host: AppHost;\n  /** The live session: what the page's loop steps. */\n  readonly session: Session;\n  /** The frame clock over the run's settings. */\n  readonly clock: Clock;\n  /** The view, or null. */\n  readonly view: RunView | null;\n  /** Runs one step with `intents` through the session, hands its hit-stop to the clock, and lets the view read it. */\n  stepOnce(intents: unknown): void;\n  /**\n   * After a step played outside `stepOnce` (a page's real-time `?replay=` playback): hands the step's hit-stop to the\n   * clock and lets the view read the world, as `stepOnce` does.\n   */\n  stepped(): void;\n  /** True while a replay plays: the page's loop steps nothing then. */\n  readonly playing: boolean;\n  /** Starts a replay's run (its scene, seed and settings), for playing it step by step; returns its session. */\n  begin(replay: Replay): Session;\n  /** The stats meter (engine/dev/stats.ts): it times every step and phase; a page times its frames through it. */\n  readonly meter: StatsMeter;\n}\n\n/** How `createAppHost` makes a run: `createHeadless`'s options, plus a page's drawing and material library. */\nexport interface AppHostOptions<\n  C extends object = AnyComponents,\n  E extends EventMap = EventMap,\n> extends HeadlessOptions<C, E> {","numLines":150,"startLine":1,"totalLines":358}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01FRprxazoHRb8YG8JSkrzdd","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgj99e56jAdLQj1xkqszY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BQaAMo81LWeaKSmK8ZktFw","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211947__x8ab6bc/work/.research/my-3dge/labs/box/README.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1535,"cache_read_input_tokens":130176,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1535},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b0d0401-1a79-4c2f-8a33-ba9239fdbfed","uuid":"6205a8a7-06df-42ad-91bb-12fd0bccec05","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:21:46.789Z","request_id":"req_011Cgj99dpibvpSxE9UeANtF","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01BQaAMo81LWeaKSmK8ZktFw":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211947__x8ab6bc/work/.research/my-3dge/labs/box/README.md"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BQaAMo81LWeaKSmK8ZktFw","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# The Stress Box\n2\t\n3\tThe engine's integration target (PLAN.md §9.0): a test scene, benchmark and sample that grows through six stages,\n4\teach proved by commands that need no display. Stage 1 (Box 1, gate G2): the box renders on WebGPU, steps headless\n5\twith golden hashes that hold in Node and in Chromium, and is inspected and set from `node x` and `window.__engine`.\n6\tStage 2 (Box 2, gate G3): a hero walks, dashes and jumps through the character controller, his body stepped by the\n7\tanimator, in replays whose hashes hold while the page renders and whatever the camera. Stage 3 (Box 3, gate G4): the\n8\thero climbs the hall's stairs to a gallery, walks its dais, and pushes and shoves its crates and barrels in replays\n9\tthat hold in Node and in the page. Stage 4 (Box 4, gate G5): the hall fills with a crowd of walkers, slimes and wisps,\n10\t100 to 5,000, that chase the hero round the pillars and up the stairs. Stage 5 (Box 5, gate G6): the hero fights the\n11\tcrowd with a sword and a bolt; it swings, pounces and shoots back, telegraphed, taking turns; blows kill, throw and\n12\tlaunch bodies, burst effects and show damage numbers, in replays that hold in Node and in the page. Stage 6 (Box 6,\n13\tgate G7): the box's looks on the hall with its props, the torch-lit hall with its flickering torches and fog, toon\n14\tshading with ink outlines, and the prototype's cel, pixel, bloom and FXAA over it, on the hall's rune floor, with no\n15\tpipeline built after a warm-up and the knock replay's goldens unchanged; the fight's blows through the bodies'\n16\treactions (walkers flinch, are knocked down and get up, the slain fall; the hero flinches) and the hero's cape, swung\n17\tby the view; and the benchmark, the fight and the crowd at 100, 1,000 and 5,000 within their budgets. Clip mode\n18\t(Phase 8): the hero and the mannequin play any clip of the animation library through the clip layer, the clip\n19\t`node x anim show` prints, frame for frame. Every claim below is checked by `tests/unit/box-readme.test.ts`: a\n20\tsetting, file or command named here that does not exist fails it.\n21\t\n22\t## The demo index\n23\t\n24\tEvery scene, what it proves, and the command that shows it; each scene opens in the page at `labs/box/?scene=<name>`.\n25\tA test (`tests/unit/box-readme.test.ts`) fails when a scene of `labs/box/scenes/` is missing here, or a `box.*`\n26\tsetting from the settings below.\n27\t\n28\t| Scene | What it proves | The command that shows it |\n29\t|---|---|---|\n30\t| `labs/box/scenes/room.ts` | Box 1: the box renders on WebGPU and steps headless, its goldens the same in Node and in Chromium; it is inspected and set from `node x` and `window.__engine`. | `node x replay tests/replays/box-1-room.replay.json --browser page` |\n31\t| `labs/box/scenes/room-hero.ts` | Box 2: the hero walks, dashes and jumps through the character controller, his body stepped by the animator; his goldens hold while the page renders, whatever the camera. | `node x replay tests/replays/box-2-jump.replay.json --browser page` |\n32\t| `labs/box/scenes/hall.ts` | Box 3: a physics level, its stairs, galleries and the dais's slopes walked and climbed, the cutaway showing the hero; the floor its rune bake (Box 6). | `node x replay tests/replays/box-3-climb.replay.json --browser page` |\n33\t| `labs/box/scenes/hall-props.ts` | Box 3: 10 to 300 props standing in Rapier, pushed and shoved, drawn as instanced batches; Box 6: its replay's goldens hold through every box look and a look of each material style. | `node x replay tests/replays/box-3-knock.replay.json --browser page` |\n34\t| `labs/box/scenes/crowd-100.ts` | Box 4: a crowd chasing the hero by flow field up the stairs, drawn through its level of detail; its goldens hold in the page. | `node x replay tests/replays/box-4-chase.replay.json --browser page` |\n35\t| `labs/box/scenes/crowd-1000.ts` | Box 4: the crowd's cost at 100, 1,000 and 5,000 agents, within budget. | `node x perf labs/box --scene crowd-1000 --ladder --budget` |\n36\t| `labs/box/scenes/crowd-5000.ts` | Box 4: 5,000 bodies entering with no pipeline built; Box 6: the benchmark's crowd, within budget; its page within budget, drawn through a GPU crowd (WP 11.4), and against the instancing service. | `node x perf labs/box --scene crowd-5000 --ladder --budget`, `node x perf labs/box --scene crowd-5000 --budget`, `node x perf labs/box --scene crowd-5000 --feature feature:gpuCrowds` |\n37\t| `labs/box/scenes/fight.ts` | Box 5: combat, its deaths, launches, telegraphs, effects and damage numbers drawn from the sim, its goldens the same with effects on and off; Box 6: its blows through the bodies' reactions (flinch, knockdown, get-up, death) and the hero's cape, which the ID pass sees. | `node x replay tests/replays/box-5-fight.replay.json --browser page` |\n38\t| `labs/box/scenes/fight-1000.ts` | Box 6: the benchmark, the fight at 100, 1,000 and 5,000, within budget. | `node x perf labs/box --scene fight-1000 --ladder --budget` |\n39\t| `labs/box/scenes/hall-props.ts`, every look | Box 6: every box look, and one of the engine's looks in each material style, renders on the hall with its props with no pipeline built after a warm-up, across every toggle, the knock replay's goldens unchanged (Looks, below); the engine's 98 looks each build nothing and keep the hash on the room (`tests/e2e/post.spec.ts`). Each test lists the scene and the looks it covered as its annotations (`looks`) in out/e2e/report.json. | `npm run e2e -- tests/e2e/box-look.spec.ts tests/e2e/parity.spec.ts` |\n40\t| `labs/box/sounds/page.ts` | Phase 9: the box plays its sim events as sounds, spatialized and ducked, with torch ambience and a demo song; the fight replay's sound timeline hashes the same in Node and in Chromium. | `npm run e2e -- tests/e2e/box-audio.spec.ts` |\n41\t| `labs/box/scenes/clips.ts` | Clip mode (Phase 8): the hero and the mannequin play any clip of the library's 1,218 through the clip layer, over the hero's own rig; the clip a setting names is the one `x anim show` prints, frame for frame; its replay's goldens are the same in Node and in Chromium, drawn or not (`node x replay tests/replays/box-8-clips.replay.json --browser page`). | `npm run e2e -- tests/e2e/box-clips.spec.ts` |\n42\t| `labs/box/scenes/ragdoll.ts` | Ragdolls (WP 10.2): a blow from the front, from behind, a launch and a death hand four partners off to their ragdolls, joints as data on Rapier, and each gets up the way it lies (the dead one when the cycle stands it), its goldens the same in Node and in Chromium; `box.ragdoll.handOff` off, they fall through their reactions' timelines instead. | `node x replay tests/replays/ragdoll-falls.replay.json tests/replays/ragdoll-strike.replay.json --browser sim` |\n43\t\n44\tThe benchmark's budgets and the numbers they were measured from are in `tests/baselines/perf/box-fight-1000.json`\n45\tand `tests/baselines/perf/box-crowd-5000.json`.\n46\t\n47\t## Scenes\n48\t\n49\t| Scene | What it shows | Covered by |\n50\t|---|---|---|\n51\t| `box:room` (`labs/box/scenes/room.ts`) | The room, `labs/box/levels/room.txt`: 16 × 12 m of flagstones in brick walls 3 m high, one low wall (0.75 m), a 2 × 2 m pillar, the hero's spawn and three numbered markers. Three crates move on fixed paths from the markers, no physics yet: along the low wall, round a circle, round the pillar. | `tests/e2e/box.spec.ts`, `tests/e2e/parity.spec.ts`, `tests/replays/box-1-room.replay.json`, `tests/replays/box-1-tuned.replay.json`, `labs/box/scenes/room.test.ts`, `tests/baselines/thumbs/box-room-iso.json` |\n52\t| `box:room-hero` (`labs/box/scenes/room-hero.ts`) | The same room as a physics level, and the hero (`labs/box/cast/hero.ts`: the stress test's speeds and timings, 5 m/s, a 1.46 m jump, a 3.25 m dash) at the spawn, the player: he walks (WASD, a stick), jumps (Space) onto the low wall but not the walls, and dashes (Shift); his animator steps his body with the sim, drawn as the neutral humanoid. Every camera follows him, and the walls and the pillar before him cut away; first person hides his body but his hands. | `tests/e2e/box-hero.spec.ts`, `tests/e2e/parity.spec.ts`, `tests/replays/box-2-walk.replay.json`, `tests/replays/box-2-dash.replay.json`, `tests/replays/box-2-jump.replay.json`, `labs/box/scenes/room-hero.test.ts`, `labs/box/cast/hero.test.ts` |\n53\t| `box:hall` (`labs/box/scenes/hall.ts`) | The hall, `labs/box/levels/hall.txt`, as a physics level: 64 × 44 m inside walls 3 m high, a grid of pillars, low walls, 30 brazier stands, two galleries 1 m up along the north wall with stairs rising to each, and the octagonal rune dais at the centre, 0.5 m up. The hero starts on the dais: he walks down its slopes and up them, climbs the stairs to the galleries, jumps onto the low walls; the walls and pillars before him cut away. Its floor is its bake (`labs/box/looks/hall-floor.ts`): flagstones, moss creeping from the walls' feet, contact shadows along them, and the rune circle glowing on the dais. | `tests/e2e/box-hall.spec.ts`, `tests/e2e/parity.spec.ts`, `tests/replays/box-3-climb.replay.json`, `tests/replays/box-3-dais.replay.json`, `labs/box/scenes/hall.test.ts`, `tests/baselines/thumbs/box-hall-iso.json` |\n54\t| `box:hall-props` (`labs/box/scenes/hall-props.ts`) | The hall with the hero and its props, standing in Rapier and drawn through one instanced batch per prop part: a brazier's fire on each of the 30 stands, and 100 crates and barrels (10 to 300) on the prototype's seeded spots, every fifth crate stacked on the one before where both are crates. He pushes them by walking into them, and shoves (J, the left mouse button) every prop within 1.9 m in his arc, knocking it away, both hands thrust forward. | `tests/e2e/box-hall.spec.ts`, `tests/e2e/parity.spec.ts`, `tests/replays/box-3-knock.replay.json`, `labs/box/scenes/hall-props.test.ts` |\n55\t| `box:crowd-1000` (`labs/box/scenes/crowd-1000.ts`) | The hall with its hero and a crowd of 1,000 (its presets for 100 and 5,000 are `labs/box/scenes/crowd-100.ts` and `labs/box/scenes/crowd-5000.ts`, at `?scene=crowd-100` and `?scene=crowd-5000`): walkers (`labs/box/cast/walker.ts`, capsules walking at 1.75 to 2.5 m/s), slimes (`labs/box/cast/slime.ts`, balls hopping up to 2.75 m) and wisps (`labs/box/cast/wisp.ts`, flyers hovering 1.25 m up), half, three in ten and two in ten, queued at the start on the hall's floor and entering 25 a step. They chase the hero along a flow field toward his tile, round the pillars and up the stairs when he climbs to a gallery; level with him the walkers wait on a ring 1.5 m round him and the slimes on one 2.1 m round him, and the wisps circle him 4.4 to 6.3 m out. Their bodies push each other apart in Rapier, and the hero's capsule shoves them aside (his `shoves: ['crowd']`): with 1,000 pressing round him at the stairs' foot he still climbs to the gallery (box-4-stairs). The page draws them through a crowd (instanced batches; while `feature:gpuCrowds` is on, a GPU crowd's: a draw call a batch, its instances culled against the view on the GPU, `gfx.featuresOff` turning it off), each posed at the detail its distance from the camera allows: walkers as the neutral humanoid in four builds, slimes as blobs with horns, ears or wings, wisps as floaters with their motes. | `tests/e2e/box-crowd.spec.ts`, `tests/e2e/parity.spec.ts`, `tests/replays/box-4-chase.replay.json`, `tests/replays/box-4-hop.replay.json`, `tests/replays/box-4-stairs.replay.json`, `labs/box/scenes/crowd-1000.test.ts`, `labs/box/cast/crowd.test.ts`, `tests/baselines/perf/box-crowd-1000.json` |\n56\t| `box:fight` (`labs/box/scenes/fight.ts`) | Box 5: the hall, its hero with a sword (`HERO_FIGHT`, `labs/box/cast/hero.ts`) and a crowd of 36, mixed (its preset for 1,000 is `labs/box/scenes/fight-1000.ts`, at `?scene=fight-1000`), fighting. Attack (J, the left mouse button) runs his combo, a slash, a backslash and a spin, and out of a dash the thrust; skill (L, the right mouse button) fires a bolt (`labs/box/scenes/fight-hero.ts`). The walkers swing their fists, the slimes pounce and the wisps shoot (`WALKER_ATTACK`, `SLIME_ATTACK`, `WISP_ATTACK` in the cast's files; `labs/box/scenes/fight-foes.ts`), each telegraphing on the floor while it winds up, the walkers and slimes three at a time through his attack tokens. Blows land through the engine's `damage` (`labs/box/scenes/fight-rules.ts`): hit points, pushes, big hits throwing bodies up a little and killing ones throwing them high, corpses the crowd walks through, hit-stop, and the events the page draws effects and damage numbers from. Each blow goes through the body's reactions (the component `reactions`, Box 6): a walker flinches, a big blow knocks it down and it gets up the way it lies, acting on nothing meanwhile, and a killing one fells it; a foe's blow flinches the hero. He wears a cape (the component `secondary`), which the view swings and the ID pass names as his (actor#1/cape). | `tests/e2e/box-fight.spec.ts`, `tests/e2e/parity.spec.ts`, `tests/replays/box-5-fight.replay.json`, `tests/replays/box-5-precise.replay.json`, `labs/box/scenes/fight.test.ts` |\n57\t| `box:clips` (`labs/box/scenes/clips.ts`) | Clip mode, the Mocap Lab's: the room, the hero at its spawn and the mannequin 1.5 m east of him (`body:mannequin` on `build:mannequin`, the figure the Quaternius clips were measured on), both playing the clip `box.clips.clip` names through the clip layer in their animators, the hero's retargeted to his build. He stays the player and walks under it; masked to his upper body (`box.clips.mask`), his legs keep their own walk. A new clip crossfades in from the pose on screen; a one-shot holds its end 0.8 s, then plays again; clips that travel play in place. The page loads the library first: every set under `data/anim/sets`, registered as a `clipset` (`__engine.describe('clipset')`); `node x sim`, `node x replay` and the sim-only page register it too. | `tests/e2e/box-clips.spec.ts`, `tests/e2e/parity.spec.ts`, `tests/replays/box-8-clips.replay.json`, `labs/box/scenes/clips.test.ts` |\n58\t| `box:ragdoll` (`labs/box/scenes/ragdoll.ts`) | Ragdolls (WP 10.2): the room as a physics level, the hero at its spawn and four sparring partners on `build:adult` across its south half, each where it falls on open floor in view, facing him. Every 8 s a blow lands on each in turn: the first from the front (it falls onto its back), the second from behind (onto its face), the third a launch, up and to the south-east, the fourth a killing one; each falls as a ragdoll (engine/sim/ragdolls.ts: eleven capsules held by balls with a body's limits and hinges at the elbows and knees, faded onto the puppet) and gets up the way it lies once its trunk lies still, the dead one when the cycle stands it up at 6 s; at each cycle's start a partner standing is put back on its spot. His attack (J) knocks down the partner nearest in front of him, within 2.5 m. | `labs/box/scenes/ragdoll.test.ts`, `tests/replays/ragdoll-falls.replay.json`, `tests/replays/ragdoll-strike.replay.json`, `engine/sim/ragdolls.test.ts` |\n59\t\n60\tThe page draws each mover as a crate: an entity is drawn as a stand-in box when one of its components declares `x`\n61\tand `z` in metres (engine/gfx/stage.ts), until it draws itself: actors with an animator are puppets from Box 2\n62\t(engine/gfx/puppets/actors.ts), props a scene stands with `spawnProp` (engine/sim/props.ts) are drawn as their\n63\tprops from Box 3 (engine/gfx/stageProps.ts), and crowd bodies (`crowdBody`, engine/sim/crowdBodies.ts) through a crowd\n64\twith its level of detail from Box 4 (engine/gfx/stageCrowd.ts).\n65\t\n66\t## Looks\n67\t\n68\tA look is how the page draws a scene, as data (`node x describe look`): the sky that lights it, a material style and a\n69\tfilter chain; a look never changes play, so any scene can show any look. The box's own (`labs/box/looks/`) are the\n70\ttorch-lit hall and the prototype's looks over it; the engine's 98 (`look:cartoon`, `look:game-boy`, the one-filter\n71\tpresets…) show in the box too. What is proved, on the hall with its props: every box look, and one engine look of each\n72\tmaterial style, builds nothing after its warm-up and keeps the knock replay's goldens (`tests/e2e/box-look.spec.ts`,\n73\t`tests/e2e/parity.spec.ts`); each of the engine's 98 does the same on the room (`tests/e2e/post.spec.ts`).\n74\t\n75\t| Look | What it draws |\n76\t|---|---|\n77\t| `look:torch-lit` (`labs/box/looks/torch-lit.ts`) | The torch-lit hall: the sky `sky:hall`, dark but for the torches (all 30 with tiled lighting, else the 12 nearest the hero), each flickering on its own, the nearest casting shadows, and fog from 12 m past him. |\n78\t| `look:torch-toon` (`labs/box/looks/torch-toon.ts`) | Toon shading in it: three bands of light with a rim, the characters and objects inked. |\n79\t| `look:torch-cel` (`labs/box/looks/torch-cel.ts`) | The prototype's comic cel in it: four flat bands, pushed colour, ink lines. |\n80\t| `look:torch-pixel` (`labs/box/looks/torch-pixel.ts`) | The prototype's pixel look in it: 4 px blocks, 8 shades a channel, dithered. |\n81\t| `look:torch-bloom` (`labs/box/looks/torch-bloom.ts`) | Bloom in it: the flames, coals, runes and sparks glow (off at the `low` tier). |\n82\t| `look:torch-fxaa` (`labs/box/looks/torch-fxaa.ts`) | FXAA in it: every edge smoothed. |\n83\t| `look:daylight` (`labs/box/looks/daylight.ts`) | A plain day: the sky `sky:daylight`, its sun casting through three cascades on a renderer with cascaded shadows; `tests/e2e/enhanced.spec.ts` draws it on the crowd arena. |\n84\t\n85\tSwitch with `?post.look=look:torch-toon` (`labs/box/?scene=fight&cam3=chase&post.look=look:torch-toon`), with\n86\t`node x set post.look look:torch-toon` in an inspect session, or with `__engine.set('post.look', 'look:torch-toon')`;\n87\t`look:clean` is the scene's own. The first switch to the torch-lit sky, or to a material style, warms up first (on\n88\tSwiftShader, about a minute for the hall in a style under the sky; a GPU takes a moment); from then on a switch builds\n89\tnothing. `quality` sets how many torches cast shadows: 2 at `high`, 1 at `medium`, none at `low`. A new look comes\n90\tfrom `node x new look labs/box/looks/<name>`; the page imports every module under `labs/box/looks/`.\n91\t\n92\tThe chain's shading (WP 11.5: `ao`, `gi`, `air` and `ssr`, laid on any look with `post.filters`, as in\n93\t`labs/box/?scene=room&post.filters={\"air\":{\"scope\":\"all\"}}`, or by the looks `look:sunbeams`, `look:lamplit-fog` and\n94\tthe engine's air presets) is measured on the room by `tests/e2e/enhanced.spec.ts`. The box draws no metal, so its\n95\treflections show on `tests/pages/shading.html` instead.\n96\t\n97\t## Sound\n98\t\n99\tThe box sounds through its page (`labs/box/sounds/page.ts`, `window.__boxSound`): silent until the first key, click or\n100\tend of a touch. It then plays the sim's events as sounds (`labs/box/sounds/events.ts`: footsteps by the surface\n101\tunderfoot, landings, jumps and dashes, hits, bolts launched, pounces, and deaths that duck the music), placed where they\n102\thappen and muffled behind walls. The level sets the room's reverb, and the two torches nearest the camera crackle\n103\t(`sfx:boxTorch`). The demo song is `song:boxHall` (`labs/box/sounds/boxHall.ts`); its drums and lead join while blows\n104\tland. The effects are `labs/box/sounds/effects.ts`: `node x qa audio` checks them, and\n105\t`node x audio sfx:boxHit --spectrogram` shows one. The fight replay's sound timeline hashes the same in Node and in\n106\tChromium (`tests/e2e/box-audio.spec.ts`).\n107\t\n108\t## Settings\n109\t\n110\t| Setting | What it tunes |\n111\t|---|---|\n112\t| `box.room.speed` | How fast the movers go along their paths, m/s (1.5). Changes play: recorded in replays. |\n113\t| `box.room.movers` | How many of the three movers run (3), when the scene starts. |\n114\t| `box.roomHero.speed` | How fast the hero walks, m/s (5), when the scene starts. Changes play: recorded in replays. |\n115\t| `box.roomHero.jump` | The hero's take-off speed, m/s (9.375: a 1.46 m apex under his 30 m/s² gravity), when the scene starts. |\n116\t| `box.roomHero.dash` | The hero's dash speed, m/s (16.25, for 0.2 s; 0 turns it off), when the scene starts. |\n117\t| `box.hall.speed` | How fast the hero walks in the hall, m/s (5), when the scene starts. Changes play: recorded in replays. |\n118\t| `box.hall.jump` | The hero's take-off speed in the hall, m/s (9.375), when the scene starts: below about 7.75 m/s he no longer jumps onto the galleries, 1 m up, and climbs to them by the stairs alone. |\n119\t| `box.hall.dash` | The hero's dash speed in the hall, m/s (16.25, for 0.2 s; 0 turns it off), when the scene starts. |\n120\t| `box.hallProps.count` | How many crates and barrels stand in the hall with its props (100, 10 to 300), when the scene starts. Changes play: recorded in replays. |\n121\t| `box.crowd.count` | How many walkers, slimes and wisps fill the hall with the crowd (1,000 in `box:crowd-1000`, 100 and 5,000 in its presets; 0 to 5,000), when the scene starts. Changes play: recorded in replays. |\n122\t| `box.crowd.mix` | Who fills it: `mixed` (half walkers, three in ten slimes, two in ten wisps), `walkers`, `slimes` or `wisps`, when the scene starts. |\n123\t| `box.fight.god` | Whether foes' blows only flinch and push the hero in the fight (true, as the prototype's proof ran) or also take his hit points (false: at none he rallies at once), when the scene starts. |\n124\t| `box.fight.precise` | Whether the fight's hero is posed in the sim every step (his animator's precise hits), so his sword's trail is sim data in the hash (false by default; `tests/replays/box-5-precise.replay.json` plays it on), when the scene starts. |\n125\t| `box.clips.clip` | The clip the figures play in clip mode, `<set>/<clip>` as `node x anim find cartwheel` lists them (the Quaternius set's Dance_Loop by default), or a name only one set has. Changes play: recorded in replays. |\n126\t| `box.clips.speed` | The rate it plays at (1; 0 holds it). |\n127\t| `box.clips.frame` | Frame stepping: the frame of its bake held, from 0, 30 a second (-1 plays). |\n128\t| `box.clips.mirror` | Whether it plays mirrored (false). |\n129\t| `box.clips.mask` | The joints it plays: `full`, or `upper` over the legs' own walk. |\n130\t| `box.clips.cast` | Who plays it: `both`, `mannequin` or `hero`, when the scene starts. |\n131\t| `box.clips.ik` | Whether the figures plant their feet and lift over the floor (true), when the scene starts. |\n132\t| `box.ragdoll.handOff` | Whether a hard blow or a death hands a partner of `box:ragdoll` off to its ragdoll (true) or lets it fall through its reactions' timelines (false), when the scene starts. Changes play: recorded in replays. |\n133\t| `box.ragdoll.push` | How hard `box:ragdoll`'s blows land, m/s along the blow (3.5), when the scene starts. |\n134\t| `post.look` | The look drawn (`look:clean`, the scene's own; the box's looks above). A view setting: never in the hash. |\n135\t| `quality` | The quality tier: `auto` (`high` on a desktop), `high`, `medium` or `low`: shadow casters, bloom, pixel caps. A view setting. |\n136\t| `gfx.effects` | Whether the fight's effects draw (true): bolts, telegraphs, trails, bursts. A view setting. |\n137\t| `gfx.resolution` | The resolution mode: `auto` (the default: the look's `resolution`, `pixels` for a look naming none, as every box look does), `pixels`, `balanced` or `full`. A view setting: never in the hash. |\n138\t| `time.scale` | Sim seconds per real second (1). A view setting. |\n139\t| `touch` | The touch controls: `auto`, `on` or `off`. A view setting (below). |\n140\t| `box.menu` | The page's menu for humans (below): `auto` shows it unless automation drives the browser, `on` and `off` force it, when the page opens. A view setting. |\n141\t\n142\tSet one with `node x set box.room.speed 3`, as a URL parameter (`labs/box/?box.room.speed=3`), or with\n143\t`__engine.set('box.room.speed', 3)`; `node x describe setting` lists them all.\n144\t\n145\t## The page\n146\t\n147\t`labs/box/` opens the room (at its own path, listed by the labs index; the site's landing page, `index.html`, opens\n148\tthe playground). Its routes: `?scene=room`, `?seed=4`,\n149\t`?cam=iso` (a camera code: `cam=topdown`, `cam=iso,45,2,persp`, `cam3=orbit`, `cam3=fly`; with the hero also\n150\t`cam3=chase`, `cam3=first` and `cam3=rail`, which follow him), any setting by its path,\n151\tand `?replay=box-1-room` (a replay played in real time; `?replay=box-2-jump` opens the hero's room, `?replay=box-3-climb`\n152\tthe hall, `?replay=box-3-knock` the hall with its props, `?replay=box-4-chase` the hall with a crowd of 100, `?replay=box-5-fight` the fight, `?replay=box-8-clips` clip mode)\n153\tand `?post.look=look:torch-lit` (a look, above). In the page,\n154\t`window.__engine.help()` lists every member.\n155\t\n156\tThe page opens with its menu for humans (`labs/box/menu.ts`) in the top-left corner: every scene above as a link with\n157\ta one-line label, the replays, cameras (`cam3=chase`, `cam3=first`, `cam3=orbit`, `cam=iso`, `cam=topdown`) and looks\n158\t(the box's, then `look:cartoon`, `look:game-boy` and a few more of the engine's) that keep the scene, and the\n159\tcontrols, read from the action map the page's input binds (`actionMap:thirdPerson`: WASD or the arrows move, Space\n160\tjumps, Shift dashes, the left button or J attacks, the right button or L fires the bolt, E interacts), with the\n161\twheel's zoom and the first click or key that starts the sound. Its button or M shows and hides it; no action map binds\n162\tM (`tests/e2e/box-menu.spec.ts`). The page remembers the last toggle in the browser: closed, the menu stays closed\n163\tacross reloads and its own links, its button still in the corner, until it is opened again. A browser that automation drives (navigator.webdriver: every e2e spec and every `x`\n164\tcommand that opens the page) gets none of it, so no test's screenshot holds it, and `__engine.shot` reads the GPU,\n165\tnever the page; `?box.menu=on` shows it there.\n166\t\n167\t`?scene=clips` opens clip mode (`labs/box/?scene=clips&box.clips.clip=cmu/Cartwheel&cam=threequarter`); the page loads\n168\tthe animation library for it and its replays alone. The page ships the clips, so it always shows 100STYLE's credit (CC BY 4.0,\n169\t`data/anim/SOURCES.md`) in its corner.\n170\t\n171\tOn a phone or tablet the page shows the touch controls (`labs/box/touch.ts`, for every scene): a floating stick\n172\twherever the thumb lands, attack as the main button, and jump, dash and the bolt beside it. The menu is a page panel\n173\tthere: it starts below its button and scrolls, the touch buttons hide while it is open, and a tap on the game closes\n174\tit. Like the rest of the touch layer they are not tested (ADR-0021); `labs/box/?touch=on` shows them on a desktop.\n175\t\n176\t## The quick loop\n177\t\n178\t1. Change a setting or the scene, then run it headless: `node x sim labs/box/scenes/room --steps 600 --set box.room.speed=3`;\n179\t   for the hero, `node x sim labs/box/scenes/room-hero --feel --set box.roomHero.speed=6` also prints how he handles.\n180\t   `x sim` steps with no intents: its replay (`out/sim/box-<name>/run.replay.json`) has empty `inputs`, which you edit to\n181\t   drive the hero (`[0, { \"move\": [0, 1] }]` walks him south, +Z; tests/replays/README.md, \"Coordinates and inputs\").\n182\t2. See it as numbers: `node x shot labs/box --scene room --cam iso` (the ID pass and the look metrics; `--png` for\n183\t   a picture, `--thumb box-room-iso` against the baseline); for the hall,\n184\t   `node x shot labs/box --scene hall --cam iso --thumb box-hall-iso`; for the crowd,\n185\t   `node x sim labs/box/scenes/crowd-100 --steps 600 --set box.crowd.mix=slimes`, and its cost at 100, 1,000 and\n186\t   5,000, `node x perf labs/box --scene crowd-1000 --ladder`; for the fight,\n187\t   `node x sim labs/box/scenes/fight --steps 600 --set box.fight.god=false`; in a look,\n188\t   `node x shot labs/box --scene hall --cam iso --set post.look=look:torch-cel`; in clip mode,\n189\t   `node x anim show Cartwheel` (the clip as text) and\n190\t   `node x shot labs/box --scene clips --cam threequarter,0,5 --set box.clips.clip=cmu/Cartwheel --set box.clips.frame=30`.\n191\t3. Prove play: `node x replay tests/replays/box-1-room.replay.json --browser page` (the goldens, in Node and in the\n192\t   page while it renders); `node x replay tests/replays/box-2-jump.replay.json --browser page` for the hero,\n193\t   `node x replay tests/replays/box-3-climb.replay.json --browser page` in the hall,\n194\t   `node x replay tests/replays/box-4-chase.replay.json --browser page` with the crowd,\n195\t   `node x replay tests/replays/box-5-fight.replay.json --browser page` in the fight,\n196\t   `node x replay tests/replays/box-8-clips.replay.json --browser page` in clip mode, and with `--state` (or\n197\t   `--until 300`) the state a run reaches, in out/replay/<name>/state.json: where the hero, the props and the\n198\t   bodies ended, every component; the crowd's budgets,\n199\t   `node x perf labs/box --scene crowd-1000 --ladder --budget`, and the benchmark's,\n200\t   `node x perf labs/box --scene fight-1000 --ladder --budget` and\n201\t   `node x perf labs/box --scene crowd-5000 --ladder --budget`.\n202\t4. Keep a page open while iterating: `node x inspect --scene room`, then `node x eval \"__engine.hash()\"`,\n203\t   `node x set box.room.speed 3`, `node x dump --step 60 --filter pathMover` and `node x shot labs/box --scene room`\n204\t   (it reuses the session); `node x inspect --stop` ends it.\n205\t5. Commit with the suites green: `npm run e2e -- tests/e2e/box.spec.ts tests/e2e/parity.spec.ts`, and for the hall\n206\t   `npm run e2e -- tests/e2e/box-hall.spec.ts`, for the crowd `npm run e2e -- tests/e2e/box-crowd.spec.ts`, for the\n207\t   fight `npm run e2e -- tests/e2e/box-fight.spec.ts`, for the looks `npm run e2e -- tests/e2e/box-look.spec.ts`, for\n208\t   clip mode `npm run e2e -- tests/e2e/box-clips.spec.ts`.\n209\t\n210\t## Adding a scene or a variant\n211\t\n212\tA variant is a new scene file or a settings preset, never a change of meaning in a passing scene (PLAN.md §9.0).\n213\t`node x new scene labs/box/scenes/<name>` writes a box scene with its replay test, which passes its checks; the page\n214\timports every module under `labs/box/scenes/`, so it opens at `labs/box/?scene=<name>`. Then keep a replay of it, the\n215\tsequence `tests/e2e/parity.spec.ts` runs on a new scene:\n216\t\n217\t1. `node x sim labs/box/scenes/<name> --steps 600` writes the run's replay beside its report, with no intents.\n218\t2. Copy `out/sim/box-<name>/run.replay.json` to `tests/replays/box-<stage>-<name>.replay.json`. `<stage>` is the\n219\t   stage the scene proves; a variant outside every stage's claims takes the newest stage's number (the highest\n220\t   `box-<n>-` among tests/replays/) and stays out of `STAGES`. Edit its `inputs` to drive it before you record (tests/replays/README.md,\n221\t   \"Coordinates and inputs\": `move` is world [x, z], +X east, +Z south); `node x replay <file> --state` then shows\n222\t   where the run ends.\n223\t3. `node x replay <file> --browser sim --update` records its goldens, which hold in Node and in Chromium.\n224\t4. `node x replay <file> --browser page` checks them while the page renders.\n225\t5. List the scene and the replay here, with what it shows, what covers it and the settings that tune it (the demo\n226\t   index and the settings table: `tests/unit/box-readme.test.ts` fails a scene or a `box.*` setting left out).\n227\t6. When it belongs to a stage, add it to `STAGES` in `tests/e2e/parity-stages.ts`: T2's rendering-page check plays\n228\t   only the replays named there.\n229\t\n230\t## Adding a prop\n231\t\n232\t`labs/box/scenes/hall-props.ts` is the worked example. A prop is data (engine/world/props: its parts, its body, where\n233\ta level places it):\n234\t\n235\t1. `node x new prop labs/box/props/<name>` writes `prop:<name>` and its test (its parts build clean and stand as tall\n236\t   as its body), which pass their checks; `node x qa geo tex --only prop:<name>` checks its parts and textures and\n237\t   counts what it checked (a prefix that keeps nothing is a usage error naming the closest ids).\n238\t2. Import it from the scene that shows it (`import '../props/<name>';`): the page reaches labs/box/props/ only\n239\t   through the scenes it imports, and QA through its own import of every module there.\n240\t3. The scene needs a physics world and floors to stand on: `physics: true`, then in `setup`\n241\t   `addLevelBodies(physicsOf(w), <compiled level>)` (the template's `level: 'level:room'` has none: the page draws\n242\t   the room, but nothing in it is solid; `labs/box/scenes/room-hero.ts` exports the room compiled as\n243\t   `ROOM_HERO_LEVEL`, `labs/box/scenes/hall.ts` the hall as `HALL_LEVEL`).\n244\t4. Stand it: `spawnProp(w, { prop: 'prop:<name>', at: [x, y, z], yaw })`, its base at `at` (m), turned `yaw` (rad)\n245\t   about +Y; it returns the entity, whose `sceneProp` component the sim hashes and the view draws as the prop.\n246\t5. Or let the level place it: give the prop `place: { spawn: '<spot>' }` and the level a glyph with that spawn\n247\t   (`defineGlyph('glyph:<spot>', { char, description, mesh: 'floor', spawn: '<spot>' })` in the scene module, before\n248\t   the level compiles), then `for (const placement of levelProps(<compiled level>)) spawnProp(w, placement);`. The\n249\t   digits are the engine's own spawns (`3` places at `spawn:3`).\n250\t\n251\tTile (col, row) of a level has its centre at x = (col + 0.5) × tile, z = (row + 0.5) × tile (1 m tiles in the box),\n252\trows running +Z (south), as tests/replays/README.md says.\n253\t\n254\tThe `stress-box` skill (`.claude/skills/stress-box/SKILL.md`) says the rest.\n255\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b0d0401-1a79-4c2f-8a33-ba9239fdbfed","uuid":"9e7fad5b-2b81-4c39-8eee-3de74217e19d","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:21:46.945Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211947__x8ab6bc/work/.research/my-3dge/labs/box/README.md","content":"# The Stress Box\n\nThe engine's integration target (PLAN.md §9.0): a test scene, benchmark and sample that grows through six stages,\neach proved by commands that need no display. Stage 1 (Box 1, gate G2): the box renders on WebGPU, steps headless\nwith golden hashes that hold in Node and in Chromium, and is inspected and set from `node x` and `window.__engine`.\nStage 2 (Box 2, gate G3): a hero walks, dashes and jumps through the character controller, his body stepped by the\nanimator, in replays whose hashes hold while the page renders and whatever the camera. Stage 3 (Box 3, gate G4): the\nhero climbs the hall's stairs to a gallery, walks its dais, and pushes and shoves its crates and barrels in replays\nthat hold in Node and in the page. Stage 4 (Box 4, gate G5): the hall fills with a crowd of walkers, slimes and wisps,\n100 to 5,000, that chase the hero round the pillars and up the stairs. Stage 5 (Box 5, gate G6): the hero fights the\ncrowd with a sword and a bolt; it swings, pounces and shoots back, telegraphed, taking turns; blows kill, throw and\nlaunch bodies, burst effects and show damage numbers, in replays that hold in Node and in the page. Stage 6 (Box 6,\ngate G7): the box's looks on the hall with its props, the torch-lit hall with its flickering torches and fog, toon\nshading with ink outlines, and the prototype's cel, pixel, bloom and FXAA over it, on the hall's rune floor, with no\npipeline built after a warm-up and the knock replay's goldens unchanged; the fight's blows through the bodies'\nreactions (walkers flinch, are knocked down and get up, the slain fall; the hero flinches) and the hero's cape, swung\nby the view; and the benchmark, the fight and the crowd at 100, 1,000 and 5,000 within their budgets. Clip mode\n(Phase 8): the hero and the mannequin play any clip of the animation library through the clip layer, the clip\n`node x anim show` prints, frame for frame. Every claim below is checked by `tests/unit/box-readme.test.ts`: a\nsetting, file or command named here that does not exist fails it.\n\n## The demo index\n\nEvery scene, what it proves, and the command that shows it; each scene opens in the page at `labs/box/?scene=<name>`.\nA test (`tests/unit/box-readme.test.ts`) fails when a scene of `labs/box/scenes/` is missing here, or a `box.*`\nsetting from the settings below.\n\n| Scene | What it proves | The command that shows it |\n|---|---|---|\n| `labs/box/scenes/room.ts` | Box 1: the box renders on WebGPU and steps headless, its goldens the same in Node and in Chromium; it is inspected and set from `node x` and `window.__engine`. | `node x replay tests/replays/box-1-room.replay.json --browser page` |\n| `labs/box/scenes/room-hero.ts` | Box 2: the hero walks, dashes and jumps through the character controller, his body stepped by the animator; his goldens hold while the page renders, whatever the camera. | `node x replay tests/replays/box-2-jump.replay.json --browser page` |\n| `labs/box/scenes/hall.ts` | Box 3: a physics level, its stairs, galleries and the dais's slopes walked and climbed, the cutaway showing the hero; the floor its rune bake (Box 6). | `node x replay tests/replays/box-3-climb.replay.json --browser page` |\n| `labs/box/scenes/hall-props.ts` | Box 3: 10 to 300 props standing in Rapier, pushed and shoved, drawn as instanced batches; Box 6: its replay's goldens hold through every box look and a look of each material style. | `node x replay tests/replays/box-3-knock.replay.json --browser page` |\n| `labs/box/scenes/crowd-100.ts` | Box 4: a crowd chasing the hero by flow field up the stairs, drawn through its level of detail; its goldens hold in the page. | `node x replay tests/replays/box-4-chase.replay.json --browser page` |\n| `labs/box/scenes/crowd-1000.ts` | Box 4: the crowd's cost at 100, 1,000 and 5,000 agents, within budget. | `node x perf labs/box --scene crowd-1000 --ladder --budget` |\n| `labs/box/scenes/crowd-5000.ts` | Box 4: 5,000 bodies entering with no pipeline built; Box 6: the benchmark's crowd, within budget; its page within budget, drawn through a GPU crowd (WP 11.4), and against the instancing service. | `node x perf labs/box --scene crowd-5000 --ladder --budget`, `node x perf labs/box --scene crowd-5000 --budget`, `node x perf labs/box --scene crowd-5000 --feature feature:gpuCrowds` |\n| `labs/box/scenes/fight.ts` | Box 5: combat, its deaths, launches, telegraphs, effects and damage numbers drawn from the sim, its goldens the same with effects on and off; Box 6: its blows through the bodies' reactions (flinch, knockdown, get-up, death) and the hero's cape, which the ID pass sees. | `node x replay tests/replays/box-5-fight.replay.json --browser page` |\n| `labs/box/scenes/fight-1000.ts` | Box 6: the benchmark, the fight at 100, 1,000 and 5,000, within budget. | `node x perf labs/box --scene fight-1000 --ladder --budget` |\n| `labs/box/scenes/hall-props.ts`, every look | Box 6: every box look, and one of the engine's looks in each material style, renders on the hall with its props with no pipeline built after a warm-up, across every toggle, the knock replay's goldens unchanged (Looks, below); the engine's 98 looks each build nothing and keep the hash on the room (`tests/e2e/post.spec.ts`). Each test lists the scene and the looks it covered as its annotations (`looks`) in out/e2e/report.json. | `npm run e2e -- tests/e2e/box-look.spec.ts tests/e2e/parity.spec.ts` |\n| `labs/box/sounds/page.ts` | Phase 9: the box plays its sim events as sounds, spatialized and ducked, with torch ambience and a demo song; the fight replay's sound timeline hashes the same in Node and in Chromium. | `npm run e2e -- tests/e2e/box-audio.spec.ts` |\n| `labs/box/scenes/clips.ts` | Clip mode (Phase 8): the hero and the mannequin play any clip of the library's 1,218 through the clip layer, over the hero's own rig; the clip a setting names is the one `x anim show` prints, frame for frame; its replay's goldens are the same in Node and in Chromium, drawn or not (`node x replay tests/replays/box-8-clips.replay.json --browser page`). | `npm run e2e -- tests/e2e/box-clips.spec.ts` |\n| `labs/box/scenes/ragdoll.ts` | Ragdolls (WP 10.2): a blow from the front, from behind, a launch and a death hand four partners off to their ragdolls, joints as data on Rapier, and each gets up the way it lies (the dead one when the cycle stands it), its goldens the same in Node and in Chromium; `box.ragdoll.handOff` off, they fall through their reactions' timelines instead. | `node x replay tests/replays/ragdoll-falls.replay.json tests/replays/ragdoll-strike.replay.json --browser sim` |\n\nThe benchmark's budgets and the numbers they were measured from are in `tests/baselines/perf/box-fight-1000.json`\nand `tests/baselines/perf/box-crowd-5000.json`.\n\n## Scenes\n\n| Scene | What it shows | Covered by |\n|---|---|---|\n| `box:room` (`labs/box/scenes/room.ts`) | The room, `labs/box/levels/room.txt`: 16 × 12 m of flagstones in brick walls 3 m high, one low wall (0.75 m), a 2 × 2 m pillar, the hero's spawn and three numbered markers. Three crates move on fixed paths from the markers, no physics yet: along the low wall, round a circle, round the pillar. | `tests/e2e/box.spec.ts`, `tests/e2e/parity.spec.ts`, `tests/replays/box-1-room.replay.json`, `tests/replays/box-1-tuned.replay.json`, `labs/box/scenes/room.test.ts`, `tests/baselines/thumbs/box-room-iso.json` |\n| `box:room-hero` (`labs/box/scenes/room-hero.ts`) | The same room as a physics level, and the hero (`labs/box/cast/hero.ts`: the stress test's speeds and timings, 5 m/s, a 1.46 m jump, a 3.25 m dash) at the spawn, the player: he walks (WASD, a stick), jumps (Space) onto the low wall but not the walls, and dashes (Shift); his animator steps his body with the sim, drawn as the neutral humanoid. Every camera follows him, and the walls and the pillar before him cut away; first person hides his body but his hands. | `tests/e2e/box-hero.spec.ts`, `tests/e2e/parity.spec.ts`, `tests/replays/box-2-walk.replay.json`, `tests/replays/box-2-dash.replay.json`, `tests/replays/box-2-jump.replay.json`, `labs/box/scenes/room-hero.test.ts`, `labs/box/cast/hero.test.ts` |\n| `box:hall` (`labs/box/scenes/hall.ts`) | The hall, `labs/box/levels/hall.txt`, as a physics level: 64 × 44 m inside walls 3 m high, a grid of pillars, low walls, 30 brazier stands, two galleries 1 m up along the north wall with stairs rising to each, and the octagonal rune dais at the centre, 0.5 m up. The hero starts on the dais: he walks down its slopes and up them, climbs the stairs to the galleries, jumps onto the low walls; the walls and pillars before him cut away. Its floor is its bake (`labs/box/looks/hall-floor.ts`): flagstones, moss creeping from the walls' feet, contact shadows along them, and the rune circle glowing on the dais. | `tests/e2e/box-hall.spec.ts`, `tests/e2e/parity.spec.ts`, `tests/replays/box-3-climb.replay.json`, `tests/replays/box-3-dais.replay.json`, `labs/box/scenes/hall.test.ts`, `tests/baselines/thumbs/box-hall-iso.json` |\n| `box:hall-props` (`labs/box/scenes/hall-props.ts`) | The hall with the hero and its props, standing in Rapier and drawn through one instanced batch per prop part: a brazier's fire on each of the 30 stands, and 100 crates and barrels (10 to 300) on the prototype's seeded spots, every fifth crate stacked on the one before where both are crates. He pushes them by walking into them, and shoves (J, the left mouse button) every prop within 1.9 m in his arc, knocking it away, both hands thrust forward. | `tests/e2e/box-hall.spec.ts`, `tests/e2e/parity.spec.ts`, `tests/replays/box-3-knock.replay.json`, `labs/box/scenes/hall-props.test.ts` |\n| `box:crowd-1000` (`labs/box/scenes/crowd-1000.ts`) | The hall with its hero and a crowd of 1,000 (its presets for 100 and 5,000 are `labs/box/scenes/crowd-100.ts` and `labs/box/scenes/crowd-5000.ts`, at `?scene=crowd-100` and `?scene=crowd-5000`): walkers (`labs/box/cast/walker.ts`, capsules walking at 1.75 to 2.5 m/s), slimes (`labs/box/cast/slime.ts`, balls hopping up to 2.75 m) and wisps (`labs/box/cast/wisp.ts`, flyers hovering 1.25 m up), half, three in ten and two in ten, queued at the start on the hall's floor and entering 25 a step. They chase the hero along a flow field toward his tile, round the pillars and up the stairs when he climbs to a gallery; level with him the walkers wait on a ring 1.5 m round him and the slimes on one 2.1 m round him, and the wisps circle him 4.4 to 6.3 m out. Their bodies push each other apart in Rapier, and the hero's capsule shoves them aside (his `shoves: ['crowd']`): with 1,000 pressing round him at the stairs' foot he still climbs to the gallery (box-4-stairs). The page draws them through a crowd (instanced batches; while `feature:gpuCrowds` is on, a GPU crowd's: a draw call a batch, its instances culled against the view on the GPU, `gfx.featuresOff` turning it off), each posed at the detail its distance from the camera allows: walkers as the neutral humanoid in four builds, slimes as blobs with horns, ears or wings, wisps as floaters with their motes. | `tests/e2e/box-crowd.spec.ts`, `tests/e2e/parity.spec.ts`, `tests/replays/box-4-chase.replay.json`, `tests/replays/box-4-hop.replay.json`, `tests/replays/box-4-stairs.replay.json`, `labs/box/scenes/crowd-1000.test.ts`, `labs/box/cast/crowd.test.ts`, `tests/baselines/perf/box-crowd-1000.json` |\n| `box:fight` (`labs/box/scenes/fight.ts`) | Box 5: the hall, its hero with a sword (`HERO_FIGHT`, `labs/box/cast/hero.ts`) and a crowd of 36, mixed (its preset for 1,000 is `labs/box/scenes/fight-1000.ts`, at `?scene=fight-1000`), fighting. Attack (J, the left mouse button) runs his combo, a slash, a backslash and a spin, and out of a dash the thrust; skill (L, the right mouse button) fires a bolt (`labs/box/scenes/fight-hero.ts`). The walkers swing their fists, the slimes pounce and the wisps shoot (`WALKER_ATTACK`, `SLIME_ATTACK`, `WISP_ATTACK` in the cast's files; `labs/box/scenes/fight-foes.ts`), each telegraphing on the floor while it winds up, the walkers and slimes three at a time through his attack tokens. Blows land through the engine's `damage` (`labs/box/scenes/fight-rules.ts`): hit points, pushes, big hits throwing bodies up a little and killing ones throwing them high, corpses the crowd walks through, hit-stop, and the events the page draws effects and damage numbers from. Each blow goes through the body's reactions (the component `reactions`, Box 6): a walker flinches, a big blow knocks it down and it gets up the way it lies, acting on nothing meanwhile, and a killing one fells it; a foe's blow flinches the hero. He wears a cape (the component `secondary`), which the view swings and the ID pass names as his (actor#1/cape). | `tests/e2e/box-fight.spec.ts`, `tests/e2e/parity.spec.ts`, `tests/replays/box-5-fight.replay.json`, `tests/replays/box-5-precise.replay.json`, `labs/box/scenes/fight.test.ts` |\n| `box:clips` (`labs/box/scenes/clips.ts`) | Clip mode, the Mocap Lab's: the room, the hero at its spawn and the mannequin 1.5 m east of him (`body:mannequin` on `build:mannequin`, the figure the Quaternius clips were measured on), both playing the clip `box.clips.clip` names through the clip layer in their animators, the hero's retargeted to his build. He stays the player and walks under it; masked to his upper body (`box.clips.mask`), his legs keep their own walk. A new clip crossfades in from the pose on screen; a one-shot holds its end 0.8 s, then plays again; clips that travel play in place. The page loads the library first: every set under `data/anim/sets`, registered as a `clipset` (`__engine.describe('clipset')`); `node x sim`, `node x replay` and the sim-only page register it too. | `tests/e2e/box-clips.spec.ts`, `tests/e2e/parity.spec.ts`, `tests/replays/box-8-clips.replay.json`, `labs/box/scenes/clips.test.ts` |\n| `box:ragdoll` (`labs/box/scenes/ragdoll.ts`) | Ragdolls (WP 10.2): the room as a physics level, the hero at its spawn and four sparring partners on `build:adult` across its south half, each where it falls on open floor in view, facing him. Every 8 s a blow lands on each in turn: the first from the front (it falls onto its back), the second from behind (onto its face), the third a launch, up and to the south-east, the fourth a killing one; each falls as a ragdoll (engine/sim/ragdolls.ts: eleven capsules held by balls with a body's limits and hinges at the elbows and knees, faded onto the puppet) and gets up the way it lies once its trunk lies still, the dead one when the cycle stands it up at 6 s; at each cycle's start a partner standing is put back on its spot. His attack (J) knocks down the partner nearest in front of him, within 2.5 m. | `labs/box/scenes/ragdoll.test.ts`, `tests/replays/ragdoll-falls.replay.json`, `tests/replays/ragdoll-strike.replay.json`, `engine/sim/ragdolls.test.ts` |\n\nThe page draws each mover as a crate: an entity is drawn as a stand-in box when one of its components declares `x`\nand `z` in metres (engine/gfx/stage.ts), until it draws itself: actors with an animator are puppets from Box 2\n(engine/gfx/puppets/actors.ts), props a scene stands with `spawnProp` (engine/sim/props.ts) are drawn as their\nprops from Box 3 (engine/gfx/stageProps.ts), and crowd bodies (`crowdBody`, engine/sim/crowdBodies.ts) through a crowd\nwith its level of detail from Box 4 (engine/gfx/stageCrowd.ts).\n\n## Looks\n\nA look is how the page draws a scene, as data (`node x describe look`): the sky that lights it, a material style and a\nfilter chain; a look never changes play, so any scene can show any look. The box's own (`labs/box/looks/`) are the\ntorch-lit hall and the prototype's looks over it; the engine's 98 (`look:cartoon`, `look:game-boy`, the one-filter\npresets…) show in the box too. What is proved, on the hall with its props: every box look, and one engine look of each\nmaterial style, builds nothing after its warm-up and keeps the knock replay's goldens (`tests/e2e/box-look.spec.ts`,\n`tests/e2e/parity.spec.ts`); each of the engine's 98 does the same on the room (`tests/e2e/post.spec.ts`).\n\n| Look | What it draws |\n|---|---|\n| `look:torch-lit` (`labs/box/looks/torch-lit.ts`) | The torch-lit hall: the sky `sky:hall`, dark but for the torches (all 30 with tiled lighting, else the 12 nearest the hero), each flickering on its own, the nearest casting shadows, and fog from 12 m past him. |\n| `look:torch-toon` (`labs/box/looks/torch-toon.ts`) | Toon shading in it: three bands of light with a rim, the characters and objects inked. |\n| `look:torch-cel` (`labs/box/looks/torch-cel.ts`) | The prototype's comic cel in it: four flat bands, pushed colour, ink lines. |\n| `look:torch-pixel` (`labs/box/looks/torch-pixel.ts`) | The prototype's pixel look in it: 4 px blocks, 8 shades a channel, dithered. |\n| `look:torch-bloom` (`labs/box/looks/torch-bloom.ts`) | Bloom in it: the flames, coals, runes and sparks glow (off at the `low` tier). |\n| `look:torch-fxaa` (`labs/box/looks/torch-fxaa.ts`) | FXAA in it: every edge smoothed. |\n| `look:daylight` (`labs/box/looks/daylight.ts`) | A plain day: the sky `sky:daylight`, its sun casting through three cascades on a renderer with cascaded shadows; `tests/e2e/enhanced.spec.ts` draws it on the crowd arena. |\n\nSwitch with `?post.look=look:torch-toon` (`labs/box/?scene=fight&cam3=chase&post.look=look:torch-toon`), with\n`node x set post.look look:torch-toon` in an inspect session, or with `__engine.set('post.look', 'look:torch-toon')`;\n`look:clean` is the scene's own. The first switch to the torch-lit sky, or to a material style, warms up first (on\nSwiftShader, about a minute for the hall in a style under the sky; a GPU takes a moment); from then on a switch builds\nnothing. `quality` sets how many torches cast shadows: 2 at `high`, 1 at `medium`, none at `low`. A new look comes\nfrom `node x new look labs/box/looks/<name>`; the page imports every module under `labs/box/looks/`.\n\nThe chain's shading (WP 11.5: `ao`, `gi`, `air` and `ssr`, laid on any look with `post.filters`, as in\n`labs/box/?scene=room&post.filters={\"air\":{\"scope\":\"all\"}}`, or by the looks `look:sunbeams`, `look:lamplit-fog` and\nthe engine's air presets) is measured on the room by `tests/e2e/enhanced.spec.ts`. The box draws no metal, so its\nreflections show on `tests/pages/shading.html` instead.\n\n## Sound\n\nThe box sounds through its page (`labs/box/sounds/page.ts`, `window.__boxSound`): silent until the first key, click or\nend of a touch. It then plays the sim's events as sounds (`labs/box/sounds/events.ts`: footsteps by the surface\nunderfoot, landings, jumps and dashes, hits, bolts launched, pounces, and deaths that duck the music), placed where they\nhappen and muffled behind walls. The level sets the room's reverb, and the two torches nearest the camera crackle\n(`sfx:boxTorch`). The demo song is `song:boxHall` (`labs/box/sounds/boxHall.ts`); its drums and lead join while blows\nland. The effects are `labs/box/sounds/effects.ts`: `node x qa audio` checks them, and\n`node x audio sfx:boxHit --spectrogram` shows one. The fight replay's sound timeline hashes the same in Node and in\nChromium (`tests/e2e/box-audio.spec.ts`).\n\n## Settings\n\n| Setting | What it tunes |\n|---|---|\n| `box.room.speed` | How fast the movers go along their paths, m/s (1.5). Changes play: recorded in replays. |\n| `box.room.movers` | How many of the three movers run (3), when the scene starts. |\n| `box.roomHero.speed` | How fast the hero walks, m/s (5), when the scene starts. Changes play: recorded in replays. |\n| `box.roomHero.jump` | The hero's take-off speed, m/s (9.375: a 1.46 m apex under his 30 m/s² gravity), when the scene starts. |\n| `box.roomHero.dash` | The hero's dash speed, m/s (16.25, for 0.2 s; 0 turns it off), when the scene starts. |\n| `box.hall.speed` | How fast the hero walks in the hall, m/s (5), when the scene starts. Changes play: recorded in replays. |\n| `box.hall.jump` | The hero's take-off speed in the hall, m/s (9.375), when the scene starts: below about 7.75 m/s he no longer jumps onto the galleries, 1 m up, and climbs to them by the stairs alone. |\n| `box.hall.dash` | The hero's dash speed in the hall, m/s (16.25, for 0.2 s; 0 turns it off), when the scene starts. |\n| `box.hallProps.count` | How many crates and barrels stand in the hall with its props (100, 10 to 300), when the scene starts. Changes play: recorded in replays. |\n| `box.crowd.count` | How many walkers, slimes and wisps fill the hall with the crowd (1,000 in `box:crowd-1000`, 100 and 5,000 in its presets; 0 to 5,000), when the scene starts. Changes play: recorded in replays. |\n| `box.crowd.mix` | Who fills it: `mixed` (half walkers, three in ten slimes, two in ten wisps), `walkers`, `slimes` or `wisps`, when the scene starts. |\n| `box.fight.god` | Whether foes' blows only flinch and push the hero in the fight (true, as the prototype's proof ran) or also take his hit points (false: at none he rallies at once), when the scene starts. |\n| `box.fight.precise` | Whether the fight's hero is posed in the sim every step (his animator's precise hits), so his sword's trail is sim data in the hash (false by default; `tests/replays/box-5-precise.replay.json` plays it on), when the scene starts. |\n| `box.clips.clip` | The clip the figures play in clip mode, `<set>/<clip>` as `node x anim find cartwheel` lists them (the Quaternius set's Dance_Loop by default), or a name only one set has. Changes play: recorded in replays. |\n| `box.clips.speed` | The rate it plays at (1; 0 holds it). |\n| `box.clips.frame` | Frame stepping: the frame of its bake held, from 0, 30 a second (-1 plays). |\n| `box.clips.mirror` | Whether it plays mirrored (false). |\n| `box.clips.mask` | The joints it plays: `full`, or `upper` over the legs' own walk. |\n| `box.clips.cast` | Who plays it: `both`, `mannequin` or `hero`, when the scene starts. |\n| `box.clips.ik` | Whether the figures plant their feet and lift over the floor (true), when the scene starts. |\n| `box.ragdoll.handOff` | Whether a hard blow or a death hands a partner of `box:ragdoll` off to its ragdoll (true) or lets it fall through its reactions' timelines (false), when the scene starts. Changes play: recorded in replays. |\n| `box.ragdoll.push` | How hard `box:ragdoll`'s blows land, m/s along the blow (3.5), when the scene starts. |\n| `post.look` | The look drawn (`look:clean`, the scene's own; the box's looks above). A view setting: never in the hash. |\n| `quality` | The quality tier: `auto` (`high` on a desktop), `high`, `medium` or `low`: shadow casters, bloom, pixel caps. A view setting. |\n| `gfx.effects` | Whether the fight's effects draw (true): bolts, telegraphs, trails, bursts. A view setting. |\n| `gfx.resolution` | The resolution mode: `auto` (the default: the look's `resolution`, `pixels` for a look naming none, as every box look does), `pixels`, `balanced` or `full`. A view setting: never in the hash. |\n| `time.scale` | Sim seconds per real second (1). A view setting. |\n| `touch` | The touch controls: `auto`, `on` or `off`. A view setting (below). |\n| `box.menu` | The page's menu for humans (below): `auto` shows it unless automation drives the browser, `on` and `off` force it, when the page opens. A view setting. |\n\nSet one with `node x set box.room.speed 3`, as a URL parameter (`labs/box/?box.room.speed=3`), or with\n`__engine.set('box.room.speed', 3)`; `node x describe setting` lists them all.\n\n## The page\n\n`labs/box/` opens the room (at its own path, listed by the labs index; the site's landing page, `index.html`, opens\nthe playground). Its routes: `?scene=room`, `?seed=4`,\n`?cam=iso` (a camera code: `cam=topdown`, `cam=iso,45,2,persp`, `cam3=orbit`, `cam3=fly`; with the hero also\n`cam3=chase`, `cam3=first` and `cam3=rail`, which follow him), any setting by its path,\nand `?replay=box-1-room` (a replay played in real time; `?replay=box-2-jump` opens the hero's room, `?replay=box-3-climb`\nthe hall, `?replay=box-3-knock` the hall with its props, `?replay=box-4-chase` the hall with a crowd of 100, `?replay=box-5-fight` the fight, `?replay=box-8-clips` clip mode)\nand `?post.look=look:torch-lit` (a look, above). In the page,\n`window.__engine.help()` lists every member.\n\nThe page opens with its menu for humans (`labs/box/menu.ts`) in the top-left corner: every scene above as a link with\na one-line label, the replays, cameras (`cam3=chase`, `cam3=first`, `cam3=orbit`, `cam=iso`, `cam=topdown`) and looks\n(the box's, then `look:cartoon`, `look:game-boy` and a few more of the engine's) that keep the scene, and the\ncontrols, read from the action map the page's input binds (`actionMap:thirdPerson`: WASD or the arrows move, Space\njumps, Shift dashes, the left button or J attacks, the right button or L fires the bolt, E interacts), with the\nwheel's zoom and the first click or key that starts the sound. Its button or M shows and hides it; no action map binds\nM (`tests/e2e/box-menu.spec.ts`). The page remembers the last toggle in the browser: closed, the menu stays closed\nacross reloads and its own links, its button still in the corner, until it is opened again. A browser that automation drives (navigator.webdriver: every e2e spec and every `x`\ncommand that opens the page) gets none of it, so no test's screenshot holds it, and `__engine.shot` reads the GPU,\nnever the page; `?box.menu=on` shows it there.\n\n`?scene=clips` opens clip mode (`labs/box/?scene=clips&box.clips.clip=cmu/Cartwheel&cam=threequarter`); the page loads\nthe animation library for it and its replays alone. The page ships the clips, so it always shows 100STYLE's credit (CC BY 4.0,\n`data/anim/SOURCES.md`) in its corner.\n\nOn a phone or tablet the page shows the touch controls (`labs/box/touch.ts`, for every scene): a floating stick\nwherever the thumb lands, attack as the main button, and jump, dash and the bolt beside it. The menu is a page panel\nthere: it starts below its button and scrolls, the touch buttons hide while it is open, and a tap on the game closes\nit. Like the rest of the touch layer they are not tested (ADR-0021); `labs/box/?touch=on` shows them on a desktop.\n\n## The quick loop\n\n1. Change a setting or the scene, then run it headless: `node x sim labs/box/scenes/room --steps 600 --set box.room.speed=3`;\n   for the hero, `node x sim labs/box/scenes/room-hero --feel --set box.roomHero.speed=6` also prints how he handles.\n   `x sim` steps with no intents: its replay (`out/sim/box-<name>/run.replay.json`) has empty `inputs`, which you edit to\n   drive the hero (`[0, { \"move\": [0, 1] }]` walks him south, +Z; tests/replays/README.md, \"Coordinates and inputs\").\n2. See it as numbers: `node x shot labs/box --scene room --cam iso` (the ID pass and the look metrics; `--png` for\n   a picture, `--thumb box-room-iso` against the baseline); for the hall,\n   `node x shot labs/box --scene hall --cam iso --thumb box-hall-iso`; for the crowd,\n   `node x sim labs/box/scenes/crowd-100 --steps 600 --set box.crowd.mix=slimes`, and its cost at 100, 1,000 and\n   5,000, `node x perf labs/box --scene crowd-1000 --ladder`; for the fight,\n   `node x sim labs/box/scenes/fight --steps 600 --set box.fight.god=false`; in a look,\n   `node x shot labs/box --scene hall --cam iso --set post.look=look:torch-cel`; in clip mode,\n   `node x anim show Cartwheel` (the clip as text) and\n   `node x shot labs/box --scene clips --cam threequarter,0,5 --set box.clips.clip=cmu/Cartwheel --set box.clips.frame=30`.\n3. Prove play: `node x replay tests/replays/box-1-room.replay.json --browser page` (the goldens, in Node and in the\n   page while it renders); `node x replay tests/replays/box-2-jump.replay.json --browser page` for the hero,\n   `node x replay tests/replays/box-3-climb.replay.json --browser page` in the hall,\n   `node x replay tests/replays/box-4-chase.replay.json --browser page` with the crowd,\n   `node x replay tests/replays/box-5-fight.replay.json --browser page` in the fight,\n   `node x replay tests/replays/box-8-clips.replay.json --browser page` in clip mode, and with `--state` (or\n   `--until 300`) the state a run reaches, in out/replay/<name>/state.json: where the hero, the props and the\n   bodies ended, every component; the crowd's budgets,\n   `node x perf labs/box --scene crowd-1000 --ladder --budget`, and the benchmark's,\n   `node x perf labs/box --scene fight-1000 --ladder --budget` and\n   `node x perf labs/box --scene crowd-5000 --ladder --budget`.\n4. Keep a page open while iterating: `node x inspect --scene room`, then `node x eval \"__engine.hash()\"`,\n   `node x set box.room.speed 3`, `node x dump --step 60 --filter pathMover` and `node x shot labs/box --scene room`\n   (it reuses the session); `node x inspect --stop` ends it.\n5. Commit with the suites green: `npm run e2e -- tests/e2e/box.spec.ts tests/e2e/parity.spec.ts`, and for the hall\n   `npm run e2e -- tests/e2e/box-hall.spec.ts`, for the crowd `npm run e2e -- tests/e2e/box-crowd.spec.ts`, for the\n   fight `npm run e2e -- tests/e2e/box-fight.spec.ts`, for the looks `npm run e2e -- tests/e2e/box-look.spec.ts`, for\n   clip mode `npm run e2e -- tests/e2e/box-clips.spec.ts`.\n\n## Adding a scene or a variant\n\nA variant is a new scene file or a settings preset, never a change of meaning in a passing scene (PLAN.md §9.0).\n`node x new scene labs/box/scenes/<name>` writes a box scene with its replay test, which passes its checks; the page\nimports every module under `labs/box/scenes/`, so it opens at `labs/box/?scene=<name>`. Then keep a replay of it, the\nsequence `tests/e2e/parity.spec.ts` runs on a new scene:\n\n1. `node x sim labs/box/scenes/<name> --steps 600` writes the run's replay beside its report, with no intents.\n2. Copy `out/sim/box-<name>/run.replay.json` to `tests/replays/box-<stage>-<name>.replay.json`. `<stage>` is the\n   stage the scene proves; a variant outside every stage's claims takes the newest stage's number (the highest\n   `box-<n>-` among tests/replays/) and stays out of `STAGES`. Edit its `inputs` to drive it before you record (tests/replays/README.md,\n   \"Coordinates and inputs\": `move` is world [x, z], +X east, +Z south); `node x replay <file> --state` then shows\n   where the run ends.\n3. `node x replay <file> --browser sim --update` records its goldens, which hold in Node and in Chromium.\n4. `node x replay <file> --browser page` checks them while the page renders.\n5. List the scene and the replay here, with what it shows, what covers it and the settings that tune it (the demo\n   index and the settings table: `tests/unit/box-readme.test.ts` fails a scene or a `box.*` setting left out).\n6. When it belongs to a stage, add it to `STAGES` in `tests/e2e/parity-stages.ts`: T2's rendering-page check plays\n   only the replays named there.\n\n## Adding a prop\n\n`labs/box/scenes/hall-props.ts` is the worked example. A prop is data (engine/world/props: its parts, its body, where\na level places it):\n\n1. `node x new prop labs/box/props/<name>` writes `prop:<name>` and its test (its parts build clean and stand as tall\n   as its body), which pass their checks; `node x qa geo tex --only prop:<name>` checks its parts and textures and\n   counts what it checked (a prefix that keeps nothing is a usage error naming the closest ids).\n2. Import it from the scene that shows it (`import '../props/<name>';`): the page reaches labs/box/props/ only\n   through the scenes it imports, and QA through its own import of every module there.\n3. The scene needs a physics world and floors to stand on: `physics: true`, then in `setup`\n   `addLevelBodies(physicsOf(w), <compiled level>)` (the template's `level: 'level:room'` has none: the page draws\n   the room, but nothing in it is solid; `labs/box/scenes/room-hero.ts` exports the room compiled as\n   `ROOM_HERO_LEVEL`, `labs/box/scenes/hall.ts` the hall as `HALL_LEVEL`).\n4. Stand it: `spawnProp(w, { prop: 'prop:<name>', at: [x, y, z], yaw })`, its base at `at` (m), turned `yaw` (rad)\n   about +Y; it returns the entity, whose `sceneProp` component the sim hashes and the view draws as the prop.\n5. Or let the level place it: give the prop `place: { spawn: '<spot>' }` and the level a glyph with that spawn\n   (`defineGlyph('glyph:<spot>', { char, description, mesh: 'floor', spawn: '<spot>' })` in the scene module, before\n   the level compiles), then `for (const placement of levelProps(<compiled level>)) spawnProp(w, placement);`. The\n   digits are the engine's own spawns (`3` places at `spawn:3`).\n\nTile (col, row) of a level has its centre at x = (col + 0.5) × tile, z = (row + 0.5) × tile (1 m tiles in the box),\nrows running +Z (south), as tests/replays/README.md says.\n\nThe `stress-box` skill (`.claude/skills/stress-box/SKILL.md`) says the rest.\n","numLines":255,"startLine":1,"totalLines":255}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01BQaAMo81LWeaKSmK8ZktFw","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
