{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HiXvBNxPPSLmudGHDibW2P","type":"tool_result","content":"/**\n * @file The intents vocabulary (PLAN.md §6.4, §6.5 item 3, §8.4, WP 1.5; doctrine: Reproducible): everything the sim\n * reads from outside arrives once per step as plain data, recorded by replays. `move` is a world-space direction\n * `[x, z]` (`fromCamera` turns a stick or keys into one, so W walks away from the camera), `cam` the camera heading,\n * `aim` a world-space aim point, `look` a view direction, `b` the buttons held and `p` the buttons pressed this step,\n * and game code adds its own keys, namespaced (`'game:charge'`). Devices (WP 3.3) make intents; the sim only reads them.\n *\n * Invariants: `normalizeIntents` checks every key and value (an unknown key names the closest; numbers are finite;\n * custom values are plain data) and returns a frozen object with keys in a fixed order, buttons sorted and unique, and\n * absent or empty entries left out. `p` is the union of the presses given and the edges of `b` (held now, not held the\n * step before), so a press is never lost and a hold presses once; when one frame runs several steps, the frame loop\n * passes its taps to the first step only (§6.4). `diffIntents` and `applyIntents` are the replay encoding (§8.4): held\n * state repeats until a change-point changes it (`null` clears a key), `p` belongs to its step and is written only for\n * presses the edges of `b` do not explain, so `applyIntents(prev, diffIntents(prev, next))` is `next` again. `-0` is\n * kept (`Object.is`), since replays must give the sim the very bits live play gave it.\n *\n * `cam` is the yaw of the camera's horizontal view direction, forward(ψ) = (sin ψ, 0, cos ψ) (§6.3), not three.js's\n * `camera.rotation.y`, which is ψ − π since a camera looks down its −Z.\n *\n * Edges, buffering and `consume` in sim time (WP 3.3): an `InputBuffer` is what a body remembers of its buttons across\n * steps, plain data in a component field, so the world hashes, captures and restores it. `updateInputBuffer(buffer,\n * intents, w.tick)` runs once per step (a system in the phase `intents`); then `released` says a button went up this\n * step (a tap shorter than a step is pressed and released on the same one), `buffered` that it was pressed within the\n * last `BUFFER_STEPS` steps and not yet used up by `consume` (a jump pressed just before landing still jumps), and\n * `repeated` that a held button repeats, as a menu cursor does. Carried from `my-3d2dge:engine/my-3d2dge.js:564-583`\n * (`released`, `repeat`, `buffered`, `consume`, `consumeAll`), counted in steps instead of seconds.\n *\n * @example\n * const step1 = normalizeIntents({ move: fromCamera(Math.PI / 2, [0, 1]), b: ['jump'] }); // move ≈ [1, 0]: +X\n * pressed(step1, 'jump'); // true: an edge of b\n * const step2 = normalizeIntents({ move: step1.move, b: ['jump'] }, step1);\n * [held(step2, 'jump'), pressed(step2, 'jump')]; // [true, false]\n * diffIntents(step1, normalizeIntents({}, step1)); // { b: null, move: null }\n * const buffer = updateInputBuffer(createInputBuffer(), step1, 1);\n * buffered(buffer, 'jump'); // true for 9 steps, or until consume(buffer, 'jump')\n * @see engine/input/intents.test.ts\n * @see engine/input/buffer.test.ts\n */\nimport { codeError, defineCodes, didYouMean } from '../core/log';\nimport { isPlainObject, show } from '../core/schema';\n\n/** The codes this module raises, with their fixes. */\nexport const INTENT_CODES = defineCodes('input', {\n  INPUT_BAD_INTENTS: {\n    template: '{where}: {problems}',\n    fix: 'give intents as { move: [x, z], cam, aim: [x, y, z], look: [yaw, pitch], b: [held buttons], p: [pressed buttons] } with finite numbers, plus custom keys namespaced \"game:key\" holding plain data (engine/input/intents.ts); null or a missing key means not given',\n    doc: 'Raised by `normalizeIntents`, `applyIntents` and the replay checks (engine/input/intents.ts, engine/sim/replay.ts) for an unknown key (named with the closest), a non-finite or misshapen number, a button that is not a non-empty string, or a custom value that is not plain data. Every problem is listed at once.',\n  },\n});\n\n/** A custom intent's value: plain data, as a replay file holds it. */\nexport type IntentValue = number | string | boolean | readonly IntentValue[] | { readonly [key: string]: IntentValue };\n\n/** A namespaced key for game code's own intents: `'game:charge'`. */\nexport type CustomIntentKey = `${string}:${string}`;\n\n/** One step's intents, as the sim reads them (systems get them as their second argument). */\nexport type Intents = {\n  /** The direction to move in, world space `[x, z]`, length 1 at most from `fromCamera`. */\n  readonly move?: readonly [number, number];\n  /** The camera heading: the yaw of its horizontal view direction, rad (see the file comment). */\n  readonly cam?: number;\n  /** The point aimed at, world space `[x, y, z]`, m. */\n  readonly aim?: readonly [number, number, number];\n  /** The view direction `[yaw, pitch]`, rad (first-person look). */\n  readonly look?: readonly [number, number];\n  /** The buttons held this step, sorted. */\n  readonly b?: readonly string[];\n  /** The buttons pressed this step (edges of `b` plus taps released within the step), sorted. */\n  readonly p?: readonly string[];\n} & { readonly [key: CustomIntentKey]: IntentValue | undefined };\n\n/** A replay change-point's intent part: the keys that changed, `null` for a key cleared, `p` for unexplained presses. */\nexport type IntentChanges = { -readonly [K in keyof Intents]?: Intents[K] | null };\n\n/** The built-in keys, in the order a normalized object holds them, each with what it means. */\nexport const INTENT_KEYS = {\n  move: 'the direction to move in, world space [x, z]',\n  cam: 'the camera heading (yaw of its view direction), rad',\n  aim: 'the point aimed at, world space [x, y, z], m',\n  look: 'the view direction [yaw, pitch], rad',\n  b: 'the buttons held, sorted',\n  p: 'the buttons pressed this step, sorted',\n} as const;\n\n/** A built-in key. */\nexport type IntentKey = keyof typeof INTENT_KEYS;\n\n/** No intents: what a step gets when nothing is given. */\nexport const NO_INTENTS: Intents = Object.freeze({});\n\n/** A namespaced key: a lower-case word, a colon, a name. */\nconst CUSTOM = /^[a-z][A-Za-z0-9]*:[A-Za-z0-9_.-]+$/;\n\n/** The namespaced key a bad one most likely means: `'Game:x'` → `'game:x'`, `'charge'` → `'game:charge'`. */\nfunction customKey(key: string): string {\n  const at = key.indexOf(':');\n  const space = (at < 0 ? '' : key.slice(0, at)).replace(/[^A-Za-z0-9]/g, '').replace(/^[^A-Za-z]+/, '');\n  const name = (at < 0 ? key : key.slice(at + 1)).replace(/[^A-Za-z0-9_.-]/g, '');\n  return `${space ? space[0].toLowerCase() + space.slice(1) : 'game'}:${name || 'key'}`;\n}\n\n/** How many numbers each vector key holds. */\nconst VECTORS: Partial<Record<IntentKey, number>> = { move: 2, aim: 3, look: 2 };\n/** Code-unit order, so sorting never depends on the locale. */\nconst byText = (a: string, b: string) => (a < b ? -1 : a > b ? 1 : 0);\n/** Deepest nesting a custom value may have. */\nconst MAX_DEPTH = 32;\n\n/** A frozen copy of plain data, or a problem pushed for the first value that is not. */\n-------\n/**\n * @file Action maps and presets (PLAN.md WP 3.3, I-24; doctrine: Common ground): the registry kind `actionMap`, a set\n * of named actions with the physical codes bound to each (engine/input/codes.ts), as Unity's action maps and Godot's\n * InputMap hold them; the presets; and the system layer, which no player rebinds.\n *\n * An action is a button the sim reads: held actions arrive as the intents' `b`, pressed ones as `p`\n * (engine/input/intents.ts). The four actions a map names in `move` (forward, back, left, right) are not buttons:\n * their strengths make the move axes `[right − left, forward − back]`, so keys walk at full speed and a half-pushed\n * stick at half, and `fromCamera` turns the axes into a world direction. `values` writes an action's analog strength\n * (a trigger) as a custom intent. `look: true` (first person, the shooter) adds the camera's view direction as `look`,\n * `aimWith` names the rule that gives the intents' `aim` its point (engine/input/aim.ts: the screen centre's ray, the\n * pointer's onto the floor, or none; the action `aim`, where a map has one, raises the sights), and `lock: true` takes\n * the pointer lock on a click so the mouse turns the view (with the cursor free, it points and aims). The actions a\n * map names in `view` (a camera switch, a view's turn) are the page's: bound and rebound like the others, never\n * buttons in the intents (`createEngine({ onView })`). A game with several camera modes gives each its own map\n * (`createEngine({ actionMap })`, WP 13.9).\n *\n * The system layer (`SYSTEM_ACTIONS`): pause, and the menu's accept, cancel and directions. It is always active\n * beside the map, never rebound, and never part of the intents: the app and the UI read it (`input.pressed('pause')`),\n * so remapping movement never breaks a menu (the lesson of `my-3d2dge:docs/CONTROLS-AUDIT.md`). `RESERVED_CODES` (the\n * pause buttons, and keys the browser or system keeps) and a map's own `reserved` codes are refused by rebinding.\n *\n * Invariants (`CORE_BAD_SPEC` when broken): every code is valid (`isCode`), action names are lower-case words\n * (`jump`, `skill2`) and none is a system action, `move` names four actions of the map and `view` others, `values` keys\n * are namespaced custom intents naming actions of the map, and no action binds a reserved code. The presets are registered on the\n * shared registry when this module loads.\n *\n * Carried from `my-3d2dge:engine/my-3d2dge.js:670-693` (`Input.DEFAULT`, `PLATFORMER`, `SHMUP`, `MENU_KEYS`) with 3D\n * movement, and shardfall's layer that is never rebound (`shardfall:crates/pav_app/src/input.rs:131-161`).\n *\n * @example\n * const map = getActionMap('actionMap:thirdPerson');\n * map.actions.jump; // ['Space', 'PadSouth']\n * map.move; // ['forward', 'back', 'left', 'right']\n * SYSTEM_ACTIONS.pause; // ['Escape', 'PadStart']\n * listActionMaps().map((entry) => entry.id); // ['actionMap:firstPerson', 'actionMap:platformer', …]\n * @see engine/input/bindings.test.ts\n */\nimport { registry as sharedRegistry, type Entry, type Registry } from '../core/registry';\nimport { show, type Schema } from '../core/schema';\nimport { AIM_RULES, type AimRule } from './aim';\nimport { isCode } from './codes';\n\n/** The system layer: action → codes. Always active, never rebound, never in the intents. */\nexport const SYSTEM_ACTIONS: Readonly<Record<string, readonly string[]>> = Object.freeze({\n  pause: ['Escape', 'PadStart'],\n  uiAccept: ['Enter', 'NumpadEnter', 'Space', 'PadSouth'],\n  uiCancel: ['Escape', 'Backspace', 'PadEast'],\n  uiUp: ['ArrowUp', 'PadUp', 'PadLeftStickUp'],\n  uiDown: ['ArrowDown', 'PadDown', 'PadLeftStickDown'],\n  uiLeft: ['ArrowLeft', 'PadLeft', 'PadLeftStickLeft'],\n  uiRight: ['ArrowRight', 'PadRight', 'PadLeftStickRight'],\n});\n\n/** Codes no action map binds: the pause buttons, and keys the browser or the system keeps. */\nexport const RESERVED_CODES: readonly string[] = Object.freeze([\n  'Escape',\n  'PadStart',\n  'PadHome',\n  'F5',\n  'F11',\n  'F12',\n  'MetaLeft',\n  'MetaRight',\n]);\n\n/** The fields of an `actionMap` entry. */\nconst ACTION_MAP_FIELDS = {\n  description: { type: 'string', default: '', description: 'What the map is for, in plain words.' },\n  actions: {\n    type: 'object',\n    required: true,\n    description:\n      'Action name → the codes bound to it (KeyboardEvent.code, MouseLeft…, PadSouth…, PadLeftStickUp…): held actions are the intents b, pressed ones p.',\n  },\n  move: {\n    type: 'array',\n    items: { type: 'string' },\n    default: ['forward', 'back', 'left', 'right'],\n    description: 'The four actions that walk, as forward, back, left, right: their strengths make the move axes.',\n  },\n  values: {\n    type: 'object',\n    default: {},\n    description:\n      'Custom intent key (\"game:throttle\") → action: its analog strength (0 to 1, a trigger) is that intent.',\n  },\n  look: {\n    type: 'boolean',\n    default: false,\n    description: \"True for first person and the shooter: the intents carry look = [the camera's yaw, its pitch].\",\n  },\n  aimWith: {\n    type: 'string',\n    enum: AIM_RULES,\n    default: 'none',\n    description:\n      \"What the intents' aim holds: none; centre, the point the screen centre's ray meets (first person, the shooter); pointer, the pointer's ray onto the player's floor or a right stick's push (isometric, top-down).\",\n  },\n  lock: {\n    type: 'boolean',\n    default: false,\n    description:\n      'True when the mouse turns the view: a click on the game takes the pointer lock, which pause and Escape give back.',\n  },\n  view: {\n    type: 'array',\n    items: { type: 'string' },\n    default: [],\n    description:\n      \"Actions the page reads for its view (a camera switch, a view's turn): bound and rebound like the others, never buttons in the intents.\",\n  },\n  reserved: {\n    type: 'array',\n    items: { type: 'string' },\n    default: [],\n    description: 'Codes the game keeps for its own hotkeys: rebinding refuses them, as it refuses RESERVED_CODES.',\n  },\n} as const satisfies Schema;\n\n/** An action map entry. */\nexport type ActionMap = Entry & {\n  readonly description: string;\n  readonly actions: Readonly<Record<string, readonly string[]>>;\n  readonly move: readonly string[];\n  readonly values: Readonly<Record<string, string>>;\n  readonly look: boolean;\n  readonly aimWith: AimRule;\n  readonly lock: boolean;\n  readonly view: readonly string[];\n  readonly reserved: readonly string[];\n};\n\n/** An action name: a lower-case word, letters and digits. */\nconst ACTION = /^[a-z][A-Za-z0-9]*$/;\n\n/** The problems of a map beyond its fields (the file comment lists them). */\nfunction mapProblems(map: ActionMap): string[] {\n  const problems: string[] = [];\n  const reserved = new Set([...RESERVED_CODES, ...map.reserved]);\n  for (const [action, codes] of Object.entries(map.actions)) {\n    if (!ACTION.test(action)) problems.push(`the action ${show(action)} must be a lower-case word (jump, skill2)`);\n    if (Object.hasOwn(SYSTEM_ACTIONS, action)) problems.push(`${action} is a system action, never rebound: rename it`);\n    if (!Array.isArray(codes)) {\n      problems.push(`actions.${action} is ${show(codes)}; it must be a list of codes`);\n      continue;\n    }\n    for (const code of codes) {\n      if (!isCode(code)) problems.push(`actions.${action} holds ${show(code)}, not a code (KeyW, MouseLeft, PadSouth)`);\n      else if (reserved.has(code)) problems.push(`actions.${action} binds the reserved code ${code}`);\n    }\n  }\n  if (map.move.length !== 4) problems.push(`move names ${map.move.length} actions: give forward, back, left, right`);\n  for (const action of map.move) {\n    if (!Object.hasOwn(map.actions, action)) problems.push(`move names ${show(action)}, which actions lacks`);\n  }\n  for (const action of map.view) {\n    if (!Object.hasOwn(map.actions, action)) problems.push(`view names ${show(action)}, which actions lacks`);\n    else if (map.move.includes(action)) problems.push(`view names ${action}, a move action`);\n  }\n  for (const [key, action] of Object.entries(map.values)) {\n    if (!/^[a-z][A-Za-z0-9]*:[A-Za-z0-9_.-]+$/.test(key)) problems.push(`values key ${show(key)} must be \"game:name\"`);\n    if (typeof action !== 'string' || !Object.hasOwn(map.actions, action)) {\n      problems.push(`values.${key} names ${show(action)}, which actions lacks`);\n    }\n  }\n  for (const code of map.reserved) if (!isCode(code)) problems.push(`reserved holds ${show(code)}, not a code`);\n  return problems;\n}\n\n/** Declares the kind `actionMap` on `registry` unless it has it. */\nexport function actionMapKind(registry: Registry = sharedRegistry): void {\n  if (registry.kinds().includes('actionMap')) return;\n  registry.defineKind('actionMap', {\n    description:\n      'Named actions and the physical codes bound to each (keys by KeyboardEvent.code, mouse, pad by position): what the input devices turn into intents.',\n    fields: ACTION_MAP_FIELDS,\n    defineWith: \"defineActionMap('actionMap:<name>', { actions: { jump: ['Space', 'PadSouth'] } })\",\n    check: (entry) => mapProblems(entry as ActionMap),\n  });\n}\n\n/** How an action map is written. */\nexport interface ActionMapSpec {\n  description?: string;\n  actions: Readonly<Record<string, readonly string[]>>;\n  move?: readonly [string, string, string, string];\n  values?: Readonly<Record<string, string>>;\n  look?: boolean;\n  aimWith?: AimRule;\n  lock?: boolean;\n  view?: readonly string[];\n  reserved?: readonly string[];\n}\n\n/** Registers an action map (on the shared registry by default). Throws `CORE_BAD_SPEC` naming each problem. */\nexport function defineActionMap(id: string, spec: ActionMapSpec, registry: Registry = sharedRegistry): ActionMap {\n  actionMapKind(registry);\n  return registry.def('actionMap', id, spec as unknown as Record<string, unknown>) as ActionMap;\n}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b0d0401-1a79-4c2f-8a33-ba9239fdbfed","uuid":"59019afd-894f-4159-9fec-9c1d0fded83f","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:23:29.980Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"/**\n * @file The intents vocabulary (PLAN.md §6.4, §6.5 item 3, §8.4, WP 1.5; doctrine: Reproducible): everything the sim\n * reads from outside arrives once per step as plain data, recorded by replays. `move` is a world-space direction\n * `[x, z]` (`fromCamera` turns a stick or keys into one, so W walks away from the camera), `cam` the camera heading,\n * `aim` a world-space aim point, `look` a view direction, `b` the buttons held and `p` the buttons pressed this step,\n * and game code adds its own keys, namespaced (`'game:charge'`). Devices (WP 3.3) make intents; the sim only reads them.\n *\n * Invariants: `normalizeIntents` checks every key and value (an unknown key names the closest; numbers are finite;\n * custom values are plain data) and returns a frozen object with keys in a fixed order, buttons sorted and unique, and\n * absent or empty entries left out. `p` is the union of the presses given and the edges of `b` (held now, not held the\n * step before), so a press is never lost and a hold presses once; when one frame runs several steps, the frame loop\n * passes its taps to the first step only (§6.4). `diffIntents` and `applyIntents` are the replay encoding (§8.4): held\n * state repeats until a change-point changes it (`null` clears a key), `p` belongs to its step and is written only for\n * presses the edges of `b` do not explain, so `applyIntents(prev, diffIntents(prev, next))` is `next` again. `-0` is\n * kept (`Object.is`), since replays must give the sim the very bits live play gave it.\n *\n * `cam` is the yaw of the camera's horizontal view direction, forward(ψ) = (sin ψ, 0, cos ψ) (§6.3), not three.js's\n * `camera.rotation.y`, which is ψ − π since a camera looks down its −Z.\n *\n * Edges, buffering and `consume` in sim time (WP 3.3): an `InputBuffer` is what a body remembers of its buttons across\n * steps, plain data in a component field, so the world hashes, captures and restores it. `updateInputBuffer(buffer,\n * intents, w.tick)` runs once per step (a system in the phase `intents`); then `released` says a button went up this\n * step (a tap shorter than a step is pressed and released on the same one), `buffered` that it was pressed within the\n * last `BUFFER_STEPS` steps and not yet used up by `consume` (a jump pressed just before landing still jumps), and\n * `repeated` that a held button repeats, as a menu cursor does. Carried from `my-3d2dge:engine/my-3d2dge.js:564-583`\n * (`released`, `repeat`, `buffered`, `consume`, `consumeAll`), counted in steps instead of seconds.\n *\n * @example\n * const step1 = normalizeIntents({ move: fromCamera(Math.PI / 2, [0, 1]), b: ['jump'] }); // move ≈ [1, 0]: +X\n * pressed(step1, 'jump'); // true: an edge of b\n * const step2 = normalizeIntents({ move: step1.move, b: ['jump'] }, step1);\n * [held(step2, 'jump'), pressed(step2, 'jump')]; // [true, false]\n * diffIntents(step1, normalizeIntents({}, step1)); // { b: null, move: null }\n * const buffer = updateInputBuffer(createInputBuffer(), step1, 1);\n * buffered(buffer, 'jump'); // true for 9 steps, or until consume(buffer, 'jump')\n * @see engine/input/intents.test.ts\n * @see engine/input/buffer.test.ts\n */\nimport { codeError, defineCodes, didYouMean } from '../core/log';\nimport { isPlainObject, show } from '../core/schema';\n\n/** The codes this module raises, with their fixes. */\nexport const INTENT_CODES = defineCodes('input', {\n  INPUT_BAD_INTENTS: {\n    template: '{where}: {problems}',\n    fix: 'give intents as { move: [x, z], cam, aim: [x, y, z], look: [yaw, pitch], b: [held buttons], p: [pressed buttons] } with finite numbers, plus custom keys namespaced \"game:key\" holding plain data (engine/input/intents.ts); null or a missing key means not given',\n    doc: 'Raised by `normalizeIntents`, `applyIntents` and the replay checks (engine/input/intents.ts, engine/sim/replay.ts) for an unknown key (named with the closest), a non-finite or misshapen number, a button that is not a non-empty string, or a custom value that is not plain data. Every problem is listed at once.',\n  },\n});\n\n/** A custom intent's value: plain data, as a replay file holds it. */\nexport type IntentValue = number | string | boolean | readonly IntentValue[] | { readonly [key: string]: IntentValue };\n\n/** A namespaced key for game code's own intents: `'game:charge'`. */\nexport type CustomIntentKey = `${string}:${string}`;\n\n/** One step's intents, as the sim reads them (systems get them as their second argument). */\nexport type Intents = {\n  /** The direction to move in, world space `[x, z]`, length 1 at most from `fromCamera`. */\n  readonly move?: readonly [number, number];\n  /** The camera heading: the yaw of its horizontal view direction, rad (see the file comment). */\n  readonly cam?: number;\n  /** The point aimed at, world space `[x, y, z]`, m. */\n  readonly aim?: readonly [number, number, number];\n  /** The view direction `[yaw, pitch]`, rad (first-person look). */\n  readonly look?: readonly [number, number];\n  /** The buttons held this step, sorted. */\n  readonly b?: readonly string[];\n  /** The buttons pressed this step (edges of `b` plus taps released within the step), sorted. */\n  readonly p?: readonly string[];\n} & { readonly [key: CustomIntentKey]: IntentValue | undefined };\n\n/** A replay change-point's intent part: the keys that changed, `null` for a key cleared, `p` for unexplained presses. */\nexport type IntentChanges = { -readonly [K in keyof Intents]?: Intents[K] | null };\n\n/** The built-in keys, in the order a normalized object holds them, each with what it means. */\nexport const INTENT_KEYS = {\n  move: 'the direction to move in, world space [x, z]',\n  cam: 'the camera heading (yaw of its view direction), rad',\n  aim: 'the point aimed at, world space [x, y, z], m',\n  look: 'the view direction [yaw, pitch], rad',\n  b: 'the buttons held, sorted',\n  p: 'the buttons pressed this step, sorted',\n} as const;\n\n/** A built-in key. */\nexport type IntentKey = keyof typeof INTENT_KEYS;\n\n/** No intents: what a step gets when nothing is given. */\nexport const NO_INTENTS: Intents = Object.freeze({});\n\n/** A namespaced key: a lower-case word, a colon, a name. */\nconst CUSTOM = /^[a-z][A-Za-z0-9]*:[A-Za-z0-9_.-]+$/;\n\n/** The namespaced key a bad one most likely means: `'Game:x'` → `'game:x'`, `'charge'` → `'game:charge'`. */\nfunction customKey(key: string): string {\n  const at = key.indexOf(':');\n  const space = (at < 0 ? '' : key.slice(0, at)).replace(/[^A-Za-z0-9]/g, '').replace(/^[^A-Za-z]+/, '');\n  const name = (at < 0 ? key : key.slice(at + 1)).replace(/[^A-Za-z0-9_.-]/g, '');\n  return `${space ? space[0].toLowerCase() + space.slice(1) : 'game'}:${name || 'key'}`;\n}\n\n/** How many numbers each vector key holds. */\nconst VECTORS: Partial<Record<IntentKey, number>> = { move: 2, aim: 3, look: 2 };\n/** Code-unit order, so sorting never depends on the locale. */\nconst byText = (a: string, b: string) => (a < b ? -1 : a > b ? 1 : 0);\n/** Deepest nesting a custom value may have. */\nconst MAX_DEPTH = 32;\n\n/** A frozen copy of plain data, or a problem pushed for the first value that is not. */\n-------\n/**\n * @file Action maps and presets (PLAN.md WP 3.3, I-24; doctrine: Common ground): the registry kind `actionMap`, a set\n * of named actions with the physical codes bound to each (engine/input/codes.ts), as Unity's action maps and Godot's\n * InputMap hold them; the presets; and the system layer, which no player rebinds.\n *\n * An action is a button the sim reads: held actions arrive as the intents' `b`, pressed ones as `p`\n * (engine/input/intents.ts). The four actions a map names in `move` (forward, back, left, right) are not buttons:\n * their strengths make the move axes `[right − left, forward − back]`, so keys walk at full speed and a half-pushed\n * stick at half, and `fromCamera` turns the axes into a world direction. `values` writes an action's analog strength\n * (a trigger) as a custom intent. `look: true` (first person, the shooter) adds the camera's view direction as `look`,\n * `aimWith` names the rule that gives the intents' `aim` its point (engine/input/aim.ts: the screen centre's ray, the\n * pointer's onto the floor, or none; the action `aim`, where a map has one, raises the sights), and `lock: true` takes\n * the pointer lock on a click so the mouse turns the view (with the cursor free, it points and aims). The actions a\n * map names in `view` (a camera switch, a view's turn) are the page's: bound and rebound like the others, never\n * buttons in the intents (`createEngine({ onView })`). A game with several camera modes gives each its own map\n * (`createEngine({ actionMap })`, WP 13.9).\n *\n * The system layer (`SYSTEM_ACTIONS`): pause, and the menu's accept, cancel and directions. It is always active\n * beside the map, never rebound, and never part of the intents: the app and the UI read it (`input.pressed('pause')`),\n * so remapping movement never breaks a menu (the lesson of `my-3d2dge:docs/CONTROLS-AUDIT.md`). `RESERVED_CODES` (the\n * pause buttons, and keys the browser or system keeps) and a map's own `reserved` codes are refused by rebinding.\n *\n * Invariants (`CORE_BAD_SPEC` when broken): every code is valid (`isCode`), action names are lower-case words\n * (`jump`, `skill2`) and none is a system action, `move` names four actions of the map and `view` others, `values` keys\n * are namespaced custom intents naming actions of the map, and no action binds a reserved code. The presets are registered on the\n * shared registry when this module loads.\n *\n * Carried from `my-3d2dge:engine/my-3d2dge.js:670-693` (`Input.DEFAULT`, `PLATFORMER`, `SHMUP`, `MENU_KEYS`) with 3D\n * movement, and shardfall's layer that is never rebound (`shardfall:crates/pav_app/src/input.rs:131-161`).\n *\n * @example\n * const map = getActionMap('actionMap:thirdPerson');\n * map.actions.jump; // ['Space', 'PadSouth']\n * map.move; // ['forward', 'back', 'left', 'right']\n * SYSTEM_ACTIONS.pause; // ['Escape', 'PadStart']\n * listActionMaps().map((entry) => entry.id); // ['actionMap:firstPerson', 'actionMap:platformer', …]\n * @see engine/input/bindings.test.ts\n */\nimport { registry as sharedRegistry, type Entry, type Registry } from '../core/registry';\nimport { show, type Schema } from '../core/schema';\nimport { AIM_RULES, type AimRule } from './aim';\nimport { isCode } from './codes';\n\n/** The system layer: action → codes. Always active, never rebound, never in the intents. */\nexport const SYSTEM_ACTIONS: Readonly<Record<string, readonly string[]>> = Object.freeze({\n  pause: ['Escape', 'PadStart'],\n  uiAccept: ['Enter', 'NumpadEnter', 'Space', 'PadSouth'],\n  uiCancel: ['Escape', 'Backspace', 'PadEast'],\n  uiUp: ['ArrowUp', 'PadUp', 'PadLeftStickUp'],\n  uiDown: ['ArrowDown', 'PadDown', 'PadLeftStickDown'],\n  uiLeft: ['ArrowLeft', 'PadLeft', 'PadLeftStickLeft'],\n  uiRight: ['ArrowRight', 'PadRight', 'PadLeftStickRight'],\n});\n\n/** Codes no action map binds: the pause buttons, and keys the browser or the system keeps. */\nexport const RESERVED_CODES: readonly string[] = Object.freeze([\n  'Escape',\n  'PadStart',\n  'PadHome',\n  'F5',\n  'F11',\n  'F12',\n  'MetaLeft',\n  'MetaRight',\n]);\n\n/** The fields of an `actionMap` entry. */\nconst ACTION_MAP_FIELDS = {\n  description: { type: 'string', default: '', description: 'What the map is for, in plain words.' },\n  actions: {\n    type: 'object',\n    required: true,\n    description:\n      'Action name → the codes bound to it (KeyboardEvent.code, MouseLeft…, PadSouth…, PadLeftStickUp…): held actions are the intents b, pressed ones p.',\n  },\n  move: {\n    type: 'array',\n    items: { type: 'string' },\n    default: ['forward', 'back', 'left', 'right'],\n    description: 'The four actions that walk, as forward, back, left, right: their strengths make the move axes.',\n  },\n  values: {\n    type: 'object',\n    default: {},\n    description:\n      'Custom intent key (\"game:throttle\") → action: its analog strength (0 to 1, a trigger) is that intent.',\n  },\n  look: {\n    type: 'boolean',\n    default: false,\n    description: \"True for first person and the shooter: the intents carry look = [the camera's yaw, its pitch].\",\n  },\n  aimWith: {\n    type: 'string',\n    enum: AIM_RULES,\n    default: 'none',\n    description:\n      \"What the intents' aim holds: none; centre, the point the screen centre's ray meets (first person, the shooter); pointer, the pointer's ray onto the player's floor or a right stick's push (isometric, top-down).\",\n  },\n  lock: {\n    type: 'boolean',\n    default: false,\n    description:\n      'True when the mouse turns the view: a click on the game takes the pointer lock, which pause and Escape give back.',\n  },\n  view: {\n    type: 'array',\n    items: { type: 'string' },\n    default: [],\n    description:\n      \"Actions the page reads for its view (a camera switch, a view's turn): bound and rebound like the others, never buttons in the intents.\",\n  },\n  reserved: {\n    type: 'array',\n    items: { type: 'string' },\n    default: [],\n    description: 'Codes the game keeps for its own hotkeys: rebinding refuses them, as it refuses RESERVED_CODES.',\n  },\n} as const satisfies Schema;\n\n/** An action map entry. */\nexport type ActionMap = Entry & {\n  readonly description: string;\n  readonly actions: Readonly<Record<string, readonly string[]>>;\n  readonly move: readonly string[];\n  readonly values: Readonly<Record<string, string>>;\n  readonly look: boolean;\n  readonly aimWith: AimRule;\n  readonly lock: boolean;\n  readonly view: readonly string[];\n  readonly reserved: readonly string[];\n};\n\n/** An action name: a lower-case word, letters and digits. */\nconst ACTION = /^[a-z][A-Za-z0-9]*$/;\n\n/** The problems of a map beyond its fields (the file comment lists them). */\nfunction mapProblems(map: ActionMap): string[] {\n  const problems: string[] = [];\n  const reserved = new Set([...RESERVED_CODES, ...map.reserved]);\n  for (const [action, codes] of Object.entries(map.actions)) {\n    if (!ACTION.test(action)) problems.push(`the action ${show(action)} must be a lower-case word (jump, skill2)`);\n    if (Object.hasOwn(SYSTEM_ACTIONS, action)) problems.push(`${action} is a system action, never rebound: rename it`);\n    if (!Array.isArray(codes)) {\n      problems.push(`actions.${action} is ${show(codes)}; it must be a list of codes`);\n      continue;\n    }\n    for (const code of codes) {\n      if (!isCode(code)) problems.push(`actions.${action} holds ${show(code)}, not a code (KeyW, MouseLeft, PadSouth)`);\n      else if (reserved.has(code)) problems.push(`actions.${action} binds the reserved code ${code}`);\n    }\n  }\n  if (map.move.length !== 4) problems.push(`move names ${map.move.length} actions: give forward, back, left, right`);\n  for (const action of map.move) {\n    if (!Object.hasOwn(map.actions, action)) problems.push(`move names ${show(action)}, which actions lacks`);\n  }\n  for (const action of map.view) {\n    if (!Object.hasOwn(map.actions, action)) problems.push(`view names ${show(action)}, which actions lacks`);\n    else if (map.move.includes(action)) problems.push(`view names ${action}, a move action`);\n  }\n  for (const [key, action] of Object.entries(map.values)) {\n    if (!/^[a-z][A-Za-z0-9]*:[A-Za-z0-9_.-]+$/.test(key)) problems.push(`values key ${show(key)} must be \"game:name\"`);\n    if (typeof action !== 'string' || !Object.hasOwn(map.actions, action)) {\n      problems.push(`values.${key} names ${show(action)}, which actions lacks`);\n    }\n  }\n  for (const code of map.reserved) if (!isCode(code)) problems.push(`reserved holds ${show(code)}, not a code`);\n  return problems;\n}\n\n/** Declares the kind `actionMap` on `registry` unless it has it. */\nexport function actionMapKind(registry: Registry = sharedRegistry): void {\n  if (registry.kinds().includes('actionMap')) return;\n  registry.defineKind('actionMap', {\n    description:\n      'Named actions and the physical codes bound to each (keys by KeyboardEvent.code, mouse, pad by position): what the input devices turn into intents.',\n    fields: ACTION_MAP_FIELDS,\n    defineWith: \"defineActionMap('actionMap:<name>', { actions: { jump: ['Space', 'PadSouth'] } })\",\n    check: (entry) => mapProblems(entry as ActionMap),\n  });\n}\n\n/** How an action map is written. */\nexport interface ActionMapSpec {\n  description?: string;\n  actions: Readonly<Record<string, readonly string[]>>;\n  move?: readonly [string, string, string, string];\n  values?: Readonly<Record<string, string>>;\n  look?: boolean;\n  aimWith?: AimRule;\n  lock?: boolean;\n  view?: readonly string[];\n  reserved?: readonly string[];\n}\n\n/** Registers an action map (on the shared registry by default). Throws `CORE_BAD_SPEC` naming each problem. */\nexport function defineActionMap(id: string, spec: ActionMapSpec, registry: Registry = sharedRegistry): ActionMap {\n  actionMapKind(registry);\n  return registry.def('actionMap', id, spec as unknown as Record<string, unknown>) as ActionMap;\n}","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01HiXvBNxPPSLmudGHDibW2P","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgj9HHpAjkQ5A32wsBaZB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013nLGNAk2Erx8CLttk5pbZH","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"sed -n 60,200p engine/sim/session.ts && echo ---------- && sed -n 1,90p engine/sim/devActions.ts && echo ------ && sed -n 1,60p engine/dev/members.ts","description":"Read session API, dev actions and inspector members"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14901,"cache_read_input_tokens":167490,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14901},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b0d0401-1a79-4c2f-8a33-ba9239fdbfed","uuid":"66943743-4036-4eda-80a1-b5ec4e6b9bfc","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:23:32.223Z","request_id":"req_011Cgj9HHaGzJRqcSxuWynvt","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_013nLGNAk2Erx8CLttk5pbZH":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211947__x8ab6bc/work/.research/my-3dge && sed -n 60,200p engine/sim/session.ts && echo ---------- && sed -n 1,90p engine/sim/devActions.ts && echo ------ && sed -n 1,60p engine/dev/members.ts","description":"Read session API, dev actions and inspector members"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_013nLGNAk2Erx8CLttk5pbZH":{"cwd":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211947__x8ab6bc/work/.research/my-3dge"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013nLGNAk2Erx8CLttk5pbZH","type":"tool_result","content":"  },\n});\n\n/**\n * A started scene that records its inputs from step 0, so `record()` returns it as a replay. `step(intents)`\n * normalizes the intents against the step before and logs what changed. Setting changes through the store\n * (`settings`: set, setText, load, fromUrl, reset, override) are logged as `set` points: before each `set`, `act` and\n * `step`, the session compares the store's non-view values with the last ones it saw. `act` captures the world, runs\n * the action inside `w.run` and, if it throws, restores the capture and logs nothing; else it logs it with its args.\n */\nexport interface Session<C extends object = AnyComponents, E extends EventMap = EventMap> extends SceneRun<C, E> {\n  /** Steps taken through the session. */\n  readonly steps: number;\n  /** The intents the last step got. */\n  readonly intents: Intents;\n  /** The change-points so far. */\n  readonly inputs: readonly InputEntry[];\n  /** One step with these intents, normalized; recorded once the world counts it. Throws `INPUT_BAD_INTENTS`. */\n  step(intents?: unknown): Intents;\n  /** Sets a setting between steps; a non-view change is recorded at this step (as is any change through `settings`). */\n  set(path: string, value: unknown): SettingChange;\n  /**\n   * Runs the dev action `name` between steps, the scene's own or else the engine's (engine/sim/devActions.ts: its args\n   * checked, its settings set, then its run), all or nothing, then records it. Throws `SIM_NO_ACTION`, or\n   * `CORE_BAD_SPEC` for args its schema refuses.\n   */\n  act(name: string, args?: unknown): void;\n  /** The whole sim, copied (`world.capture()`), with where the recording stands: what `restore` takes. */\n  capture(): WorldCapture;\n  /**\n   * Puts back a capture this session took, unchanged, with its recording (change-points, steps, intents) as it stood\n   * then. Throws `SIM_FOREIGN_CAPTURE` or `SIM_EDITED_CAPTURE` (or the world's `SIM_BAD_CAPTURE`), changing nothing.\n   */\n  restore(capture: WorldCapture): void;\n  /** The replay of every step so far, from step 0, without hashes. Throws `SIM_OFF_RECORD`. */\n  record(): Replay;\n}\n\n/** Where a session's recording stood at a capture (change-points as text: the last may change since) and its digest. */\ntype Mark = { steps: number; inputs: string; last: Intents; seen: Record<string, SettingValue>; hash: string };\n\n/** The digest of a capture's data, or a note when it no longer is plain data. */\nfunction digest(capture: WorldCapture): string {\n  try {\n    return hashValue(capture as unknown as Canonical);\n  } catch {\n    return 'no hash (no longer plain data)';\n  }\n}\n\n/** Starts a scene as a recorded session: `startScene`, plus the recording. */\nexport function createSession<C extends object = AnyComponents, E extends EventMap = EventMap>(\n  scene: Parameters<typeof startScene<C, E>>[0],\n  options: SceneOptions = {},\n): Session<C, E> {\n  const run = startScene<C, E>(scene, { ...options, seed: checkSeed(options.seed, 'createSession(scene, { seed })') });\n  const { world, settings } = run;\n  const registry = options.registry ?? sharedRegistry;\n  const viewOf = (path: string) => registry.get('setting', path).view === true;\n  const start = Object.fromEntries(Object.entries(options.settings ?? {}).filter(([path]) => !viewOf(path)));\n  const inputs: InputEntry[] = [];\n  let last: Intents = NO_INTENTS;\n  let steps = 0;\n  let seen = settings.sim.values();\n  const marks = new WeakMap<WorldCapture, Mark>();\n  /** The change-point to write a `what` into at step `at`: the last one when the play order allows, else a new one. */\n  const pointFor = (what: 'set' | 'dev' | 'intents', at = world.tick): InputChange => {\n    const tail = inputs[inputs.length - 1];\n    if (tail && tail[0] === at) {\n      const change = tail[1];\n      const intents = Object.keys(change).some((key) => Object.hasOwn(INTENT_KEYS, key) || key.includes(':'));\n      if (!intents && (what === 'intents' || change.dev === undefined)) return change;\n    }\n    const change: InputChange = {};\n    inputs.push([at, change]);\n    return change;\n  };\n  /** Logs every non-view value the store holds that differs from the last ones seen, as a `set` at this step. */\n  const sync = () => {\n    const now = settings.sim.values();\n    for (const [path, value] of Object.entries(now)) {\n      const before = Object.hasOwn(seen, path) ? seen[path] : registry.get('setting', path).default;\n      if (sameValue(before, value)) continue;\n      const point = pointFor('set');\n      point.set = { ...point.set, [path]: deserialize(serialize(value as Canonical)) as SettingValue };\n    }\n    seen = now;\n  };\n  const session: Session<C, E> = {\n    ...run,\n    get steps() {\n      return steps;\n    },\n    get intents() {\n      return last;\n    },\n    inputs,\n    step(raw = {}) {\n      const next = normalizeIntents(raw, last);\n      sync();\n      const at = world.tick;\n      try {\n        world.step(next);\n      } finally {\n        if (world.tick !== at) {\n          const change = diffIntents(last, next);\n          if (Object.keys(change).length) Object.assign(pointFor('intents', at), change);\n          [last, steps] = [next, steps + 1];\n        }\n      }\n      return next;\n    },\n    set(path, value) {\n      sync();\n      const change = settings.set(path, value);\n      sync();\n      return change;\n    },\n    act(name, args) {\n      const actions = run.scene.actions as Record<string, (w: unknown, a: unknown) => void>;\n      const own = Object.hasOwn(actions, name) && typeof actions[name] === 'function' ? actions[name] : undefined;\n      const engine = own ? undefined : findDevAction(registry, name);\n      if (!own && !engine) {\n        const names = [...new Set([...Object.keys(actions), ...listDevActions(registry).map((a) => a.id)])].sort();\n        const near = didYouMean(name, names).trim().slice(1, -1);\n        const suggestion = near || (names.length ? `its actions: ${names.map(show).join(', ')}` : 'it has none');\n        throw codeError('SIM_NO_ACTION', { scene: run.scene.id, name: show(name), suggestion });\n      }\n      const text = args === undefined ? undefined : serialize(args as Canonical);\n      const given = () => (text === undefined ? undefined : deserialize(text));\n      const checked = engine ? devArgs(engine, given(), name) : {}; // before anything changes\n      sync();\n      const before = world.capture(); // the sim and its recorded settings: a throw puts both back\n      try {\n        for (const [path, value] of Object.entries(engine?.settings(checked) ?? {})) settings.set(path, value);\n        if (own) world.run((w) => own(w, given()));\n        else if (engine && changesSim(engine)) world.run((w) => engine.run(w as never, checked));\n      } catch (error) {\n        world.restore(before);\n        throw error;\n      }\n----------\n/**\n * @file The engine's dev actions (PLAN.md WP 5.6, §5.6; doctrines: Agent-operable, Reproducible): the registry kind\n * `devAction`, a change a developer makes to a running scene between steps, recorded so that a replay makes it again,\n * and the engine's own five. An entry says what it changes:\n * - `run(w, args)`: the sim, inside `w.run`, through the session (`session.act(name, args)`: all or nothing, recorded\n *   as the change-point's `dev` with its `args`); a scene's own action of the same name wins (engine/sim/scene.ts);\n * - `settings(args)`: the settings it sets, by path, through the session's store (recorded as `set`, unless view).\n * Its `args` are a schema (engine/core/schema.ts): `devArgs` checks what it is given and fills the defaults before\n * anything changes. `__engine.actions` lists and runs them (engine/dev/actions.ts); `defineDevAction` adds a game's.\n *\n * The engine's, each on the player (the first actor whose `player` is set) unless given an `id`:\n * - `god { on, id }`: the entity holds the component `invulnerable`, so `damage` takes no hit on it\n *   (engine/sim/damage.ts); off, it lets go of it;\n * - `freeze { on }`: the setting `ai.frozen`, so the step skips the systems of the phase `ai` (engine/sim/world.ts),\n *   and the movers they drive stand: each actor that is not a player lets go of its AI's intents, and each living crowd\n *   agent (a component holding every field of `CROWD_AGENT_FIELDS`) stops across the ground;\n * - `spawn { prop, count, distance }`: `count` props of the entry `prop`, `distance` m from the player, 0.4 rad apart\n *   about the way it faces, each on the floor below (the physics' probe from 2 m over its feet, else at its feet);\n * - `travel { at, yaw, id }`: the actor put at `at` (its feet, m), facing `yaw` (its own when absent), at rest\n *   (`placeActor`, engine/sim/actors.ts);\n * - `timeScale { scale }`: the setting `time.scale`, the frame clock's speed (engine/core/time.ts): a view setting,\n *   so it never reaches the sim or a replay.\n *\n * Invariants: an action changes the sim only through `run`, inside the session's capture, so a throw leaves nothing\n * (settings included) and a replay's `dev` makes the same change; `settings` is a pure function of the args.\n * `defineDevActionKinds(registry)` declares the kind, the component `invulnerable`, the setting `ai.frozen` and the\n * engine's five on a registry (the shared one when this module loads; engine/sim/session.ts imports it, so every\n * session finds them). Carried from `my-3d2dge:src/emberdeep/62-developer.js:1-132` (the sandbox's switches, its\n * spawn in a fan before the hero, its travel) and `10-combat.js:106` (god mode: a hit takes nothing), mechanisms only.\n *\n * @example\n * import { registry } from '../core/registry';\n * listDevActions(registry).map((action) => action.id); // ['freeze', 'god', 'spawn', 'timeScale', 'travel']\n * devArgs(findDevAction(registry, 'freeze')!, undefined, 'freeze'); // { on: true }: the default filled\n * // in a scene with a player actor: session.act('travel', { at: [3, 0, 5] }) puts him there, and record() holds\n * // the change-point { dev: 'travel', args: { at: [3, 0, 5] } }\n * @see engine/dev/actions.test.ts\n */\nimport { codeError, defineCodes } from '../core/log';\nimport { registry as sharedRegistry, type Entry, type Registry } from '../core/registry';\nimport { checkField, isPlainObject, parse, show, type Schema } from '../core/schema';\nimport { defineSettings, type SettingValue } from '../core/settings';\nimport { CROWD_AGENT_FIELDS } from '../physics/crowd';\nimport { physicsOf } from '../physics/binding';\nimport { placeActor, type ActorComponent } from './actors';\nimport { spawnProp } from './props';\nimport { defineComponent } from './state';\nimport { AI_FROZEN, AI_FROZEN_SETTINGS } from './systems';\nimport type { World } from './world';\n\n/** The codes this module raises, with their fixes. */\nexport const DEV_ACTION_CODES = defineCodes('sim', {\n  SIM_NO_ACTOR: {\n    template: '{what} has no actor to work on: {problem}',\n    fix: 'give the id of an actor ({ id }), or spawn a player actor in the scene (spawnActor, player: true)',\n    doc: \"Raised by the engine's dev actions that work on an actor (engine/sim/devActions.ts: god, spawn, travel) and by the bot (engine/dev/bot.ts) when the id given is no live actor, or none is given and the scene has no player actor. Nothing has changed.\",\n  },\n});\n\n/** How a dev action is written: `defineDevAction(name, spec)`. */\nexport interface DevActionSpec {\n  /** What it does, one line: `__engine.actions.list()` shows it. */\n  help: string;\n  /** Its arguments, name → schema field: checked, defaults filled, before it runs. */\n  args?: Schema;\n  /** What it changes in the sim, inside `w.run`, between steps: recorded as a dev action. */\n  run?: (w: World, args: Record<string, unknown>) => void;\n  /** The settings it sets, by path: through the session, recorded unless view. */\n  settings?: (args: Record<string, unknown>) => Record<string, SettingValue>;\n}\n\n/** A registered dev action: its spec, plus `id` (its name) and `kind`. */\nexport type DevAction = Entry & Required<DevActionSpec>;\n\n/** What an entry without a `run` changes in the sim: nothing, and it is not recorded as a dev action. */\nconst NO_RUN = (): void => {};\n/** What an entry without `settings` sets: nothing. */\nconst NO_SETTINGS = (): Record<string, SettingValue> => ({});\n\n/** The fields of a `devAction` entry. */\nconst DEV_ACTION_FIELDS = {\n  help: { type: 'string', required: true, description: 'What it does, one line: __engine.actions.list() shows it.' },\n  args: {\n    type: 'object',\n    default: {},\n    description:\n      'Its arguments, name → schema field (engine/core/schema.ts): checked, defaults filled, before it runs.',\n  },\n  run: {\n    type: 'function',\n------\n/**\n * @file The registry kind `inspectorMember` (PLAN.md §8.3, §5.8's one tool table, WP 1.6): what an inspector member\n * is (a help line, its arguments as schema fields, its implementation), the checks each one passes when defined, and\n * the signatures and help lines made from them. engine/dev/inspector.ts assembles `__engine` from these entries and\n * registers the core members.\n *\n * Each WP registers its members from its own files: `defineMember(name, spec)` from `dev/`, or `def('inspectorMember',\n * name, spec)` through engine/core/registry.ts from any layer that loads after this module, so no layer imports\n * `dev/` for it. One table feeds `help()`, the argument checks and, later, the MCP server's tool schemas (WP 7.6):\n * `args` is a schema (engine/core/schema.ts) whose key order is the call order.\n *\n * Invariants (each a `CORE_BAD_SPEC` problem when broken): a name is a lower-case word or dotted words\n * (`scene.dump`), and is a member or a namespace of members, never both; every argument field is valid and\n * documented; required arguments come before optional ones; a `value` member (read as a property) takes none; `impl`\n * takes no argument `args` lacks (`impl.length` counts the host).\n *\n * The rule for members that change the sim: only through the session's recorded operations, so `record()` always\n * replays what happened (PLAN.md §8.4). The host hands members `recordedRun(session)`: the session's `step` (or\n * `host.step`, through the clock), `set` and its settings store, `act`, `capture` and `restore`, `record`, and the\n * world read-only (`WorldReads`: no spawn, add, emit, step, run, capture or restore; entities, the systems list and\n * the change-points as frozen copies, so a write through them throws instead of changing the run off the record).\n * A change no recorded operation can make is refused (a coded error naming the fix), or added to the session first;\n * presentation that never reaches the sim (the clock's view settings) is free.\n *\n * @example\n * import { createRegistry } from '../core/registry';\n * const members = createRegistry();\n * const at = { type: 'string', required: true, description: 'Whom.' } as const;\n * defineMember('wave', { help: 'Waves.', args: { at }, impl: () => 1 }, members);\n * signatureOf(members.get('inspectorMember', 'wave') as Member); // 'wave(at)'\n * helpText(members); // 'wave(at)  Waves.'\n * @see engine/dev/inspector.test.ts\n */\nimport type { Log } from '../core/log';\nimport { registry as sharedRegistry, type Entry, type Registry } from '../core/registry';\nimport { checkField, copyValue, freezeValue, show, type Field, type Schema } from '../core/schema';\nimport type { Clock } from '../core/time';\nimport type { Session } from '../sim/session';\nimport type { EntityData } from '../sim/state';\nimport type { World, WorldEvents } from '../sim/world';\n\n/** The world as members read it: its reads, none of its mutators (members change the sim through the session). */\nexport type WorldReads = Pick<\n  World,\n  'seed' | 'hz' | 'dt' | 'tick' | 'time' | 'count' | 'has' | 'state' | 'hash' | 'trace'\n> & {\n  /** A frozen copy of one live entity, or undefined. */\n  get(id: number): EntityData | undefined;\n  /** Frozen copies of the live entities holding every named component, in id order. Throws `SIM_UNKNOWN_COMPONENT`. */\n  query(...names: string[]): readonly EntityData[];\n  /** The delivered events' trace; listeners are the scene's. */\n  readonly events: Pick<WorldEvents, 'trace'>;\n  /** The systems in run order, a frozen list; adding or removing them is the scene's. */\n  readonly systems: Pick<World['systems'], 'list'>;\n};\n\n/** The run as members reach it: the session's recorded operations, scene and settings store, and the world read-only. */\nexport type RecordedRun = Omit<Session, 'world'> & { readonly world: WorldReads };\n\n/**","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b0d0401-1a79-4c2f-8a33-ba9239fdbfed","uuid":"fbd9fe69-3061-4b1c-ab29-95aa7397545f","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:23:32.323Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"  },\n});\n\n/**\n * A started scene that records its inputs from step 0, so `record()` returns it as a replay. `step(intents)`\n * normalizes the intents against the step before and logs what changed. Setting changes through the store\n * (`settings`: set, setText, load, fromUrl, reset, override) are logged as `set` points: before each `set`, `act` and\n * `step`, the session compares the store's non-view values with the last ones it saw. `act` captures the world, runs\n * the action inside `w.run` and, if it throws, restores the capture and logs nothing; else it logs it with its args.\n */\nexport interface Session<C extends object = AnyComponents, E extends EventMap = EventMap> extends SceneRun<C, E> {\n  /** Steps taken through the session. */\n  readonly steps: number;\n  /** The intents the last step got. */\n  readonly intents: Intents;\n  /** The change-points so far. */\n  readonly inputs: readonly InputEntry[];\n  /** One step with these intents, normalized; recorded once the world counts it. Throws `INPUT_BAD_INTENTS`. */\n  step(intents?: unknown): Intents;\n  /** Sets a setting between steps; a non-view change is recorded at this step (as is any change through `settings`). */\n  set(path: string, value: unknown): SettingChange;\n  /**\n   * Runs the dev action `name` between steps, the scene's own or else the engine's (engine/sim/devActions.ts: its args\n   * checked, its settings set, then its run), all or nothing, then records it. Throws `SIM_NO_ACTION`, or\n   * `CORE_BAD_SPEC` for args its schema refuses.\n   */\n  act(name: string, args?: unknown): void;\n  /** The whole sim, copied (`world.capture()`), with where the recording stands: what `restore` takes. */\n  capture(): WorldCapture;\n  /**\n   * Puts back a capture this session took, unchanged, with its recording (change-points, steps, intents) as it stood\n   * then. Throws `SIM_FOREIGN_CAPTURE` or `SIM_EDITED_CAPTURE` (or the world's `SIM_BAD_CAPTURE`), changing nothing.\n   */\n  restore(capture: WorldCapture): void;\n  /** The replay of every step so far, from step 0, without hashes. Throws `SIM_OFF_RECORD`. */\n  record(): Replay;\n}\n\n/** Where a session's recording stood at a capture (change-points as text: the last may change since) and its digest. */\ntype Mark = { steps: number; inputs: string; last: Intents; seen: Record<string, SettingValue>; hash: string };\n\n/** The digest of a capture's data, or a note when it no longer is plain data. */\nfunction digest(capture: WorldCapture): string {\n  try {\n    return hashValue(capture as unknown as Canonical);\n  } catch {\n    return 'no hash (no longer plain data)';\n  }\n}\n\n/** Starts a scene as a recorded session: `startScene`, plus the recording. */\nexport function createSession<C extends object = AnyComponents, E extends EventMap = EventMap>(\n  scene: Parameters<typeof startScene<C, E>>[0],\n  options: SceneOptions = {},\n): Session<C, E> {\n  const run = startScene<C, E>(scene, { ...options, seed: checkSeed(options.seed, 'createSession(scene, { seed })') });\n  const { world, settings } = run;\n  const registry = options.registry ?? sharedRegistry;\n  const viewOf = (path: string) => registry.get('setting', path).view === true;\n  const start = Object.fromEntries(Object.entries(options.settings ?? {}).filter(([path]) => !viewOf(path)));\n  const inputs: InputEntry[] = [];\n  let last: Intents = NO_INTENTS;\n  let steps = 0;\n  let seen = settings.sim.values();\n  const marks = new WeakMap<WorldCapture, Mark>();\n  /** The change-point to write a `what` into at step `at`: the last one when the play order allows, else a new one. */\n  const pointFor = (what: 'set' | 'dev' | 'intents', at = world.tick): InputChange => {\n    const tail = inputs[inputs.length - 1];\n    if (tail && tail[0] === at) {\n      const change = tail[1];\n      const intents = Object.keys(change).some((key) => Object.hasOwn(INTENT_KEYS, key) || key.includes(':'));\n      if (!intents && (what === 'intents' || change.dev === undefined)) return change;\n    }\n    const change: InputChange = {};\n    inputs.push([at, change]);\n    return change;\n  };\n  /** Logs every non-view value the store holds that differs from the last ones seen, as a `set` at this step. */\n  const sync = () => {\n    const now = settings.sim.values();\n    for (const [path, value] of Object.entries(now)) {\n      const before = Object.hasOwn(seen, path) ? seen[path] : registry.get('setting', path).default;\n      if (sameValue(before, value)) continue;\n      const point = pointFor('set');\n      point.set = { ...point.set, [path]: deserialize(serialize(value as Canonical)) as SettingValue };\n    }\n    seen = now;\n  };\n  const session: Session<C, E> = {\n    ...run,\n    get steps() {\n      return steps;\n    },\n    get intents() {\n      return last;\n    },\n    inputs,\n    step(raw = {}) {\n      const next = normalizeIntents(raw, last);\n      sync();\n      const at = world.tick;\n      try {\n        world.step(next);\n      } finally {\n        if (world.tick !== at) {\n          const change = diffIntents(last, next);\n          if (Object.keys(change).length) Object.assign(pointFor('intents', at), change);\n          [last, steps] = [next, steps + 1];\n        }\n      }\n      return next;\n    },\n    set(path, value) {\n      sync();\n      const change = settings.set(path, value);\n      sync();\n      return change;\n    },\n    act(name, args) {\n      const actions = run.scene.actions as Record<string, (w: unknown, a: unknown) => void>;\n      const own = Object.hasOwn(actions, name) && typeof actions[name] === 'function' ? actions[name] : undefined;\n      const engine = own ? undefined : findDevAction(registry, name);\n      if (!own && !engine) {\n        const names = [...new Set([...Object.keys(actions), ...listDevActions(registry).map((a) => a.id)])].sort();\n        const near = didYouMean(name, names).trim().slice(1, -1);\n        const suggestion = near || (names.length ? `its actions: ${names.map(show).join(', ')}` : 'it has none');\n        throw codeError('SIM_NO_ACTION', { scene: run.scene.id, name: show(name), suggestion });\n      }\n      const text = args === undefined ? undefined : serialize(args as Canonical);\n      const given = () => (text === undefined ? undefined : deserialize(text));\n      const checked = engine ? devArgs(engine, given(), name) : {}; // before anything changes\n      sync();\n      const before = world.capture(); // the sim and its recorded settings: a throw puts both back\n      try {\n        for (const [path, value] of Object.entries(engine?.settings(checked) ?? {})) settings.set(path, value);\n        if (own) world.run((w) => own(w, given()));\n        else if (engine && changesSim(engine)) world.run((w) => engine.run(w as never, checked));\n      } catch (error) {\n        world.restore(before);\n        throw error;\n      }\n----------\n/**\n * @file The engine's dev actions (PLAN.md WP 5.6, §5.6; doctrines: Agent-operable, Reproducible): the registry kind\n * `devAction`, a change a developer makes to a running scene between steps, recorded so that a replay makes it again,\n * and the engine's own five. An entry says what it changes:\n * - `run(w, args)`: the sim, inside `w.run`, through the session (`session.act(name, args)`: all or nothing, recorded\n *   as the change-point's `dev` with its `args`); a scene's own action of the same name wins (engine/sim/scene.ts);\n * - `settings(args)`: the settings it sets, by path, through the session's store (recorded as `set`, unless view).\n * Its `args` are a schema (engine/core/schema.ts): `devArgs` checks what it is given and fills the defaults before\n * anything changes. `__engine.actions` lists and runs them (engine/dev/actions.ts); `defineDevAction` adds a game's.\n *\n * The engine's, each on the player (the first actor whose `player` is set) unless given an `id`:\n * - `god { on, id }`: the entity holds the component `invulnerable`, so `damage` takes no hit on it\n *   (engine/sim/damage.ts); off, it lets go of it;\n * - `freeze { on }`: the setting `ai.frozen`, so the step skips the systems of the phase `ai` (engine/sim/world.ts),\n *   and the movers they drive stand: each actor that is not a player lets go of its AI's intents, and each living crowd\n *   agent (a component holding every field of `CROWD_AGENT_FIELDS`) stops across the ground;\n * - `spawn { prop, count, distance }`: `count` props of the entry `prop`, `distance` m from the player, 0.4 rad apart\n *   about the way it faces, each on the floor below (the physics' probe from 2 m over its feet, else at its feet);\n * - `travel { at, yaw, id }`: the actor put at `at` (its feet, m), facing `yaw` (its own when absent), at rest\n *   (`placeActor`, engine/sim/actors.ts);\n * - `timeScale { scale }`: the setting `time.scale`, the frame clock's speed (engine/core/time.ts): a view setting,\n *   so it never reaches the sim or a replay.\n *\n * Invariants: an action changes the sim only through `run`, inside the session's capture, so a throw leaves nothing\n * (settings included) and a replay's `dev` makes the same change; `settings` is a pure function of the args.\n * `defineDevActionKinds(registry)` declares the kind, the component `invulnerable`, the setting `ai.frozen` and the\n * engine's five on a registry (the shared one when this module loads; engine/sim/session.ts imports it, so every\n * session finds them). Carried from `my-3d2dge:src/emberdeep/62-developer.js:1-132` (the sandbox's switches, its\n * spawn in a fan before the hero, its travel) and `10-combat.js:106` (god mode: a hit takes nothing), mechanisms only.\n *\n * @example\n * import { registry } from '../core/registry';\n * listDevActions(registry).map((action) => action.id); // ['freeze', 'god', 'spawn', 'timeScale', 'travel']\n * devArgs(findDevAction(registry, 'freeze')!, undefined, 'freeze'); // { on: true }: the default filled\n * // in a scene with a player actor: session.act('travel', { at: [3, 0, 5] }) puts him there, and record() holds\n * // the change-point { dev: 'travel', args: { at: [3, 0, 5] } }\n * @see engine/dev/actions.test.ts\n */\nimport { codeError, defineCodes } from '../core/log';\nimport { registry as sharedRegistry, type Entry, type Registry } from '../core/registry';\nimport { checkField, isPlainObject, parse, show, type Schema } from '../core/schema';\nimport { defineSettings, type SettingValue } from '../core/settings';\nimport { CROWD_AGENT_FIELDS } from '../physics/crowd';\nimport { physicsOf } from '../physics/binding';\nimport { placeActor, type ActorComponent } from './actors';\nimport { spawnProp } from './props';\nimport { defineComponent } from './state';\nimport { AI_FROZEN, AI_FROZEN_SETTINGS } from './systems';\nimport type { World } from './world';\n\n/** The codes this module raises, with their fixes. */\nexport const DEV_ACTION_CODES = defineCodes('sim', {\n  SIM_NO_ACTOR: {\n    template: '{what} has no actor to work on: {problem}',\n    fix: 'give the id of an actor ({ id }), or spawn a player actor in the scene (spawnActor, player: true)',\n    doc: \"Raised by the engine's dev actions that work on an actor (engine/sim/devActions.ts: god, spawn, travel) and by the bot (engine/dev/bot.ts) when the id given is no live actor, or none is given and the scene has no player actor. Nothing has changed.\",\n  },\n});\n\n/** How a dev action is written: `defineDevAction(name, spec)`. */\nexport interface DevActionSpec {\n  /** What it does, one line: `__engine.actions.list()` shows it. */\n  help: string;\n  /** Its arguments, name → schema field: checked, defaults filled, before it runs. */\n  args?: Schema;\n  /** What it changes in the sim, inside `w.run`, between steps: recorded as a dev action. */\n  run?: (w: World, args: Record<string, unknown>) => void;\n  /** The settings it sets, by path: through the session, recorded unless view. */\n  settings?: (args: Record<string, unknown>) => Record<string, SettingValue>;\n}\n\n/** A registered dev action: its spec, plus `id` (its name) and `kind`. */\nexport type DevAction = Entry & Required<DevActionSpec>;\n\n/** What an entry without a `run` changes in the sim: nothing, and it is not recorded as a dev action. */\nconst NO_RUN = (): void => {};\n/** What an entry without `settings` sets: nothing. */\nconst NO_SETTINGS = (): Record<string, SettingValue> => ({});\n\n/** The fields of a `devAction` entry. */\nconst DEV_ACTION_FIELDS = {\n  help: { type: 'string', required: true, description: 'What it does, one line: __engine.actions.list() shows it.' },\n  args: {\n    type: 'object',\n    default: {},\n    description:\n      'Its arguments, name → schema field (engine/core/schema.ts): checked, defaults filled, before it runs.',\n  },\n  run: {\n    type: 'function',\n------\n/**\n * @file The registry kind `inspectorMember` (PLAN.md §8.3, §5.8's one tool table, WP 1.6): what an inspector member\n * is (a help line, its arguments as schema fields, its implementation), the checks each one passes when defined, and\n * the signatures and help lines made from them. engine/dev/inspector.ts assembles `__engine` from these entries and\n * registers the core members.\n *\n * Each WP registers its members from its own files: `defineMember(name, spec)` from `dev/`, or `def('inspectorMember',\n * name, spec)` through engine/core/registry.ts from any layer that loads after this module, so no layer imports\n * `dev/` for it. One table feeds `help()`, the argument checks and, later, the MCP server's tool schemas (WP 7.6):\n * `args` is a schema (engine/core/schema.ts) whose key order is the call order.\n *\n * Invariants (each a `CORE_BAD_SPEC` problem when broken): a name is a lower-case word or dotted words\n * (`scene.dump`), and is a member or a namespace of members, never both; every argument field is valid and\n * documented; required arguments come before optional ones; a `value` member (read as a property) takes none; `impl`\n * takes no argument `args` lacks (`impl.length` counts the host).\n *\n * The rule for members that change the sim: only through the session's recorded operations, so `record()` always\n * replays what happened (PLAN.md §8.4). The host hands members `recordedRun(session)`: the session's `step` (or\n * `host.step`, through the clock), `set` and its settings store, `act`, `capture` and `restore`, `record`, and the\n * world read-only (`WorldReads`: no spawn, add, emit, step, run, capture or restore; entities, the systems list and\n * the change-points as frozen copies, so a write through them throws instead of changing the run off the record).\n * A change no recorded operation can make is refused (a coded error naming the fix), or added to the session first;\n * presentation that never reaches the sim (the clock's view settings) is free.\n *\n * @example\n * import { createRegistry } from '../core/registry';\n * const members = createRegistry();\n * const at = { type: 'string', required: true, description: 'Whom.' } as const;\n * defineMember('wave', { help: 'Waves.', args: { at }, impl: () => 1 }, members);\n * signatureOf(members.get('inspectorMember', 'wave') as Member); // 'wave(at)'\n * helpText(members); // 'wave(at)  Waves.'\n * @see engine/dev/inspector.test.ts\n */\nimport type { Log } from '../core/log';\nimport { registry as sharedRegistry, type Entry, type Registry } from '../core/registry';\nimport { checkField, copyValue, freezeValue, show, type Field, type Schema } from '../core/schema';\nimport type { Clock } from '../core/time';\nimport type { Session } from '../sim/session';\nimport type { EntityData } from '../sim/state';\nimport type { World, WorldEvents } from '../sim/world';\n\n/** The world as members read it: its reads, none of its mutators (members change the sim through the session). */\nexport type WorldReads = Pick<\n  World,\n  'seed' | 'hz' | 'dt' | 'tick' | 'time' | 'count' | 'has' | 'state' | 'hash' | 'trace'\n> & {\n  /** A frozen copy of one live entity, or undefined. */\n  get(id: number): EntityData | undefined;\n  /** Frozen copies of the live entities holding every named component, in id order. Throws `SIM_UNKNOWN_COMPONENT`. */\n  query(...names: string[]): readonly EntityData[];\n  /** The delivered events' trace; listeners are the scene's. */\n  readonly events: Pick<WorldEvents, 'trace'>;\n  /** The systems in run order, a frozen list; adding or removing them is the scene's. */\n  readonly systems: Pick<World['systems'], 'list'>;\n};\n\n/** The run as members reach it: the session's recorded operations, scene and settings store, and the world read-only. */\nexport type RecordedRun = Omit<Session, 'world'> & { readonly world: WorldReads };\n\n/**","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_013nLGNAk2Erx8CLttk5pbZH","permission_decision":{"deci