{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjA41HFqsFLKiVf1B5jh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BTmEX1q3zxauuQnqtUhnQX","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"head_comment() { awk 'NR==1 && /^\\/\\*\\*/{f=1} f{print} /\\*\\//{if(f){exit}}' \"$1\" | cut -c1-200; echo; }; for f in engine/gfx/stage.ts engine/gfx/stageFx.ts engine/gfx/puppets/actors.ts engine/sim/crowdBodies.ts engine/gfx/stageCrowd.ts engine/gfx/level/cutaway.ts; do echo \"=== $f\"; head_comment \"$f\" ; done; ls engine/gfx engine/gfx/fx engine/gfx/level engine/ui engine/audio 2>/dev/null | head -100","description":"Read the file comments of stage, effects, puppets, crowds and cutaway"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1731,"cache_read_input_tokens":254639,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1731},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b0d0401-1a79-4c2f-8a33-ba9239fdbfed","uuid":"806938ac-f325-468c-a49b-c02bc483b137","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:35:39.769Z","request_id":"req_011CgjA3zytndbjpbvyBm7gq","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01BTmEX1q3zxauuQnqtUhnQX":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211947__x8ab6bc/work/.research/proto && head_comment() { awk 'NR==1 && /^\\/\\*\\*/{f=1} f{print} /\\*\\//{if(f){exit}}' \"$1\" | cut -c1-200; echo; }; for f in engine/gfx/stage.ts engine/gfx/stageFx.ts engine/gfx/puppets/actors.ts engine/sim/crowdBodies.ts engine/gfx/stageCrowd.ts engine/gfx/level/cutaway.ts; do echo \"=== $f\"; head_comment \"$f\" ; done; ls engine/gfx engine/gfx/fx engine/gfx/level engine/ui engine/audio 2>/dev/null | head -100","description":"Read the file comments of stage, effects, puppets, crowds and cutaway"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01BTmEX1q3zxauuQnqtUhnQX":{"cwd":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211947__x8ab6bc/work/.research/proto"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BTmEX1q3zxauuQnqtUhnQX","type":"tool_result","content":"=== engine/gfx/stage.ts\n/**\n * @file The stage (PLAN.md §6.4's view, §9.0, WP 2.7): a running scene's presentation graph, built from plain data with\n * no GPU, so a page draws it and a headless engine dumps it (`createHeadless({ view: true })`). `createStage` makes a\n * three.js `Scene` with a sky colour, the stage's ground (engine/gfx/stageGround.ts: a textured plane under the level\n * reaching well past it, or a frame round a terrain, `stage/ground`), its lights (`sky`, engine/gfx/stageSky.ts: a\n * hemisphere light and a sun fitted to the level, or the sky a look names), the level's meshes by runs\n * (engine/gfx/level/runs.ts: `level:room/wall@0,0-15,0`, each wall run on its own in the ID pass, with the level's\n * swaps), the terrain's chunks (engine/gfx/terrain.ts, WP 10.5: they stand for the ground, and the sun fits them when\n * there is no level) and one stand-in per placeable entity.\n *\n * Actors with an animator draw themselves as puppets (engine/gfx/puppets/actors.ts, WP 3.10: `actors`), props standing\n * in the scene (`sceneProp`, engine/sim/props.ts) as their props (engine/gfx/stageProps.ts, WP 4.6: `props`), crowd\n * bodies (`crowdBody`) through a crowd (engine/gfx/stageCrowd.ts, WP 5.7: `crowd`), which the view draws once the\n * frame's camera is placed (`crowd.draw(alpha, camera)`), rides as themselves (engine/gfx/stageRides.ts, WP 13.7:\n * `rides`), and projectiles as bolts (engine/gfx/stageFx.ts, WP 6.7: `fx`, with telegraphs, trails and bursts, handed\n * each frame by the view), and the guns in the actors' hands as props (WP 13.20). Stand-ins: any other entity is drawn\n * as a box when one of its components declares `x` and `z` as numbers in metres (`placeableKinds`, asked of the\n * entries, never of a name: engine/gfx/standIns.ts). The first such component in registry order places it: `x`, `y` (the box's bottom, 0 by\n * default) and `z`, `yaw` (rad), `size` (the box's side, m; 0.5 by default) and `material` (a material library id;\n * `material:default` otherwise). A stand-in is named `<component>#<id>` with `userData.entity`, so the ID pass and the\n * inspector name its entity. `capture(entities, dt)` after each sim step keeps the last two places; `draw(alpha)` puts\n * every stand-in, puppet and prop `alpha` of the way from the one before to the last (§6.4's interpolation).\n *\n * The level's cutaway (engine/gfx/cutaway.ts, its fade taking the rides too) is made when a player first stands on\n * it, never without one; the view runs it as it follows the player (`frame`), with the cut by storey in a classic view\n * (storeyCut.ts) and a site's per structure (engine/gfx/stageSite.ts), the props on a storey it takes off with it.\n *\n * Warm-up: `register(warmup)` registers the ground, the level meshes, the terrain's every level of detail, the\n * cutaway's twins, the puppets, the props' and the crowd's batches and the stand-ins, and adds the stand-ins' looks\n * (side and material), the puppets' builds, the crowd's looks and whether there are a cutaway and props to the shader\n * key, so a new look makes the next frame warm up first instead of stalling.\n *\n * Invariants: presentation only: it reads sim data and never writes it (doctrine: WebGPU only); every object it makes\n * is under `scene`; equal inputs make equal graphs; materials belong to the library and are never disposed here.\n * @example\n * // const stage = createStage({ level: getLevel('level:room'), materials: createMaterialLibrary() });\n * // stage.capture(world.query('mover'));\n * // stage.draw(0.5); // halfway between the last two steps; then renderer.render(stage.scene, camera)\n * @see engine/gfx/stage.test.ts\n */\n\n=== engine/gfx/stageFx.ts\n/**\n * @file The stage's effects (PLAN.md §6.4's view: particles, shake; WP 6.4's effects shown in the box, WP 6.7 core\n * proposal, ADR-0008 amendment 8): what a running scene's sim shows engine/gfx/fx's effects, read from plain data, so\n * a scene draws particles, telegraphs, trails and bolts with no view code of its own. The stage\n * (engine/gfx/stage.ts) makes one (`stage.fx`), under its scene; the run's view (engine/app/view.ts) hands it each\n * rendered frame.\n *\n * What it reads, asked of the component entries, never of a name (`fxKinds`):\n * - **Bolts**: an entity whose component declares the projectile's fields (engine/world/projectiles.ts\n *   `PROJECTILE_FIELDS`: `state`, `kind`, `team`, `x`…`vz`, `radius`) is drawn as a bolt while it is `flying`, `alpha`\n *   of the way between its last two steps, instead of a stand-in.\n * - **Telegraphs**: a component that declares `telegraph` (a string), `position` (an array), `yaw` and `u` (numbers),\n *   and optionally `size`, is a `TelegraphPlace` (engine/world/telegraphs.ts) as plain data: drawn at floor height,\n *   filling, while `telegraph` names one.\n * - **Trails**: every actor's trail as its puppet's last pose sampled it (engine/gfx/puppets/actors.ts `trails`), as a\n *   ribbon in the blade's tint (engine/gfx/fx/ribbons.ts `TRAIL_TINTS`), while its strike sweeps.\n * - **Events**: `frame` feeds the sim world's event trace (`world.events.trace()`, read without listening): every\n *   emitter answering an event's type bursts where its payload says (`hit`, `slain`, `shot`, `slam`…), and each\n *   `gunshot` draws its tracer, flash, impact and hole (engine/gfx/weapons.ts `createWeaponFx`, `shots`), from the\n *   shooter's muzzle as `muzzle(id)` finds it (the stage's puppets' carried gun).\n *\n * The view setting `gfx.effects` (true) turns them on and off; off, they draw nothing and draw no random number, and\n * claim no bolt, so bolts draw as their stand-ins, which the ID pass names (§6.7: a view setting never hides a\n * gameplay entity); the sim hash is the same either way (doctrine: WebGPU only). The view sets it before each read,\n * and a frame that finds it switched reads the entities again first (engine/app/view.ts), so a flying bolt changes\n * hands in that frame, stepped or not (a paused page, a hit-stop, a shot).\n * Every pool is the effects' own, made at full size and registered for the warm-up (`register`), so the fight draws\n * with 0 pipelines built after it.\n *\n * Invariants: presentation only: it reads entities, the trace and the puppets' trails, and never writes the sim;\n * randomness comes from the visual streams it is given (`fxRng`: the world's, never hashed); `reset()` forgets\n * what runs and the trace read, for a new world only: a restore or a dev action keeps the world, whose trace is\n * history and never restored, so reading it again would play its events twice (engine/app/view.ts `restarted`).\n *\n * @example\n * // const fx = createStageFx({ registry, trails: () => actors.trails() });\n * // stage.scene.add(fx.effects.root);\n * // fx.capture(entities); fx.draw(0.5); fx.frame(dt, camera, world.events.trace());\n * @see engine/gfx/stageFx.test.ts\n */\n\n=== engine/gfx/puppets/actors.ts\n/**\n * @file Actors on the stage (PLAN.md WP 3.10, §6.4's view; I-21): every actor with an animator (engine/sim/actors.ts:\n * an entity with the components `actor` and `animator`) drawn as a puppet (engine/gfx/puppets/draw.ts) of the neutral\n * humanoid (`ACTOR_BODY`) or the body its component `puppet` names (`body:mannequin`, WP 8.9), in its animator's build,\n * posed every frame by its animator's presentation half (engine/anim/character.ts `pose`) at the frame's alpha; an\n * actor with clips (`clips`, engine/sim/actorClips.ts) has its clip layer laid over the body, loaded from the same data\n * (a `ClipLayerPool` of the view's own, engine/anim/clip/clipsets.ts). The stage (engine/gfx/stage.ts) draws these.\n *\n * `capture(entities, dt, queries)` after each sim step keeps each actor's last two places (feet and heading) and its\n * animator's data; `draw(alpha)` poses each puppet `alpha` of the way from the one before to the last. `player()` is\n * the first player actor (in id order) as the last draw put it: its feet and, with a puppet, its skeleton, world pose\n * and eye (the head socket, engine/gfx/cameras/first.ts's `eyePoint`), which the cameras follow (engine/app/view.ts).\n * `firstPerson(frame)` draws the player for a first-person camera's frame (engine/gfx/viewmodel/body.ts, WP 13.12:\n * his body hidden, its shadow kept, his arms posed against it by a lens of their own), or whole for null. `trails()` is\n * each puppet's trail as its last pose sampled it (WP 6.7, oldest first), which the stage's effects draw as ribbons.\n * WP 13.20: the weapon an actor has out stands in its right hand while its hold holds a gun (`carried`, `muzzle`).\n * WP 10.2: a `ragdoll` (engine/sim/ragdolls.ts) lays its parts on the bones, faded in and out (`layRagdoll`).\n *\n * WP 6.2 in the box (WP 7.8): an actor's `reactions` (engine/sim/reactions.ts) are a `Reactions` layer on its puppet's\n * animator, loaded at every pose (its flinch bends its spine; a body down on its face is drawn so), its `actions` (WP\n * 13.11, engine/sim/actorActions.ts) an `Actions` layer on its clip layer, its `secondary` a `Secondary` layer whose\n * chains hang under the puppet (engine/gfx/puppets/chains.ts: `actor#<id>/cape`…), and its `post` slot ends with a\n * `FootPlant` (engine/anim/footPlant.ts) on the ground the sim's `queries` find, faded out as far as its clips hold its\n * legs (clipsets.ts `legsHeld`). WP 13.10: an actor's movement (`motion`) shows on its body (motion.ts `MovementPose`)\n * and locks its feet as `plantsFeet` lets it, laid as the feel kit's (anim/bodyPlants.ts); its layers: actorLayers.ts.\n *\n * Invariants: presentation only (doctrine: WebGPU only): its animators and their layers are its own, loaded from the\n * sim's data at every pose and never writing it, so drawing, culling or not drawing never changes the hash (the\n * animator's own invariant, engine/anim/character.test.ts); one puppet per actor, its layers made again when its\n * animator or their components do; every object it draws is under `root`, and a puppet given up waits as a spare for\n * the next actor of its build and body (`createActorPuppets` says why). A puppet is a skinned mesh of two draw calls:\n * right for heroes and a few foes; crowds draw through instanced batches (WP 5.4).\n *\n * @example\n * // const actors = createActorPuppets({ materials: library }); stage.scene.add(actors.root);\n * // const drawn = actors.capture(world.query('actor'), world.dt); // the ids drawn as puppets\n * // actors.draw(0.5);\n * // actors.player()?.eye; // where a first-person camera sits\n * @see engine/gfx/puppets/actors.test.ts\n */\n\n=== engine/sim/crowdBodies.ts\n/**\n * @file Crowd bodies, sim-side (PLAN.md WP 5.7 core proposal, ADR-0008 amendment 6; §6.4; ADR-0009): what a member of\n * a crowd looks like, and its rig's step. An entity with the component `crowdBody` (`CROWD_BODY_FIELDS`) names its rig\n * (a humanoid in a build, a blob, a floater, a quadruped), where it stands and the rig's state as plain data; the\n * stage draws it\n * through a crowd (engine/gfx/stageCrowd.ts: instanced batches, each body posed at its band's detail), instead of a\n * stand-in.\n *\n * `stepCrowdBody(w, id, body, input)` is the rig's sim step (ADR-0009's `anim.step`: every tick, part of the hash),\n * for a system in the phase `anim`: it loads the rig from `body.state`, steps it with `input` and saves it back, and\n * moves the body to `input.at`. A humanoid's is its animator's (engine/anim/character.ts: the body states, its\n * breathing phase drawn from `rng.entity(id, 'anim')` at its first step, as an actor's); a blob's and a floater's are\n * theirs (engine/anim/blob.ts, floater.ts), the floater's clock spread from the same stream; a quadruped's is its own\n * (engine/anim/quadruped.ts, WP 13.21: its clock spread so, its feet on the world's ground where the world has\n * physics, a raycast through the group `world`, `crowdGround`). The first step fills an\n * empty `state` (a spawned body's default) with the rig at rest, turned to `body.yaw`. The rigs are pooled per world\n * and loaded at every step, so they keep no state of their own: a restore continues exactly.\n *\n * - `rig`: `humanoid` (its `look` is a build id, `build:chibi` when empty), `blob` (its `look` names its features:\n *   `horns`, `ears` or `wings`, none when empty; `size` its radius at rest, `BLOB.radius` when 0), `floater` or\n *   `quadruped` (told `input.quadruped`: to sit, what to look at and how hard to wag).\n * - `x`, `y`, `z` (m): a humanoid's, a blob's or a quadruped's feet, a floater's core; `yaw` (rad): where it faces\n *   (a humanoid's from `input.yaw`, a blob's look, a floater's and a quadruped's heading from their rigs).\n *\n * Invariants: everything a crowd body is in the sim is its component; the step writes only the component; footsteps\n * are not emitted (a crowd's would flood the events). The view poses rigs it loads from the component and never\n * writes it, so drawing, LOD and culling never change the hash.\n *\n * @example\n * import { createWorld } from './world';\n * const w = createWorld({ seed: 1 });\n * const id = w.spawn({ crowdBody: { rig: 'blob', x: 2, z: 3 } });\n * const body = w.get(id)!.crowdBody as CrowdBody;\n * w.run((w) => stepCrowdBody(w, id, body, { at: [2, 0, 3.05], velocity: [0, 0, 3] })); // a slime hopping south\n * [body.z, body.yaw]; // [3.05, 0]: moved, looking south\n * (body.state as { squash: number }).squash; // 0: the blob's state, at rest\n * @see engine/sim/crowdBodies.test.ts\n */\n\n=== engine/gfx/stageCrowd.ts\n/**\n * @file Crowd bodies on the stage (PLAN.md WP 5.7 core proposal, ADR-0008 amendment 6; §6.4's view; I-21): every\n * entity with the component `crowdBody` (engine/sim/crowdBodies.ts: a humanoid, blob, floater or quadruped rig, where it stands\n * and its rig's state) drawn through a crowd (engine/gfx/puppets/crowd.ts: instanced batches, a few dozen draw calls\n * for thousands), seen through the crowd's level of detail (engine/gfx/puppets/lod.ts) from the frame's camera. The\n * stage (engine/gfx/stage.ts) draws these instead of stand-ins.\n *\n * `capture(entities, dt)` after each sim step keeps each crowd body's last two places (where it stands and faces) and\n * its component, and returns the ids it draws. `draw(alpha, camera)`, once the frame's camera is placed, puts each\n * body `alpha` of the way from its place a step ago to its last and asks the crowd whether the camera sees it: only a\n * seen body is posed (the view's half of its rig, loaded from the component: a humanoid's animator at its band's\n * detail, `animator.pose({ lod })`; a blob, a floater or a quadruped from its state alone) and drawn, a blob shadow\n * under each humanoid, blob and quadruped on the level's floor. Humanoids wear the neutral humanoid (`body:humanoid`)\n * in their build, blobs `BLOB_BODY` with their features (`blobBody`), floaters `FLOATER_BODY`, quadrupeds\n * `QUADRUPED_BODY` (the dog).\n *\n * The crowd is made when the first crowd body arrives, and added to the stage's scene then: a stage with none has\n * none, and its scene graph is the one it had before. Each look is prepared (its batches made) when the first body\n * wearing it arrives; `register` registers the crowd's batches, present and future, with the warm-up and adds the\n * prepared looks to the shader key, so the frame after a new look arrives warms up first instead of stalling, and a\n * crowd growing in a look it has already built builds no pipeline (its new pages share their batch's shader).\n * Given the renderer's features with `feature:gpuCrowds` on (engine/gfx/features.ts `gpuCrowdsFor`, WP 11.4),\n * `register` makes the crowd again, drawn through a GPU crowd (engine/gfx/enhanced/crowds.ts) sized for the bodies held\n * then; a frame that outgrows it makes it again twice as large and draws again, its size in the shader key, so the\n * renderer warms up before the larger one draws. Headless, or with the feature off, the instancing service draws.\n *\n * Invariants: presentation only (doctrine: WebGPU only): it reads the components and writes nothing back; its rigs\n * are its own, loaded from the component at every pose, so drawing, LOD, culling or not drawing never changes the\n * hash; every object it makes is under the crowd's root.\n *\n * @example\n * // const crowd = createStageCrowd({ scene: stage.scene, materials: library, level });\n * // const drawn = crowd.capture(world.query('crowdBody'), world.dt); // the ids drawn as crowd bodies\n * // crowd.draw(0.5, camera); // halfway between the last two steps, as the camera sees them\n * @see engine/gfx/stageCrowd.test.ts\n */\n\n=== engine/gfx/level/cutaway.ts\nawk: fatal: cannot open file `engine/gfx/level/cutaway.ts' for reading: No such file or directory\n\nengine/audio:\napi.ts\ndata\ndsp\nruntime\n\nengine/gfx:\natmosphere.ts\nbackdrop.ts\ncameras\ncaps.ts\ncutaway.ts\ndaylight.ts\nenhanced\nfeatures.ts\nfx\ngeometry\nidmarks.ts\nidpass.ts\ninstanceSync.ts\ninstancing.ts\nlevel\nlights.ts\nlookMetrics.ts\nmaterials\npipelines.ts\npost\npropLooks.ts\nprops.ts\npuppets\nquality.ts\nrenderer.ts\nresolution.ts\nsceneDump.ts\nshadows.ts\nshot.ts\nsky.ts\nskyKind.ts\nstage.ts\nstageCrowd.ts\nstageFx.ts\nstageGround.ts\nstageProps.ts\nstageRides.ts\nstageShells.ts\nstageSite.ts\nstageSky.ts\nstandIns.ts\nstoreyCut.ts\nterrain.ts\nterrainSplat.ts\ntextures\nthumbnail.ts\nviewmodel\nwarmup.ts\nweapons.ts\n\nengine/gfx/fx:\ndecals.ts\neffects.ts\nemitters.ts\nparticles.ts\npayload.ts\npresets.ts\nribbons.ts\nrings.ts\nshake.ts\nsprites.ts\n\nengine/gfx/level:\nbrazier.ts\ncells.ts\ndais.ts\nfaces.ts\nflights.ts\nmeshes.ts\nopenings.ts\nramp.ts\nrecipes.ts\nroofs.ts\nruns.ts\nshapes.ts\nslab.ts\nslabs.ts\nstairs.ts\nsurface.ts\nwalls.ts\n\nengine/ui:\nchrome.ts\ndialog.ts\nlabels.ts\nmanifest.webmanifest\nmenu.ts\noverlay.ts\nstate.ts\nswipe.ts\ntouch.css\ntouch.ts\nwidgets.ts","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b0d0401-1a79-4c2f-8a33-ba9239fdbfed","uuid":"6d0b7b96-e171-424f-92af-eedd42c7e3c6","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:35:39.824Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"=== engine/gfx/stage.ts\n/**\n * @file The stage (PLAN.md §6.4's view, §9.0, WP 2.7): a running scene's presentation graph, built from plain data with\n * no GPU, so a page draws it and a headless engine dumps it (`createHeadless({ view: true })`). `createStage` makes a\n * three.js `Scene` with a sky colour, the stage's ground (engine/gfx/stageGround.ts: a textured plane under the level\n * reaching well past it, or a frame round a terrain, `stage/ground`), its lights (`sky`, engine/gfx/stageSky.ts: a\n * hemisphere light and a sun fitted to the level, or the sky a look names), the level's meshes by runs\n * (engine/gfx/level/runs.ts: `level:room/wall@0,0-15,0`, each wall run on its own in the ID pass, with the level's\n * swaps), the terrain's chunks (engine/gfx/terrain.ts, WP 10.5: they stand for the ground, and the sun fits them when\n * there is no level) and one stand-in per placeable entity.\n *\n * Actors with an animator draw themselves as puppets (engine/gfx/puppets/actors.ts, WP 3.10: `actors`), props standing\n * in the scene (`sceneProp`, engine/sim/props.ts) as their props (engine/gfx/stageProps.ts, WP 4.6: `props`), crowd\n * bodies (`crowdBody`) through a crowd (engine/gfx/stageCrowd.ts, WP 5.7: `crowd`), which the view draws once the\n * frame's camera is placed (`crowd.draw(alpha, camera)`), rides as themselves (engine/gfx/stageRides.ts, WP 13.7:\n * `rides`), and projectiles as bolts (engine/gfx/stageFx.ts, WP 6.7: `fx`, with telegraphs, trails and bursts, handed\n * each frame by the view), and the guns in the actors' hands as props (WP 13.20). Stand-ins: any other entity is drawn\n * as a box when one of its components declares `x` and `z` as numbers in metres (`placeableKinds`, asked of the\n * entries, never of a name: engine/gfx/standIns.ts). The first such component in registry order places it: `x`, `y` (the box's bottom, 0 by\n * default) and `z`, `yaw` (rad), `size` (the box's side, m; 0.5 by default) and `material` (a material library id;\n * `material:default` otherwise). A stand-in is named `<component>#<id>` with `userData.entity`, so the ID pass and the\n * inspector name its entity. `capture(entities, dt)` after each sim step keeps the last two places; `draw(alpha)` puts\n * every stand-in, puppet and prop `alpha` of the way from the one before to the last (§6.4's interpolation).\n *\n * The level's cutaway (engine/gfx/cutaway.ts, its fade taking the rides too) is made when a player first stands on\n * it, never without one; the view runs it as it follows the player (`frame`), with the cut by storey in a classic view\n * (storeyCut.ts) and a site's per structure (engine/gfx/stageSite.ts), the props on a storey it takes off with it.\n *\n * Warm-up: `register(warmup)` registers the ground, the level meshes, the terrain's every level of detail, the\n * cutaway's twins, the puppets, the props' and the crowd's batches and the stand-ins, and adds the stand-ins' looks\n * (side and material), the puppets' builds, the crowd's looks and whether there are a cutaway and props to the shader\n * key, so a new look makes the next frame warm up first instead of stalling.\n *\n * Invariants: presentation only: it reads sim data and never writes it (doctrine: WebGPU only); every object it makes\n * is under `scene`; equal inputs make equal graphs; materials belong to the library and are never disposed here.\n * @example\n * // const stage = createStage({ level: getLevel('level:room'), materials: createMaterialLibrary() });\n * // stage.capture(world.query('mover'));\n * // stage.draw(0.5); // halfway between the last two steps; then renderer.render(stage.scene, camera)\n * @see engine/gfx/stage.test.ts\n */\n\n=== engine/gfx/stageFx.ts\n/**\n * @file The stage's effects (PLAN.md §6.4's view: particles, shake; WP 6.4's effects shown in the box, WP 6.7 core\n * proposal, ADR-0008 amendment 8): what a running scene's sim shows engine/gfx/fx's effects, read from plain data, so\n * a scene draws particles, telegraphs, trails and bolts with no view code of its own. The stage\n * (engine/gfx/stage.ts) makes one (`stage.fx`), under its scene; the run's view (engine/app/view.ts) hands it each\n * rendered frame.\n *\n * What it reads, asked of the component entries, never of a name (`fxKinds`):\n * - **Bolts**: an entity whose component declares the projectile's fields (engine/world/projectiles.ts\n *   `PROJECTILE_FIELDS`: `state`, `kind`, `team`, `x`…`vz`, `radius`) is drawn as a bolt while it is `flying`, `alpha`\n *   of the way between its last two steps, instead of a stand-in.\n * - **Telegraphs**: a component that declares `telegraph` (a string), `position` (an array), `yaw` and `u` (numbers),\n *   and optionally `size`, is a `TelegraphPlace` (engine/world/telegraphs.ts) as plain data: drawn at floor height,\n *   filling, while `telegraph` names one.\n * - **Trails**: every actor's trail as its puppet's last pose sampled it (engine/gfx/puppets/actors.ts `trails`), as a\n *   ribbon in the blade's tint (engine/gfx/fx/ribbons.ts `TRAIL_TINTS`), while its strike sweeps.\n * - **Events**: `frame` feeds the sim world's event trace (`world.events.trace()`, read without listening): every\n *   emitter answering an event's type bursts where its payload says (`hit`, `slain`, `shot`, `slam`…), and each\n *   `gunshot` draws its tracer, flash, impact and hole (engine/gfx/weapons.ts `createWeaponFx`, `shots`), from the\n *   shooter's muzzle as `muzzle(id)` finds it (the stage's puppets' carried gun).\n *\n * The view setting `gfx.effects` (true) turns them on and off; off, they draw nothing and draw no random number, and\n * claim no bolt, so bolts draw as their stand-ins, which the ID pass names (§6.7: a view setting never hides a\n * gameplay entity); the sim hash is the same either way (doctrine: WebGPU only). The view sets it before each read,\n * and a frame that finds it switched reads the entities again first (engine/app/view.ts), so a flying bolt changes\n * hands in that frame, stepped or not (a paused page, a hit-stop, a shot).\n * Every pool is the effects' own, made at full size and registered for the warm-up (`register`), so the fight draws\n * with 0 pipelines built after it.\n *\n * Invariants: presentation only: it reads entities, the trace and the puppets' trails, and never writes the sim;\n * randomness comes from the visual streams it is given (`fxRng`: the world's, never hashed); `reset()` forgets\n * what runs and the trace read, for a new world only: a restore or a dev action keeps the world, whose trace is\n * history and never restored, so reading it again would play its events twice (engine/app/view.ts `restarted`).\n *\n * @example\n * // const fx = createStageFx({ registry, trails: () => actors.trails() });\n * // stage.scene.add(fx.effects.root);\n * // fx.capture(entities); fx.draw(0.5); fx.frame(dt, camera, world.events.trace());\n * @see engine/gfx/stageFx.test.ts\n */\n\n=== engine/gfx/puppets/actors.ts\n/**\n * @file Actors on the stage (PLAN.md WP 3.10, §6.4's view; I-21): every actor with an animator (engine/sim/actors.ts:\n * an entity with the components `actor` and `animator`) drawn as a puppet (engine/gfx/puppets/draw.ts) of the neutral\n * humanoid (`ACTOR_BODY`) or the body its component `puppet` names (`body:mannequin`, WP 8.9), in its animator's build,\n * posed every frame by its animator's presentation half (engine/anim/character.ts `pose`) at the frame's alpha; an\n * actor with clips (`clips`, engine/sim/actorClips.ts) has its clip layer laid over the body, loaded from the same data\n * (a `ClipLayerPool` of the view's own, engine/anim/clip/clipsets.ts). The stage (engine/gfx/stage.ts) draws these.\n *\n * `capture(entities, dt, queries)` after each sim step keeps each actor's last two places (feet and heading) and its\n * animator's data; `draw(alpha)` poses each puppet `alpha` of the way from the one before to the last. `player()` is\n * the first player actor (in id order) as the last draw put it: its feet and, with a puppet, its skeleton, world pose\n * and eye (the head socket, engine/gfx/cameras/first.ts's `eyePoint`), which the cameras follow (engine/app/view.ts).\n * `firstPerson(frame)` draws the player for a first-person camera's frame (engine/gfx/viewmodel/body.ts, WP 13.12:\n * his body hidden, its shadow kept, his arms posed against it by a lens of their own), or whole for null. `trails()` is\n * each puppet's trail as its last pose sampled it (WP 6.7, oldest first), which the stage's effects draw as ribbons.\n * WP 13.20: the weapon an actor has out stands in its right hand while its hold holds a gun (`carried`, `muzzle`).\n * WP 10.2: a `ragdoll` (engine/sim/ragdolls.ts) lays its parts on the bones, faded in and out (`layRagdoll`).\n *\n * WP 6.2 in the box (WP 7.8): an actor's `reactions` (engine/sim/reactions.ts) are a `Reactions` layer on its puppet's\n * animator, loaded at every pose (its flinch bends its spine; a body down on its face is drawn so), its `actions` (WP\n * 13.11, engine/sim/actorActions.ts) an `Actions` layer on its clip layer, its `secondary` a `Secondary` layer whose\n * chains hang under the puppet (engine/gfx/puppets/chains.ts: `actor#<id>/cape`…), and its `post` slot ends with a\n * `FootPlant` (engine/anim/footPlant.ts) on the ground the sim's `queries` find, faded out as far as its clips hold its\n * legs (clipsets.ts `legsHeld`). WP 13.10: an actor's movement (`motion`) shows on its body (motion.ts `MovementPose`)\n * and locks its feet as `plantsFeet` lets it, laid as the feel kit's (anim/bodyPlants.ts); its layers: actorLayers.ts.\n *\n * Invariants: presentation only (doctrine: WebGPU only): its animators and their layers are its own, loaded from the\n * sim's data at every pose and never writing it, so drawing, culling or not drawing never changes the hash (the\n * animator's own invariant, engine/anim/character.test.ts); one puppet per actor, its layers made again when its\n * animator or their components do; every object it draws is under `root`, and a puppet given up waits as a spare for\n * the next actor of its build and body (`createActorPuppets` says why). A puppet is a skinned mesh of two draw calls:\n * right for heroes and a few foes; crowds draw through instanced batches (WP 5.4).\n *\n * @example\n * // const actors = createActorPuppets({ materials: library }); stage.scene.add(actors.root);\n * // const drawn = actors.capture(world.query('actor'), world.dt); // the ids drawn as puppets\n * // actors.draw(0.5);\n * // actors.player()?.eye; // where a first-person camera sits\n * @see engine/gfx/puppets/actors.test.ts\n */\n\n=== engine/sim/crowdBodies.ts\n/**\n * @file Crowd bodies, sim-side (PLAN.md WP 5.7 core proposal, ADR-0008 amendment 6; §6.4; ADR-0009): what a member of\n * a crowd looks like, and its rig's step. An entity with the component `crowdBody` (`CROWD_BODY_FIELDS`) names its rig\n * (a humanoid in a build, a blob, a floater, a quadruped), where it stands and the rig's state as plain data; the\n * stage draws it\n * through a crowd (engine/gfx/stageCrowd.ts: instanced batches, each body posed at its band's detail), instead of a\n * stand-in.\n *\n * `stepCrowdBody(w, id, body, input)` is the rig's sim step (ADR-0009's `anim.step`: every tick, part of the hash),\n * for a system in the phase `anim`: it loads the rig from `body.state`, steps it with `input` and saves it back, and\n * moves the body to `input.at`. A humanoid's is its animator's (engine/anim/character.ts: the body states, its\n * breathing phase drawn from `rng.entity(id, 'anim')` at its first step, as an actor's); a blob's and a floater's are\n * theirs (engine/anim/blob.ts, floater.ts), the floater's clock spread from the same stream; a quadruped's is its own\n * (engine/anim/quadruped.ts, WP 13.21: its clock spread so, its feet on the world's ground where the world has\n * physics, a raycast through the group `world`, `crowdGround`). The first step fills an\n * empty `state` (a spawned body's default) with the rig at rest, turned to `body.yaw`. The rigs are pooled per world\n * and loaded at every step, so they keep no state of their own: a restore continues exactly.\n *\n * - `rig`: `humanoid` (its `look` is a build id, `build:chibi` when empty), `blob` (its `look` names its features:\n *   `horns`, `ears` or `wings`, none when empty; `size` its radius at rest, `BLOB.radius` when 0), `floater` or\n *   `quadruped` (told `input.quadruped`: to sit, what to look at and how hard to wag).\n * - `x`, `y`, `z` (m): a humanoid's, a blob's or a quadruped's feet, a floater's core; `yaw` (rad): where it faces\n *   (a humanoid's from `input.yaw`, a blob's look, a floater's and a quadruped's heading from their rigs).\n *\n * Invariants: everything a crowd body is in the sim is its component; the step writes only the component; footsteps\n * are not emitted (a crowd's would flood the events). The view poses rigs it loads from the component and never\n * writes it, so drawing, LOD and culling never change the hash.\n *\n * @example\n * import { createWorld } from './world';\n * const w = createWorld({ seed: 1 });\n * const id = w.spawn({ crowdBody: { rig: 'blob', x: 2, z: 3 } });\n * const body = w.get(id)!.crowdBody as CrowdBody;\n * w.run((w) => stepCrowdBody(w, id, body, { at: [2, 0, 3.05], velocity: [0, 0, 3] })); // a slime hopping south\n * [body.z, body.yaw]; // [3.05, 0]: moved, looking south\n * (body.state as { squash: number }).squash; // 0: the blob's state, at rest\n * @see engine/sim/crowdBodies.test.ts\n */\n\n=== engine/gfx/stageCrowd.ts\n/**\n * @file Crowd bodies on the stage (PLAN.md WP 5.7 core proposal, ADR-0008 amendment 6; §6.4's view; I-21): every\n * entity with the component `crowdBody` (engine/sim/crowdBodies.ts: a humanoid, blob, floater or quadruped rig, where it stands\n * and its rig's state) drawn through a crowd (engine/gfx/puppets/crowd.ts: instanced batches, a few dozen draw calls\n * for thousands), seen through the crowd's level of detail (engine/gfx/puppets/lod.ts) from the frame's camera. The\n * stage (engine/gfx/stage.ts) draws these instead of stand-ins.\n *\n * `capture(entities, dt)` after each sim step keeps each crowd body's last two places (where it stands and faces) and\n * its component, and returns the ids it draws. `draw(alpha, camera)`, once the frame's camera is placed, puts each\n * body `alpha` of the way from its place a step ago to its last and asks the crowd whether the camera sees it: only a\n * seen body is posed (the view's half of its rig, loaded from the component: a humanoid's animator at its band's\n * detail, `animator.pose({ lod })`; a blob, a floater or a quadruped from its state alone) and drawn, a blob shadow\n * under each humanoid, blob and quadruped on the level's floor. Humanoids wear the neutral humanoid (`body:humanoid`)\n * in their build, blobs `BLOB_BODY` with their features (`blobBody`), floaters `FLOATER_BODY`, quadrupeds\n * `QUADRUPED_BODY` (the dog).\n *\n * The crowd is made when the first crowd body arrives, and added to the stage's scene then: a stage with none has\n * none, and its scene graph is the one it had before. Each look is prepared (its batches made) when the first body\n * wearing it arrives; `register` registers the crowd's batches, present and future, with the warm-up and adds the\n * prepared looks to the shader key, so the frame after a new look arrives warms up first instead of stalling, and a\n * crowd growing in a look it has already built builds no pipeline (its new pages share their batch's shader).\n * Given the renderer's features with `feature:gpuCrowds` on (engine/gfx/features.ts `gpuCrowdsFor`, WP 11.4),\n * `register` makes the crowd again, drawn through a GPU crowd (engine/gfx/enhanced/crowds.ts) sized for the bodies held\n * then; a frame that outgrows it makes it again twice as large and draws again, its size in the shader key, so the\n * renderer warms up before the larger one draws. Headless, or with the feature off, the instancing service draws.\n *\n * Invariants: presentation only (doctrine: WebGPU only): it reads the components and writes nothing back; its rigs\n * are its own, loaded from the component at every pose, so drawing, LOD, culling or not drawing never changes the\n * hash; every object it makes is under the crowd's root.\n *\n * @example\n * // const crowd = createStageCrowd({ scene: stage.scene, materials: library, level });\n * // const drawn = crowd.capture(world.query('crowdBody'), world.dt); // the ids drawn as crowd bodies\n * // crowd.draw(0.5, camera); // halfway between the last two steps, as the camera sees them\n * @see engine/gfx/stageCrowd.test.ts\n */\n\n=== engine/gfx/level/cutaway.ts\nawk: fatal: cannot open file `engine/gfx/level/cutaway.ts' for reading: No such file or directory\n\nengine/audio:\napi.ts\ndata\ndsp\nruntime\n\nengine/gfx:\natmosphere.ts\nbackdrop.ts\ncameras\ncaps.ts\ncutaway.ts\ndaylight.ts\nenhanced\nfeatures.ts\nfx\ngeometry\nidmarks.ts\nidpass.ts\ninstanceSync.ts\ninstancing.ts\nlevel\nlights.ts\nlookMetrics.ts\nmaterials\npipelines.ts\npost\npropLooks.ts\nprops.ts\npuppets\nquality.ts\nrenderer.ts\nresolution.ts\nsceneDump.ts\nshadows.ts\nshot.ts\nsky.ts\nskyKind.ts\nstage.ts\nstageCrowd.ts\nstageFx.ts\nstageGround.ts\nstageProps.ts\nstageRides.ts\nstageShells.ts\nstageSite.ts\nstageSky.ts\nstandIns.ts\nstoreyCut.ts\nterrain.ts\nterrainSplat.ts\ntextures\nthumbnail.ts\nviewmodel\nwarmup.ts\nweapons.ts\n\nengine/gfx/fx:\ndecals.ts\neffects.ts\nemitters.ts\nparticles.ts\npayload.ts\npresets.ts\nribbons.ts\nrings.ts\nshake.ts\nsprites.ts\n\nengine/gfx/level:\nbrazier.ts\ncells.ts\ndais.ts\nfaces.ts\nflights.ts\nmeshes.ts\nopenings.ts\nramp.ts\nrecipes.ts\nroofs.ts\nruns.ts\nshapes.ts\nslab.ts\nslabs.ts\nstairs.ts\nsurface.ts\nwalls.ts\n\nengine/ui:\nchrome.ts\ndialog.ts\nlabels.ts\nmanifest.webmanifest\nmenu.ts\noverlay.ts\nstate.ts\nswipe.ts\ntouch.css\ntouch.ts\nwidgets.ts","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01BTmEX1q3zxauuQnqtUhnQX","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
