{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjADQWk3QHJkUNZKRQHc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HqYw9sPohdgts2zH9RB9tz","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"sed -n 1,80p labs/box/cast/walker.ts | cut -c1-170; echo ======; grep -n \"body\\|look\\|material\\|defineBody\\|recolor\\|slots\" engine/gfx/puppets/crowd.ts | head -50 | cut -c1-170; echo =====; sed -n 1,50p engine/anim/skeleton/builds.ts 2>/dev/null | cut -c1-170; ls engine/anim engine/gfx/puppets | head -60","description":"See how crowd walkers and body looks are defined"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":19390,"cache_read_input_tokens":256370,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":19390},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b0d0401-1a79-4c2f-8a33-ba9239fdbfed","uuid":"4c1cd7f1-3f43-48c4-a2d4-cf5edd8a5e1c","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:35:48.682Z","request_id":"req_011CgjADQFso7z3rKNA3Ek1f","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01HqYw9sPohdgts2zH9RB9tz":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211947__x8ab6bc/work/.research/proto && sed -n 1,80p labs/box/cast/walker.ts | cut -c1-170; echo ======; grep -n \"body\\|look\\|material\\|defineBody\\|recolor\\|slots\" engine/gfx/puppets/crowd.ts | head -50 | cut -c1-170; echo =====; sed -n 1,50p engine/anim/skeleton/builds.ts 2>/dev/null | cut -c1-170; ls engine/anim engine/gfx/puppets | head -60","description":"See how crowd walkers and body looks are defined"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01HqYw9sPohdgts2zH9RB9tz":{"cwd":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211947__x8ab6bc/work/.research/proto"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HqYw9sPohdgts2zH9RB9tz","type":"tool_result","content":"/**\n * @file The box's walker (PLAN.md §9.0, WP 5.7): the crowd's foot soldier from Box 4 on, a capsule that walks after\n * the hero. `WALKER` holds its numbers, `CROWD_WALKER` its own component (`crowdWalker`: its speed, heading and sway\n * phase, beside the crowd agent the scene keeps), `makeWalker` draws one, and `steerWalker` gives the velocity it\n * wants each step, for `setVelocity` (engine/physics/crowd.ts), whose acceleration limit and the solver do the rest.\n * `Chase` is what every member of the cast steers by (the slime and the wisp take it too).\n *\n * Its steering, the prototype's swarm: level with the hero (within `WALKER.level` of his height) it waits on a ring\n * round him (`approachRing`): in by the flow field from beyond it, backing off inside it, drifting round it on it as\n * its sway turns; anywhere else (on the floor below his gallery, on the stairs) it follows the flow field toward his\n * tile (`followFlow`), up the stairs when he is up. It faces where it walks, turning at `WALKER.turn`, and him while\n * it waits.\n *\n * Its numbers are the stress test's husk walker (`my-3d2dge:src/stress-world/20-sim.js:73-74, 196-199, 371-385`), in\n * SI units (PLAN.md Appendix C: 16 units a metre), as starting values (§9.0: similar, not identical):\n * - the capsule: radius 5 units → 0.3125 m, a straight middle of 16 → 1 m (the crowd agent's own make), 1.625 m tall;\n * - walking at 28 units/s plus up to 12 more, drawn per walker → 1.75 to 2.5 m/s, at 500 units/s² (the agent's\n *   31.25 m/s²);\n * - the ring: the hero's reach plus 10 units → 1.5 m, a band of 3 units either side, backing off at half speed and\n *   drifting round at 0.4 of it, the sway's phase drawn per walker at 0.9 rad/s; level within 14 units → 0.875 m;\n * - turning at 5 rad/s.\n *\n * Its attack (Box 5, WP 6.7): `WALKER_ATTACK`. Waiting on its ring, cooled down and granted one of the hero's attack\n * tokens (engine/world/ai.ts), it winds one of its fists' moves up (`moves`, drawn per swing; the prototype's husk's\n * claw, haymaker and hook), its wind-up at least `wind` s and twice the move's, its recovery `recover` s longer. While\n * it winds it turns to him at `turn` rad/s and walks to `stand` m from him, its arc telegraph (`telegraph:boxSwing`)\n * filling on the floor before it; as it strikes it lunges in when he stepped back, and what the arc holds as its hit\n * window opens is hit: `damage` hit points. Then it gives the token back and cools down for `cool` s plus up to\n * `coolSpread`. A hit on it breaks its swing off. It has `health` hit points.\n *\n * Its body is drawn as the neutral humanoid (a crowd body, engine/sim/crowdBodies.ts) in one of `WALKER.looks`: the\n * prototype's mixed husks, knights and skeletons, as builds.\n *\n * Game code, sim-side: it imports only engine/sim-api.ts.\n *\n * @example\n * WALKER.speed.min; // 1.75: m/s\n * // const out = steerWalker(agent, walker, chase, new Vector3()); setVelocity(physics, agent, out, w);\n * @see labs/box/cast/crowd.test.ts\n */\nimport {\n  approachAng,\n  approachRing,\n  defineComponent,\n  defineTelegraph,\n  followFlow,\n  type CrowdAgent,\n  type FlowField,\n  type Rng,\n  type SteerPoint,\n  type Vector3,\n} from '../../../engine/sim-api';\n\n/** The prototype's units per metre (PLAN.md Appendix C). */\nconst UNITS = 16;\n\n/** The walker's numbers (see the file comment). */\nexport const WALKER = Object.freeze({\n  /** Its body: the crowd agent's capsule (CROWD_AGENT's own radius and straight middle, m). */\n  agent: Object.freeze({ shape: 'capsule', radius: 5 / UNITS, height: 16 / UNITS } as const),\n  /** Its walking speed (m/s): `min` plus up to `spread`, drawn per walker. */\n  speed: Object.freeze({ min: 28 / UNITS, spread: 12 / UNITS }),\n  /** The ring it waits on round the hero (m), and its band either side (m). */\n  ring: Object.freeze({ radius: 1.5, band: 3 / UNITS }),\n  /** Within this height of the hero (m) it is level with him and waits on the ring. */\n  level: 14 / UNITS,\n  /** Its sway's rate (rad/s): how fast it drifts one way round the ring, then the other. */\n  sway: 0.9,\n  /** How fast it turns to face where it goes (rad/s). */\n  turn: 5,\n  /** The builds it is drawn in, one drawn per walker: the prototype's mixed skins (husk, knight, skeleton) and more. */\n  looks: Object.freeze(['build:chibi', 'build:heroic', 'build:bulky', 'build:skeleton']),\n});\n\n/** The walker's own state, beside its crowd agent. */\nexport interface WalkerData {\n  speed: number;\n  yaw: number;\n  sway: number;\n}\n======\n3: * service (engine/gfx/instancing.ts). `createCrowd({ materials })` holds the batches and a level of detail\n4: * (engine/gfx/puppets/lod.ts); each frame, for each body, `see` first, and pose and draw only what it returns a band\n6: * - `humanoid(compiled, pose, { band })`: a compiled body (compile.ts) in a pose from its animator, posed at the\n10: *   posed from its state alone and drawn in its body (bodies/blob.ts, bodies/floater.ts; `BLOB_BODY` and\n11: *   `FLOATER_BODY` by default), alike in every band (a rig's pose is a few matrices); `rig(body, joints)` draws any\n12: *   rig body on any joints;\n15: * A rig body (`RigBody`, rigBody.ts) is data: its slots, and its parts, each a unit shape on one joint of the rig's\n19: * The cost: a draw call per shown page of each batch (a shape and a material: the puppets' `crowd/puppets/<shape>`,\n26: * bodies before the warm-up so every batch's first page is compiled then. A rig body's problems throw\n30: * drawn, a blob shadow under every body but a wisp, shared batches per shape).\n33: * // const crowd = createCrowd({ materials: library }); crowd.prepare(compiled, BLOB_BODY); scene.add(crowd.root);\n64:    template: 'rig body {body}, part {part}: {problem}',\n66:    doc: 'Raised by `createCrowd` (engine/gfx/puppets/crowd.ts) for a rig body whose part has an unknown shape, a slot the body lacks, a size that is not positive, or \n76:/** How a body is drawn: its band (full detail when absent) and the floor under it, for a blob shadow. */\n82:/** How a rig is drawn: also its flags (`when`, `unless`) and its scale against its body. */\n117:  /** The rigs' batches, by shape (with `~<material>` for a part's own material). */\n124:  /** The band a body with this bounding sphere is drawn in, or null when it is not drawn (lod.ts). */\n126:  /** Draws a humanoid's compiled body in `pose`; returns the instances written. */\n128:  /** Poses a blob rig and draws it in `body` (`BLOB_BODY`), flagged by its state, scaled by its radius. */\n129:  blob(blob: Blob, options?: CrowdDraw & { body?: RigBody }): number;\n130:  /** Poses a floater rig and draws it in `body` (`FLOATER_BODY`). */\n131:  floater(floater: Floater, options?: CrowdDraw & { body?: RigBody }): number;\n132:  /** Draws `body` on `joints`. Throws `GFX_RIG_BODY`. */\n133:  rig(body: RigBody, joints: RigJoints, options?: CrowdRigDraw): number;\n163:  materials: PuppetMaterials;\n179:  const puppets = createPuppetBatches({ materials: options.materials, name: `${name}/puppets`, pageSlots, batches });\n180:  /** The bodies' part for post-processing: characters, one outline group, so no line falls between a body's batches. */\n186:      : createBlobShadows({ materials: options.materials, name: `${name}/shadows`, pageSlots, batches });\n193:  /** The rigs' batch of `shape` drawn with material `id`, made on first use. */\n198:      const material = options.materials.get(id);\n203:        material,\n215:  /** `body`'s parts made ready to draw, once per body. Throws `GFX_RIG_BODY`. */\n216:  const compileRig = (body: RigBody): readonly RigPiece[] => {\n217:    let pieces = compiledRigs.get(body);\n219:    pieces = body.parts.map((part, i) => {\n221:        codeError('GFX_RIG_BODY', { body: body.name, part: i, problem, fix });\n223:      if (!Object.hasOwn(body.slots, part.slot)) throw fail(`slot ${part.slot} is not in slots`, 'add it to slots');\n227:      const id = part.material ?? (glow ? body.glowMaterial : body.material);\n228:      const fallback = glow ? 'material:puppetGlow' : 'material:puppet';\n229:      const batch = batchOf(part.shape, id ?? fallback, !glow && !part.material, part.material !== undefined);\n233:      return { part, batch, color: toLinear(body.slots[part.slot]), at, local };\n235:    compiledRigs.set(body, pieces);\n271:      for (const body of list) {\n272:        if ('skeleton' in body) puppets.prepare(body);\n273:        else compileRig(body);\n301:      return crowd.rig(draw.body ?? BLOB_BODY, blob.pose(), blobDraw);\n306:      return crowd.rig(draw.body ?? FLOATER_BODY, floaterJoints, draw);\n308:    rig(body, joints, draw = {}) {\n312:      for (const piece of compileRig(body)) {\n317:          const index = body.parts.indexOf(piece.part);\n=====\nengine/anim:\n__snapshots__\nactions-check.ts\nactions-data.ts\nactions.ts\napi.ts\nattack.ts\nauthoring.ts\nblob.ts\nbodyPlants.ts\nbuilds.ts\nchain.ts\ncharacter.ts\ncheck.ts\nclip\nfk.ts\nfloater.ts\nfootPlant.ts\nfootRoll.ts\nhumanoid.ts\nhumanoidRates.ts\nik.ts\nlocomotion\nlocomotion.ts\nmotionMetrics.ts\nmoves-data.ts\nmoves.ts\npose.ts\nposeNames.ts\nposes.ts\nproc\nquadruped.ts\nragdoll.ts\nreactions.ts\nsecondary.ts\nsheet.ts\nskeleton.ts\nstateMatrix.ts\nstates.ts\nstrike.ts\ntimeline.ts\ntraversal\nweights.ts\n\nengine/gfx/puppets:\nactorLayers.ts\nactors.ts\nbatches.ts\nblobShadow.ts\nbodies\nchains.ts\ncompile.ts\ncrowd.ts\ndraw.ts\ngrammar.ts\nlod.ts\nrigBody.ts","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b0d0401-1a79-4c2f-8a33-ba9239fdbfed","uuid":"1c2c53a3-18a5-4fb1-811a-9fa3fddb2304","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:35:48.708Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"/**\n * @file The box's walker (PLAN.md §9.0, WP 5.7): the crowd's foot soldier from Box 4 on, a capsule that walks after\n * the hero. `WALKER` holds its numbers, `CROWD_WALKER` its own component (`crowdWalker`: its speed, heading and sway\n * phase, beside the crowd agent the scene keeps), `makeWalker` draws one, and `steerWalker` gives the velocity it\n * wants each step, for `setVelocity` (engine/physics/crowd.ts), whose acceleration limit and the solver do the rest.\n * `Chase` is what every member of the cast steers by (the slime and the wisp take it too).\n *\n * Its steering, the prototype's swarm: level with the hero (within `WALKER.level` of his height) it waits on a ring\n * round him (`approachRing`): in by the flow field from beyond it, backing off inside it, drifting round it on it as\n * its sway turns; anywhere else (on the floor below his gallery, on the stairs) it follows the flow field toward his\n * tile (`followFlow`), up the stairs when he is up. It faces where it walks, turning at `WALKER.turn`, and him while\n * it waits.\n *\n * Its numbers are the stress test's husk walker (`my-3d2dge:src/stress-world/20-sim.js:73-74, 196-199, 371-385`), in\n * SI units (PLAN.md Appendix C: 16 units a metre), as starting values (§9.0: similar, not identical):\n * - the capsule: radius 5 units → 0.3125 m, a straight middle of 16 → 1 m (the crowd agent's own make), 1.625 m tall;\n * - walking at 28 units/s plus up to 12 more, drawn per walker → 1.75 to 2.5 m/s, at 500 units/s² (the agent's\n *   31.25 m/s²);\n * - the ring: the hero's reach plus 10 units → 1.5 m, a band of 3 units either side, backing off at half speed and\n *   drifting round at 0.4 of it, the sway's phase drawn per walker at 0.9 rad/s; level within 14 units → 0.875 m;\n * - turning at 5 rad/s.\n *\n * Its attack (Box 5, WP 6.7): `WALKER_ATTACK`. Waiting on its ring, cooled down and granted one of the hero's attack\n * tokens (engine/world/ai.ts), it winds one of its fists' moves up (`moves`, drawn per swing; the prototype's husk's\n * claw, haymaker and hook), its wind-up at least `wind` s and twice the move's, its recovery `recover` s longer. While\n * it winds it turns to him at `turn` rad/s and walks to `stand` m from him, its arc telegraph (`telegraph:boxSwing`)\n * filling on the floor before it; as it strikes it lunges in when he stepped back, and what the arc holds as its hit\n * window opens is hit: `damage` hit points. Then it gives the token back and cools down for `cool` s plus up to\n * `coolSpread`. A hit on it breaks its swing off. It has `health` hit points.\n *\n * Its body is drawn as the neutral humanoid (a crowd body, engine/sim/crowdBodies.ts) in one of `WALKER.looks`: the\n * prototype's mixed husks, knights and skeletons, as builds.\n *\n * Game code, sim-side: it imports only engine/sim-api.ts.\n *\n * @example\n * WALKER.speed.min; // 1.75: m/s\n * // const out = steerWalker(agent, walker, chase, new Vector3()); setVelocity(physics, agent, out, w);\n * @see labs/box/cast/crowd.test.ts\n */\nimport {\n  approachAng,\n  approachRing,\n  defineComponent,\n  defineTelegraph,\n  followFlow,\n  type CrowdAgent,\n  type FlowField,\n  type Rng,\n  type SteerPoint,\n  type Vector3,\n} from '../../../engine/sim-api';\n\n/** The prototype's units per metre (PLAN.md Appendix C). */\nconst UNITS = 16;\n\n/** The walker's numbers (see the file comment). */\nexport const WALKER = Object.freeze({\n  /** Its body: the crowd agent's capsule (CROWD_AGENT's own radius and straight middle, m). */\n  agent: Object.freeze({ shape: 'capsule', radius: 5 / UNITS, height: 16 / UNITS } as const),\n  /** Its walking speed (m/s): `min` plus up to `spread`, drawn per walker. */\n  speed: Object.freeze({ min: 28 / UNITS, spread: 12 / UNITS }),\n  /** The ring it waits on round the hero (m), and its band either side (m). */\n  ring: Object.freeze({ radius: 1.5, band: 3 / UNITS }),\n  /** Within this height of the hero (m) it is level with him and waits on the ring. */\n  level: 14 / UNITS,\n  /** Its sway's rate (rad/s): how fast it drifts one way round the ring, then the other. */\n  sway: 0.9,\n  /** How fast it turns to face where it goes (rad/s). */\n  turn: 5,\n  /** The builds it is drawn in, one drawn per walker: the prototype's mixed skins (husk, knight, skeleton) and more. */\n  looks: Object.freeze(['build:chibi', 'build:heroic', 'build:bulky', 'build:skeleton']),\n});\n\n/** The walker's own state, beside its crowd agent. */\nexport interface WalkerData {\n  speed: number;\n  yaw: number;\n  sway: number;\n}\n======\n3: * service (engine/gfx/instancing.ts). `createCrowd({ materials })` holds the batches and a level of detail\n4: * (engine/gfx/puppets/lod.ts); each frame, for each body, `see` first, and pose and draw only what it returns a band\n6: * - `humanoid(compiled, pose, { band })`: a compiled body (compile.ts) in a pose from its animator, posed at the\n10: *   posed from its state alone and drawn in its body (bodies/blob.ts, bodies/floater.ts; `BLOB_BODY` and\n11: *   `FLOATER_BODY` by default), alike in every band (a rig's pose is a few matrices); `rig(body, joints)` draws any\n12: *   rig body on any joints;\n15: * A rig body (`RigBody`, rigBody.ts) is data: its slots, and its parts, each a unit shape on one joint of the rig's\n19: * The cost: a draw call per shown page of each batch (a shape and a material: the puppets' `crowd/puppets/<shape>`,\n26: * bodies before the warm-up so every batch's first page is compiled then. A rig body's problems throw\n30: * drawn, a blob shadow under every body but a wisp, shared batches per shape).\n33: * // const crowd = createCrowd({ materials: library }); crowd.prepare(compiled, BLOB_BODY); scene.add(crowd.root);\n64:    template: 'rig body {body}, part {part}: {problem}',\n66:    doc: 'Raised by `createCrowd` (engine/gfx/puppets/crowd.ts) for a rig body whose part has an unknown shape, a slot the body lacks, a size that is not positive, or \n76:/** How a body is drawn: its band (full detail when absent) and the floor under it, for a blob shadow. */\n82:/** How a rig is drawn: also its flags (`when`, `unle