{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JKf445vcxg4zkqEtmgEWxS","type":"tool_result","content":"23: * components (the sim's animators are loaded from them). Despawning leaves the body; `removeActor` removes both.\n24- * Carried from shardfall@fa2dab6 (`pavilion-lite/src/character.rs:179-399`: the order of a step, the events).\n25- * @example\n26- * import { createCharacter } from '../physics/character';\n--\n110:/** The components this module reads: `actor`, `animator`, `puppet`, `motion` (the shooter model's) and `oneWay`. */\n111-export type ActorComponents = {\n112-  actor: ActorComponent;\n113-  animator: AnimatorComponent;\n--\n139: * Declares the components `actor`, `animator`, `puppet`, `clips` (engine/sim/actorClips.ts), `oneWay`, `reactions` and\n140- * `secondary` (engine/sim/reactions.ts), the setting `physics.characterGravity` and the controls' `input.sprint` and\n141- * `input.crouch` on `registry`.\n142- */\n--\n195:export interface ActorSpec {\n196-  /** Where its feet go: on the ground below them (it starts just above, outside the skin). */\n197-  at: Vec3Like;\n198-  /** Its settings (createCharacter). */\n--\n213:   * Further components it spawns with, by name (its `reactions`, its `secondary`: engine/sim/reactions.ts), so they\n214-   * are there from its first step, and a page's first warm-up builds what they draw.\n215-   */\n216:  components?: Readonly<Record<string, object>>;\n217-}\n218-\n219-/**\n--\n240:  if (!spec.anim) return w.spawn({ ...spec.components, ...motion, actor });\n241-  if (!w.systems.has('actors.anim')) {\n5: * boundaries, named seeded RNG streams, sim-time timers, and the state, hash, trace, capture and restore of all of\n35: * const w = createWorld<{ position: { x: number } }>({ seed: 1, registry: reg });\n78:    doc: 'Raised by the world (engine/sim/world.ts) for a seed or step rate that is not a number of the right kind, a spawn that is not a\n94:  /** The seed every sim RNG stream deri