{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JnoL1wV8knVp4Djjsw1UMc","type":"tool_result","content":"3737625       02:46 /bin/bash -c source /home/micha/.claude/shell-snapshots/snapshot-bash-1793852391150-860spo.sh 2>/dev\n3737628       02:46 timeout 400 python3 -u scripts-proto/open.py file:///home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-m\n3737629       02:46 python3 -u scripts-proto/open.py file:///home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__\n3: * 3 m high, a grid of pillars 3.5 m high, low walls to jump onto, 30 brazier stands, two galleries 1 m up along the\n7: * stairs' ramps to the galleries and over the dais's slopes, keeps him out of the walls, the pillars and the brazier\n15: * (labs/box/scenes/hall-props.ts).\n45:description: The prototype's hall, 64 × 44 m (my-3d2dge:src/stress-world/10-hall.js:22-67). Walls 3 m, a grid of 3.5 m pillars, low walls to jump onto, 30 braziers with t\n5- * (silhouette layers round the horizon), a sun (a `DirectionalLight` the dome agrees with), the ambient light and fog\n6- * (engine/gfx/atmosphere.ts), and how bright the light pool's point lights shine (engine/gfx/lights.ts). The kind, its\n7: * fields and its presets (`sky:hall`, `sky:daylight`) are engine/gfx/skyKind.ts's.\n8- *\n9- * Switching presets, or showing the hour's sky (engine/gfx/daylight.ts), changes uniforms, colours and visibility\n10- * only: the dome and the backdrop stay in the scene, registered with the warm-up, the sun and the pool's lights are\n11- * made once, and the fog node stays installed. The one exception is who casts shadows (engine/gfx/shadows.ts): a\n12- * preset with a sun gives the sun the first caster, which changes the shader key, so the renderer warms up again\n13- * before the next frame instead of stalling it. Nothing here touches the sim, so no preset changes the hash. A look\n14- * may draw the dome as a clean gradient instead (`gradient`, WP 13.24: the cel look's), a uniform too.\n15- *\n16- * The backdrop is baked on the CPU into one strip (engine/gfx/backdrop.ts `bakeBackdrop`), which wraps three times\n17- * round an open cylinder that follows the camera, its foot just under eye level, drawn first and writing no depth\n18- * like the dome (`atFarPlane`), so the level always stands in front of both. With `feature:cascadedShadows` on, the sun casts through\n19- * cascades that follow the camera (engine/gfx/enhanced/csm.ts, through engine/gfx/features.ts); with tiled lighting,\n20- * the light pool holds 64 lights (engine/gfx/lights.ts). Both come from the renderer's feature report (`features`).\n21- *\n22- * Measured on r182 (WP 7.1): its lights node sorts its lights by id, in place, whenever it builds a shader, while the\n23- * render list gives them in scene order; where the two orders differ the light key flips from frame to frame, and\n24- * every instanced mesh rebuilds its pipelines (each build names its own instance buffer). So `createSky` adds its\n25- * lights in id order (the pool, the ambient light, then the sun), and a light made later belongs after them in the\n26- * scene. And a TSL uniform in the object group (the default) refreshes only when its object or material changes, so\n27- * a still floor keeps its first fog: the dome's knobs and the fog's numbers are render-group uniforms.\n28- *\n29- * Carried from `my-3d2dge:engine/my-3d2dge.js:3859-3958` (§21b: the `day` preset's colours), as a cylinder round a 3D\n--\n34- * // const sky = createSky(scene, { level });\n35- * // sky.register(gfx.warmup);\n36: * // sky.set('sky:hall');\n37- * // sky.update({ camera, focus: hero, time: seconds }); // each frame\n38- * @see engine/gfx/sky.test.ts\n39- * @see tests/e2e/lights.spec.ts\n40- */\n41-import {\n42-  BackSide,\n43-  ClampToEdgeWrapping,\n44-  Color,\n45-  CylinderGeometry,\n46-  DataTexture,\n47-  DirectionalLight,\n48-  LinearFilter,\n49-  Mesh,\n50-  MeshBasicNodeMaterial,\n51-  RepeatWrapping,\n52-  RGBAFormat,\n53-  SphereGeometry,\n54-  SRGBColorSpace,\n55-  UnsignedByteType,\n56-  type Camera,\n57-  type Node,","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b0d0401-1a79-4c2f-8a33-ba9239fdbfed","uuid":"0bc49708-0843-464a-a66c-eadda6a83182","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:51:09.178Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"3737625       02:46 /bin/bash -c source /home/micha/.claude/shell-snapshots/snapshot-bash-1793852391150-860spo.sh 2>/dev\n3737628       02:46 timeout 400 python3 -u scripts-proto/open.py file:///home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-m\n3737629       02:46 python3 -u scripts-proto/open.py file:///home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__\n3: * 3 m high, a grid of pillars 3.5 m high, low walls to jump onto, 30 brazier stands, two galleries 1 m up along the\n7: * stairs' ramps to the galleries and over the dais's slopes, keeps him out of the walls, the pillars and the brazier\n15: * (labs/box/scenes/hall-props.ts).\n45:description: The prototype's hall, 64 × 44 m (my-3d2dge:src/stress-world/10-hall.js:22-67). Walls 3 m, a grid of 3.5 m pillars, low walls to jump onto, 30 braziers with t\n5- * (silhouette layers round the horizon), a sun (a `DirectionalLight` the dome agrees with), the ambient light and fog\n6- * (engine/gfx/atmosphere.ts), and how bright the light pool's point lights shine (engine/gfx/lights.ts). The kind, its\n7: * fields and its presets (`sky:hall`, `sky:daylight`) are engine/gfx/skyKind.ts's.\n8- *\n9- * Switching presets, or showing the hour's sky (engine/gfx/daylight.ts), changes uniforms, colours and visibility\n10- * only: the dome and the backdrop stay in the scene, registered with the warm-up, the sun and the pool's lights are\n11- * made once, and the fog node stays installed. The one exception is who casts shadows (engine/gfx/shadows.ts): a\n12- * preset with a sun gives the sun the first caster, which changes the shader key, so the renderer warms up again\n13- * before the next frame instead of stalling it. Nothing here