{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0135Qr8BsGgjAZuMVnAjVuba","type":"tool_result","content":"/**\n * @file The fight's rules, Box 5 (PLAN.md §9.0, WP 6.7): what labs/box/scenes/fight.ts and its systems\n * (fight-hero.ts, fight-foes.ts) share. Its components, its setting, its events, and the two ways a blow lands:\n * `strikeFoe` (the hero's hit or bolt on a member of the crowd) and `hurtHero` (a foe's on him), each through the\n * engine's `damage` (engine/sim/damage.ts: hit points, the push as momentum, the throw, the corpse group, the\n * hit-stop and the event `damage` the page draws its damage numbers from).\n *\n * - **Components**: `fightHealth` (`HEALTH_FIELDS`) on the hero and every foe; `fightHero` (his combo and thrust as\n *   their saved states, and his counters in ticks); `fightFoe` (where a foe is in its attack and its timers);\n *   `fightTelegraph` (a foe's telegraph where it stands, a `TelegraphPlace` as plain data: none while `telegraph` is\n *   empty); `fightShot` (a bolt in flight, `PROJECTILE_FIELDS` and the hit points it takes); `fightTokens`\n *   (`ATTACK_TOKENS_FIELDS`, on the hero: who may attack him now).\n * - **Events**, for the page's effects (engine/gfx/fx: emitters answer them by type): `hit` where a blow lands,\n *   `slain` where a body falls, `shot` where a bolt leaves, `slam` where a pounce lands, each with its `position`\n *   and `size`. They change nothing in the sim.\n * - **The setting** `box.fight.god` (fight.ts; true, read when the scene starts, as the prototype's proof ran): foes'\n *   blows still flinch and push the hero, but take no hit points. Off, they do; at none he falls (`slain`) and is up again\n *   at once with all of them: the box has no end to its fight.\n *\n * A blow on a foe breaks its attack off (`breakAttack`: its token back, its telegraph gone) and stuns it for\n * `STUN` s; one that kills it lets it fall with the kill's throw (`HERO_FIGHT.kill`), a body the crowd walks through\n * that the crowd's step removes later.\n *\n * Reactions (WP 6.2 in the box, WP 7.8): every blow on the hero or a walker goes through the body's reactions (the\n * component `reactions`, engine/sim/reactions.ts `reactTo`): it flinches along the push (`HERO_FIGHT.react`), a big\n * blow knocks a walker down (it lies, then gets up the way it lies: `knockedDown` holds while it does, and the foe\n * acts on nothing meanwhile), and a killing one plays its death. The hero's are stepped by the actors' system and drawn\n * by his puppet (his flinch bends his spine); a walker's by fight-foes.ts's rigs, what they tell its body (`down`, a\n * pose) laid over its states. Slimes and wisps are not humanoids: they have none.\n *\n * Game code, sim-side: it imports only engine/sim-api.ts and the box's own files.\n *\n * @see labs/box/scenes/fight.test.ts\n */\nimport {\n  ATTACK_TOKENS_FIELDS,\n  Attack,\n  Combo,\n  HEALTH_FIELDS,\n  PROJECTILE_FIELDS,\n  SpatialHash,\n  Vector3,\n  damage,\n  defineComponent,\n  reactTo,\n  releaseToken,\n  type ActorComponent,\n  type AnimatorComponent,\n  type AttackState,\n  type AttackTokens,\n  type ComboState,\n  type DamageEvents,\n  type Health,\n  type HurtSet,\n  type Projectile,\n  type ReactionComponents,\n  type ReactionState,\n  type World,\n} from '../../../engine/sim-api';\nimport { HERO, HERO_FIGHT, type HeroHit } from '../cast/hero';\nimport type { CrowdComponents } from './crowd-1000';\n\n/** How long a blow stuns a foe (s): it steers and attacks again after. The prototype's. */\nexport const STUN = 0.22;\n\n/** The hero's combo, as `HERO_FIGHT` says (an idle one; its state is `fightHero.combo`). */\nexport const heroCombo = () => new Combo([...HERO_FIGHT.combo], { window: HERO_FIGHT.window });\n/** The hero's thrust out of a dash (an idle one; its state is `fightHero.thrust`). */\nexport const heroThrust = () => new Attack(HERO_FIGHT.thrust);\nconst IDLE_COMBO: ComboState = heroCombo().save();\n....\n180- * takes no hit: null, nothing changed.\n181- */\n182:export function damage<C extends object, E extends EventMap>(\n183-  world: World<C, E>,\n184-  target: DamageTarget,\n185-  hit: HitSpec,\n186-): DamageEvent | null {\n187-  const w = world as unknown as World<object, DamageEvents>;\n188-  check(\n/**\n * @file Damage (PLAN.md WP 6.3, §6.4): what a hit does once the rules have decided it, generic and without formulas,\n * stats or balance: `damage(w, target, hit)` takes `hit.amount` from the target's health, pushes its crowd body\n * away from the blow as momentum the solver carries on, throws it up, kills it into the corpse group with the kill\n * launch, asks for a hit-stop and emits the event `damage` for the view (numbers, sparks, sounds). How much a hit\n * takes and how hard it pushes are the game's numbers, passed in.\n *\n * - **Health**: the game keeps it in a component (`HEALTH_FIELDS`): hit points, and when and by whom it was last hit,\n *   which flinches, stuns and flashes read (`w.tick - health.hitAt`). At 0 or below it is dead.\n * - **Bodies**: a crowd agent's (engine/physics/crowd.ts): `knockback` adds the push the same for every mass and the\n *   solver carries it into the crowd; `launch` throws it up; `killAgent` moves it to the group `corpse`, which the\n *   crowd walks through, and `updateCrowd` removes it later.\n * - **Hit-stop**: a sim decision the frame clock carries out (engine/core/time.ts). `requestHitStop` keeps the longest\n *   stop asked in the step (they never add up); the run's host takes it after the step (`takeHitStop`) for\n *   `clock.hitStop`, whose leaky budget shrinks stops that follow closely, so a crowd hit stops time once however many\n *   it strikes. The clock is outside the hash: a stop changes how many steps a frame runs, never what a step does.\n *\n * Invariants: a dead or absent target (health at 0 or below, a body no longer `alive`), or an entity holding the\n * component `invulnerable` (god mode: engine/sim/devActions.ts), takes no hit: `damage` returns null and changes nothing. Everything a hit changes is in the target's components and its body\n * plain data, so a capture restores it. The asked stop waits in a side table by world, an outbox the sim never reads\n * (no listener: a listener would join the world's captured schedule), so it never changes the hash. Only hosts take it:\n * engine/sim-api.ts leaves `takeHitStop` out. No clock, no random stream: a rule that wants randomness draws from a\n * named stream and passes the result in.\n *\n * Carried from `my-3d2dge:src/stress-world/20-sim.js:324-342` (`damageEnemy`: the knockback along the blow, the big\n * hit's launch, the kill launch and its 1.3 carry, the switch to the dead group, the freeze), the hit-stop through\n * the budget of `src/emberdeep/10-combat.js:45-76` (engine/core/time.ts).\n *\n * @example\n * import { createPhysics } from '../physics/world';\n * import { attachPhysics } from '../physics/binding';\n * import { createWorld } from './world';\n * const w = createWorld({ seed: 1 });\n * attachPhysics(w, createPhysics()); // a scene with physics: true has this\n * const health = { ...HEALTH, hp: 3 };\n * damage(w, { id: 4, health }, { amount: 5, from: [0, 0, 0], stop: 0.06 }); // { killed: true, hp: -2, … }; an agent's body is also knocked","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b0d0401-1a79-4c2f-8a33-ba9239fdbfed","uuid":"c4ff7870-dfc7-42b4-952d-98b61f0d359a","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:00:57.813Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"/**\n * @file The fight's rules, Box 5 (PLAN.md §9.0, WP 6.7): what labs/box/scenes/fight.ts and its systems\n * (fight-hero.ts, fight-foes.ts) share. Its components, its setting, its events, and the two ways a blow lands:\n * `strikeFoe` (the hero's hit or bolt on a member of the crowd) and `hurtHero` (a foe's on him), each through the\n * engine's `damage` (engine/sim/damage.ts: hit points, the push as momentum, the throw, the corpse group, the\n * hit-stop and the event `damage` the page draws its damage numbers from).\n *\n * - **Components**: `fightHealth` (`HEALTH_FIELDS`) on the hero and every foe; `fightHero` (his combo and thrust as\n *   their saved states, and his counters in ticks); `fightFoe` (where a foe is in its attack and its timers);\n *   `fightTelegraph` (a foe's telegraph where it stands, a `TelegraphPlace` as plain data: none while `telegraph` is\n *   empty); `fightShot` (a bolt in flight, `PROJECTILE_FIELDS` and the hit points it takes); `fightTokens`\n *   (`ATTACK_TOKENS_FIELDS`, on the hero: who may attack him now).\n * - **Events**, for the page's effects (engine/gfx/fx: emitters answer them by type): `hit` where a blow lands,\n *   `slain` where a body falls, `shot` where a bolt leaves, `slam` where a pounce lands, each with its `position`\n *   and `size`. They change nothing in the sim.\n * - **The setting** `box.fight.god` (fight.ts; true, read when the scene starts, as the prototype's proof ran): foes'\n *   blows still flinch and push the hero, but take no hit points. Off, they do; at none he falls (`slain`) and is up again\n *   at once with all of them: the box has no end to its fight.\n *\n * A blow on a foe breaks its attack off (`breakAttack`: its token back, its telegraph gone) and stuns it for\n * `STUN` s; one that kills it lets it fall with the kill's throw (`HERO_FIGHT.kill`), a body the crowd walks through\n * that the crowd's step removes later.\n *\n * Reactions (WP 6.2 in the box, WP 7.8): every blow on the hero or a walker goes through the body's reactions (the\n * component `reactions`, engine/sim/reactions.ts `reactTo`): it flinches along the push (`HERO_FIGHT.react`), a big\n * blow knocks a walker down (it lies, then gets up the way it lies: `knockedDown` holds while it does, and the foe\n * acts on nothing meanwhile), and a killing one plays its death. The hero's are stepped by the actors' system and drawn\n * by his puppet (his flinch bends his spine); a walker's by fight-foes.ts's rigs, what they tell its body (`down`, a\n * pose) laid over its states. Slimes and wisps are not humanoids: they have none.\n *\n * Game code, sim-side: it imports only engine/sim-api.ts and the box's own files.\n *\n * @see labs/box/scenes/fight.test.ts\n */\nimport {\n  ATTACK_TOKENS_FIELDS,\n  Attack,\n  Combo,\n  HEALTH_FIELDS,\n  PROJECTILE_FIELDS,\n  SpatialHash,\n  Vector3,\n  damage,\n  defineComponent,\n  reactTo,\n  releaseToken,\n  type ActorComponent,\n  type AnimatorComponent,\n  type AttackState,\n  type AttackTokens,\n  type ComboState,\n  type DamageEvents,\n  type Health,\n  type HurtSet,\n  type Projectile,\n  type ReactionComponents,\n  type ReactionState,\n  type World,\n} from '../../../engine/sim-api';\nimport { HERO, HERO_FIGHT, type HeroHit } from '../cast/hero';\nimport type { CrowdComponents } from './crowd-1000';\n\n/** How long a blow stuns a foe (s): it steers and attacks again after. The prototype's. */\nexport const STUN = 0.22;\n\n/** The hero's combo, as `HERO_FIGHT` says (an idle one; its state is `fightHero.combo`). */\nexport const heroCombo = () => new Combo([...HERO_FIGHT.combo], { window: HERO_FIGHT.window });\n/** The hero's thrust out of a dash (an idle one; its state is `fightHero.thrust`). */\nexport const heroThrust = () => new Attack(HERO_FIGHT.thrust);\nconst IDLE_COMBO: ComboState = heroCombo().save();\n....\n180- * takes no hit: null, nothing changed.\n181- */\n182:export function damage<C extends object, E extends EventMap>(\n183-  world: World<C, E>,\n184-  target: DamageTarget,\n185-  hit: HitSpec,\n186-): DamageEvent | null {\n187-  const w = world as unknown as World<object, DamageEvents>;\n188-  check(\n/**\n * @file Damage (PLAN.md WP 6.3, §6.4): what a hit does once the rules have decided it, generic and without formulas,\n * stats or balance: `damage(w, target, hit)` takes `hit.amount` from the target's health, pushes its crowd body\n * away from the blow as momentum the solver carries on, throws it up, kills it into the corpse group with the kill\n * launch, asks for a hit-stop and emits the event `damage` for the view (numbers, sparks, sounds). How much a hit\n * takes and how hard it pushes are the game's numbers, passed in.\n *\n * - **Health**: the game keeps it in a component (`HEALTH_FIELDS`): hit points, and when and by whom it was last hit,\n *   which flinches, stuns and flashes read (`w.tick - health.hitAt`). At 0 or below it is dead.\n * - **Bodies**: a crowd agent's (engine/physics/crowd.ts): `knockback` adds the push the same for every mass and the\n *   solver carries it into the crowd; `launch` throws it up; `killAgent` moves it to the group `corpse`, which the\n *   crowd walks through, and `updateCrowd` removes it later.\n * - **Hit-stop**: a sim decision the frame clock carries out (engine/core/time.ts). `requestHitStop` keeps the longest\n *   stop asked in the step (they never add up); the run's host takes it after the step (`takeHitStop`) for\n *   `clock.hitStop`, whose leaky budget shrinks stops that follow closely, so a crowd hit stops time once however many\n *   it strikes. The clock is outside the hash: a stop changes how many steps a frame runs, never what a step does.\n *\n * Invariants: a dead or absent target (health at 0 or below, a body no longer `alive`), or an entity holding the\n * component `invulnerable` (god mode: engine/sim/devActions.ts), takes no hit: `damage` returns null and changes nothing. Everything a hit changes is in the target's components and its body\n * plain data, so a capture restores it. The asked stop waits in a side table by world, an outbox the sim never reads\n * (no listener: a listener would join the world's captured schedule), so it never changes the hash. Only hosts take it:\n * engine/sim-api.ts leaves `takeHitStop` out. No clock, no random stream: a rule that wants randomness draws from a\n * named stream and passes the result in.\n *\n * Carried from `my-3d2dge:src/stress-world/20-sim.js:324-342` (`damageEnemy`: the knockback along the blow, the big\n * hit's launch, the kill launch and its 1.3 carry, the switch to the dead group, the freeze), the hit-stop through\n * the budget of `src/emberdeep/10-combat.js:45-76` (engine/core/time.ts).\n *\n * @example\n * import { createPhysics } from '../physics/world';\n * import { attachPhysics } from '../physics/binding';\n * import { createWorld } from './world';\n * const w = createWorld({ seed: 1 });\n * attachPhysics(w, createPhysics()); // a scene with physics: true has this\n * const health = { ...HEALTH, hp: 3 };\n * damage(w, { id: 4, health }, { amount: 5, from: [0, 0, 0], stop: 0.06 }); // { killed: true, hp: -2, … }; an agent's body is also knocked","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_0135Qr8BsGgjAZuMVnAjVuba","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
