{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjFXxWvtDJ5Ea9LDFEPZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KDEfVtCAbxjv2yn2pJ4nQ1","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211947__x8ab6bc/work/PLAN.md","offset":640,"limit":215},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":474,"cache_read_input_tokens":666891,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":474},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b0d0401-1a79-4c2f-8a33-ba9239fdbfed","uuid":"03a79fc9-2f5c-45c3-be52-64506d6a1f56","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:45:29.668Z","request_id":"req_011CgjFXxCagqKnuBKdFe3gv","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01KDEfVtCAbxjv2yn2pJ4nQ1":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211947__x8ab6bc/work/PLAN.md","offset":640,"limit":215}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KDEfVtCAbxjv2yn2pJ4nQ1","type":"tool_result","content":"640\t| Q1 | The Ninth Night | Wake in Evensong. Speak to Ilsabet. Tobias shouts that the bell is wrong. |\n641\t| Q2 | The Penitents' Way | North along the road to the Hanging Field Bellpost. First Anointed pack. |\n642\t| Q3 | Gallows-Tom | Kill him. The Minster doors open. |\n643\t| Q4 | Down Among the Prayers | Undercroft: find 3 Knell-Stones (lever rooms) to open the Ossuary Choir. |\n644\t| Q5 | The Unrung | Kill Prior Ansgar. He says too much, too late. **Vigils unlock.** |\n645\t| Q6 | The Drowned Nave | Turn 2 sluice wheels to drain the way to the stairs, among waking statues. |\n646\t| Q7 | The Gilt Advocate | Kill Serein, who wants the same silence you do. That should worry you. |\n647\t| Q8 | Still the Bell | Belfry. Hold Interact for 3 s to cut the rope. All music dies. Silence. Then her voice. |\n648\t| Q9 | The Lamps Go Out | Evensong burns. Hold the square through 3 waves. Tobias explains at volume. |\n649\t| Q10 | Under the Song | Down through the Infirmary cellar into the Undersong. Recover 3 Stolen Notes. |\n650\t| Q11 | The First Voice | Kill Mother Murmur. Take the heart. |\n651\t| Q12 | Ring It | Hob casts the clapper. Belfry, last stand: monsters climb the tower. Ring the bell three times by holding the rope for 2 s. Each toll is a screen-clearing shockwave, in gold slow motion. Ending, then credits. Anguish and Hours 7 to 12 unlock. |\n652\t\n653\t### 8.4 Lines to use exactly\n654\t\n655\tThese set the voice. Write the rest to match.\n656\t\n657\t> **Chronicler, opening:** \"On the ninth night of the Long Vesper, Old Sorrow rang.\" / \"It had no clapper. It had not had a clapper in three hundred years.\" / \"Every soul in Evensong heard it anyway. By morning, so had the dead.\"\n658\t\n659\t> **Ilsabet, first meeting:** \"You came up the Penitents' Way on your own two feet. In this weather that makes you a saint or a fool, and we have buried all our saints.\" / \"That bell must be stilled, Unsung. Climb to the belfry of Saint Oriel and cut it down. I will keep the lamps lit for you. It is all I have ever done.\"\n660\t\n661\t> **Tobias:** \"WHAT? No. It's flat. FLAT! A bell tolling for the dead tolls down. This one tolls UP. Nobody ever listens to me. I barely listen to me.\" / \"Did I ever tell you about the founding of Saint Oriel? Of course I did. I tell everyone. They run.\"\n662\t\n663\t> **Hob:** \"Bring me iron. Bring me anything. I made a sword out of a church gate yesterday. The gate objected.\"\n664\t\n665\t> **Dame Agnes:** \"Every stone has a note. Yours is ugly. We can fix that.\"\n666\t\n667\t> **Pim:** \"Candles are six silver. Hope is extra.\"\n668\t\n669\t> **Prior Ansgar, on arrival:** \"Who climbs down into my choir? Another bright little candle. Come. I collect them.\" **Mid-fight:** \"Do you hear it, Unsung? That is the sound of everyone you have ever failed.\" **Dying:** \"You fool. You child. We were not ringing it to wake them. We were ringing it... to keep them... down...\"\n670\t\n671\t> **Serein:** \"Mortal noise. All of it. The High Choir has heard enough.\" / \"Silence is the last mercy, and I am merciful.\"\n672\t\n673\t> **Q8, rope cut. Chronicler:** \"And for the first time in three hundred years, the world was quiet.\" **Ilsabet's voice, from everywhere:** \"Thank you, child. Forty years I have kept those lamps. Do you know how heavy a lamp becomes?\" / \"I was the First Voice before your saints had tongues. Sing with me.\"\n674\t\n675\t> **Q9. Tobias:** \"IT WAS HOLDING THEM DOWN! THREE HUNDRED YEARS! I SAID IT WAS FLAT!\" **Hob:** \"You said it was flat. You did not say the world would end.\" **Tobias:** \"IT'S THE SAME THING!\"\n676\t\n677\t> **Mother Murmur:** \"Hush now. Hush. Everyone you lost is singing down here. They ask about you.\" / \"You cannot kill a Voice. You can only... interrupt.\" / \"Louder, then.\" **Dying:** \"Who will keep... the lamps...\"\n678\t\n679\t> **Ending. Chronicler:** \"They cast the new clapper from the heart of the First Voice, and the Unsung rang Old Sorrow with their own hands.\" / \"It was not a beautiful sound.\" / \"It was enough.\" **After the credits:** \"Far below, something answered.\"\n680\t\n681\t---\n682\t\n683\t## 9. Art direction and animation\n684\t\n685\t### 9.1 Look: the engine's native style, lit like a funeral\n686\t\n687\t**The base is the engine's native picture:** chunky pixels (at most 330 lines, nearest-neighbour upscaled; verified 480 × 270 at 1080p),\n688\tlow-poly parts on rigid-skinned skeletons, procedural textures. This also keeps the game visually its own. Keep `gfx.resolution` on `auto`\n689\tin every look, and offer Pixel, Balanced and Full in Settings.\n690\t\n691\t**Camera:** the custom view `cam=45,42,1.5,1,1`, orthographic. Verified: at 42° the floor reads far better than the `iso` preset's 30°.\n692\tThe camera stands south-east, looking north-west. Zoom steps 1.25, 1.5, 2 from the wheel and R3. A hero stands about 30 chunky pixels tall.\n693\t\n694\t**Starting recipe (verified to read well):**\n695\t\n696\t```ts\n697\tdefineSky('sky:crypt', { description: '…', background: '#06050b', pointLights: 1.6,\n698\t  ambient: { sky: '#7a74a0', ground: '#3a3440', intensity: 9 },\n699\t  fog: { color: '#06050b', start: 14, end: 60, amount: 1, floor: 0, ceiling: 1.2, height: 0.3 } });\n700\tdefineLook('look:crypt', { description: '…', sky: 'sky:crypt', filters: {\n701\t  bloom: { scope: 'all', strength: 0.55, threshold: 0.8 }, vignette: { scope: 'all', strength: 0.45 },\n702\t  outline: { scope: 'characters+objects', width: 1, darken: 0.6 } } });\n703\t```\n704\t\n705\t**Rules I learned from the renders:**\n706\t\n707\t- **Floors must be the brightest large surface** in a room (material colour around `#8a8798` with a texture map). Wall tops near black,\n708\t  wall faces mid-dark. Otherwise the picture inverts and heroes vanish.\n709\t- Near-black outside the walls makes rooms feel like islands of light. Keep it.\n710\t- Colour per zone comes from sky ambient and `grade`: ash grey-orange, crypt blue-grey, nave cold with warm stained-glass pools, Undersong\n711\t  red-black with wax yellow. Add `ao` and `air` halos as far as they look good: the budget is unlimited.\n712\t- Heroes need one saturated colour each (Penitent red, Sexton bone and lantern gold, Cantor white and sky blue), so they read in a horde.\n713\t- Check by `node x shot --png` only when the metrics (`LOOK_DARK`, `LOOK_FLAT`, `LOOK_LOW_CONTRAST`, ID-pass shares) can't answer the question.\n714\t\n715\t### 9.2 New art to make\n716\t\n717\tUse the engine's library (`prop:crate, barrel, brazier, chest, pillar, sconce, lantern, banner, table, bench, statue`) for generic props. Make\n718\teverything that makes the world yours, as `defineGeometry`, `defineProp`, `defineTexture`, `defineMaterial`:\n719\t\n720\t- **Wall kits per biome:** tall and low, plain, buttress, arched, windowed (coloured glass light in the Nave), hung with banners or chains, sconce.\n721\t- **Floors per biome:** 2 or 3 floor glyphs each (stone, cracked, wax or ash or water patches), to break up the surface.\n722\t- **Signature pieces:** Old Sorrow (a huge bell, built from stacked `frustum`s and `ring`s, in the Belfry and on the title screen), small hanging bells,\n723\t  gibbets, coffins, sarcophagi, pews, organ pipes, candle racks, wax pools, Bellposts (a post with a handbell), wheel sluices, altars.\n724\t- **Bodies:** 3 hero classes × 3 tiers; 13 monster bodies; 4 boss bodies and 3 Warden forms; 5 NPCs on foot. Use the grammar's `cape`, `cone`, `blade`, `hair`, `ball`. A cowled hero\n725\t  and a horned fiend each took about 15 lines and read clearly at 30 pixels.\n726\t- **Loot:** a small pickup prop per slot, glowing by rarity; the Reliquary's ash pillar.\n727\t- **Effects:** an emitter set per element (Ember, Rime, Blight, Toll, Physical) for hit, trail, explode and pool, plus level-up, Carnage, shrine and bell-toll\n728\t  rings. Emitter `ring` makes shockwaves; `telegraph` makes warnings.\n729\t\n730\t### 9.3 Animation\n731\t\n732\tBase: the engine's animator, `Attack`, `Combo`, `defineMove`, `defineAction`, the reaction system, ragdolls, secondary chains, and the clip library (1,218\n733\tclips; `node x anim find sword`, `… cast`, `… death`). If you import clips, ship only what you use: `node x anim cut` makes a smaller set, because the full set\n734\tis 8.8 MB of text in the deliverable.\n735\t\n736\tMake new ones for what gives the game its feel:\n737\t\n738\t- **Moves (at least 10):** three-hit flail combo, flail spin, leap slam, spade swing, crossbow fire, cast and channel, bell strike, lid slam, noose lash, statue sweep.\n739\t- **Actions:** leap with root motion, avatar transformation, hero ringing the bell (rope pull), kneeling at a Bellpost, boss phase changes.\n740\t- **Monster gaits:** shamble with a limp (`stance` plus a thin build), scuttle, gliding Mourner, statue waking. Heavy secondary on capes, chains and censers.\n741\t\n742\tCheck with the tools: `animCheck`, `node x qa anim`, `node x sheet`.\n743\t\n744\t---\n745\t\n746\t## 10. Audio\n747\t\n748\t**All sound is code, with no audio files.** `defineSfx` and `defineSong` through `createAudio`, plus Web Audio for anything they can't do.\n749\t\n750\t- **Set `audio.volume('music', 0.1)` at start: music defaults to 10%**, and the Settings slider shows 10%. Master to 1, effects and voices near 0.8.\n751\t- **The bell is the game's voice.** Write a good FM bell in `sfx` (`fm` voice, long release, inharmonic partials through layered voices), and use it for: Reliquary drop, level up,\n752\t  Bellposts, boss arrival, the toll shockwave, Carnage. Old Sorrow's toll is the same bell pitched low and detuned, audibly *wrong* before Q12 and audibly *right* in the ending.\n753\t- **Songs (at least 8, your own tunes):** title, Evensong, Way, Undercroft, Nave, Undersong, boss, ending, each in the tracker format with `intensity` layers: calm is pads, organ and a slow\n754\t  bell; fighting adds pounding drums and a low choir pad. `audio.intensity` follows combat. In Q8, cut all music on the rope cut, and hold the silence for the Chronicler's line.\n755\t- **Effects:** per element and weapon hit sets (with `variants` and `vary`), footsteps per surface, breakables, pickups by rarity (a chime rising with rarity), UI cues, per-boss stingers. Rooms set\n756\t  reverb (`audio.room`); crypt and nave ring, the road is dry.\n757\t- **Voices: Animalese/Simlish gibberish.** Each speaker gets a syllable bank of `defineSfx` entries: a pitched `saw` through two `bandpass` filters (two voices at the vowel's formants, `vib` for\n758\t  age), a short noise onset for consonants. Five vowels × four onsets. A line maps its letters to syllables by a hash, so the same word always sounds alike; punctuation shapes the pitch contour; it plays\n759\t  at the subtitle's typing speed. Pitch, formant shift, rate and filter define the speaker: the Chronicler slow and low, Tobias cracked and loud, Mother Murmur two voices an octave apart. Boss taunts and\n760\t  hero barks use the same system.\n761\t- **The first sound:** the engine's audio only starts at a key, click or touch; a pad press doesn't count. Have the title screen say \"Press any button\". If the last device is a pad and `audio.state` is\n762\t  not `running`, show a small corner note: \"Sound starts at your first key press or click.\"\n763\t- **`node x audio sfx:<id>`** renders a sound in Node as numbers; `node x qa audio` checks them. In a session, on `end`: stop music and mute.\n764\t\n765\t---\n766\t\n767\t## 11. UI and UX: 10-foot, controller first\n768\t\n769\tAll UI is your own HTML/CSS in `#ui`, on top of `engine.ui`, themed like iron and vellum, never a web page. Mark everything with `data-ui` and `data-id` so tests read the DOM. Scale by `min(vw/1920, vh/1080)`; keep\n770\ta 5% safe area; body text at least 28 px at 1080p. **No dense data screens:** few big things, one focused thing explained at a time.\n771\t\n772\t### 11.1 Controls\n773\t\n774\tDefine `actionMap:game` (`aimWith: 'pointer'`, no pointer lock). Keyboard and mouse must feel native, not like a controller stand-in.\n775\t\n776\t| Action | DualSense (standard mapping) | Keyboard and mouse |\n777\t| --- | --- | --- |\n778\t| Move | Left stick | Hold or click LMB on the floor (paths round walls), or WASD or arrows |\n779\t| Aim | Right stick (else auto-target by facing) | Pointer |\n780\t| Primary / interact when prompted | Cross `PadSouth` | LMB on a foe, or on a thing; E interacts |\n781\t| Secondary | Square `PadWest` | RMB |\n782\t| Skills 1, 2, 3, 4 | Triangle `PadNorth`, Circle `PadEast`, R1 `PadRightShoulder`, R2 `PadRightTrigger` | 1, 2, 3, 4 |\n783\t| Wine; Dodge | L1 `PadLeftShoulder`; L2 `PadLeftTrigger` | Q; Space |\n784\t| Stand still | n/a (aim with the right stick) | Shift |\n785\t| Map; Journal; Skills; Homeward Bell | D-pad Up; Left; Right; Down (hold) | M or Tab; J; K; T |\n786\t| Inventory | Create `PadSelect` | I or C |\n787\t| Show item labels; Zoom | L3; R3 | Alt; wheel |\n788\t| Pause | Options `PadStart` | Esc |\n789\t| Menus | Stick or D-pad, Cross accept, Circle back, L1 and R1 change tab, Square and Triangle as prompted | Arrows, Enter, Esc, hover and click |\n790\t\n791\tRebinding: keys and pad through `input.bindingsFor`, `rebind` and `listen`, kept in the store. **Couch and hub note:** ignore Options while Create is held (the hub's combination).\n792\t\n793\t**Pointer in the world.** Each frame the page casts `screenRay` from the mouse (`input.mouse.pointer()`) against the capsules of nearby units and items, nearest the camera first, and the hit becomes the focus: nameplate, chevron and\n794\tHP bar. The focused id goes to the sim as `game:target`. **Pad targeting:** a soft lock chooses by distance and angle from facing; the chevron shows it, and melee lunges up to 2 m to it.\n795\t\n796\t**Device tracking.** Track the last real device yourself from `keydown`, `pointermove`, `pointerdown` and pad polls. Don't read `input.lastDevice` alone: it reports `virtual` after your own `virtual.axis` calls.\n797\t\n798\t### 11.2 Prompts\n799\t\n800\tEvery prompt is a `<kbd data-action=\"primary\">` that follows the last device. **Pad:** drawn glyphs, PlayStation by default (✕ ○ □ △ L1 R1 L2 R2, in their colours), Xbox (A B X Y LB RB LT RT) by a Settings option.\n801\t**Keyboard and mouse:** a keycap from the current binding, or a mouse icon. Test: press a key, then a stubbed pad button, then flip the setting, and read the DOM after each.\n802\t\n803\t### 11.3 HUD\n804\t\n805\tOriginal layout, bottom centre: a **bell of red wine** at left for life and a **censer** at right in the class colour for its resource, with the six skill tiles between, each showing its prompt and cooldown sweep, and the Wine beside. XP as a thin\n806\tgold thread beneath. Top: boss bar with name and phase pips; focus plate for elites with affix names. Top right: minimap (2D canvas of explored tiles) and current objective in one line. Damage numbers (`engine.ui.damage`, restyled). Carnage banner.\n807\tCouch and hub: a small plate per other player, in their seat colour, with name, life and class icon; names as text only.\n808\t\n809\t### 11.4 Screens\n810\t\n811\tEach is modal and focus-driven, with the pointer moving focus and clicks selecting. D-pad and stick move focus along a simple grid (write `ui/focus.ts`; `createPadCursor` is a fallback).\n812\t\n813\t- **Title:** title, subtitle, Old Sorrow tolling behind it. Continue, New Game, Settings, Controls, About. Idle → attract.\n814\t- **Class select:** the three classes standing in the Chapel, camera pulled in, one big description at a time, difficulty choice, slot choice.\n815\t- **Inventory:** paper doll with 8 big slots, a backpack of 20 big tiles per tab. Focus shows one card: name in rarity colour, one line of big ▲▼ change against what is equipped, up to 4 affix lines, flavour. Prompts for equip, sell, salvage.\n816\t- **Skills:** six tiles; focusing one shows its three forms as three big cards with a short video-like live demo line. Passive slots.\n817\t- **Map and travel:** full-screen explored map, Bellposts as a list.\n818\t- **Journal:** quests, lore books (replay aloud), stats.\n819\t- **Shops:** Smith, Bellfounder, Chandler, Poor Box, Candle Rack: two panes at most.\n820\t- **Pause:** Resume, Settings, Controls, **Dev Mode**, Quit to Title. Solo pauses the sim (a Setting can turn this off). Couch pauses. In a hub session, it pauses nothing and offers Settings and Controls only.\n821\t- **Controls:** one big diagram for the device in use, with the rebinding screen one press away.\n822\t- **Settings:** volumes (Master, Music 10%, Effects, Voices, UI), Controller prompts (PlayStation or Xbox), rebinding, camera distance, picture (Pixel, Balanced, Full), screen shake, damage numbers, subtitle size, fullscreen, pause on menus, reset all.\n823\t- **About and Credits:** every Source Information field, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback as TASK.md lists them, with Usage reading \"added on import\". Scrolls with stick or wheel. Fill it at the end from the same data as the exit interview.\n824\t- **Dialogue:** a large subtitle band with the speaker's name; never blocks play except story beats; skippable.\n825\t\n826\t### 11.5 Dev mode\n827\t\n828\tFrom the pause menu, never in a session. Two tabs.\n829\t\n830\t- **Tools:** god mode, one-hit kills, free skills and no cooldowns, freeze AI (`freeze`), level set, add silver and materials, spawn any item by rarity, spawn any monster, elite with chosen affixes, or boss at the cursor, travel to any zone or Bellpost\n831\t  (`travel`), set a quest step, unlock everything, reveal map, time scale, show colliders and target shapes as telegraphs, live counters (`__engine.stats()`, awake actors, entities, step ms), and a bug-report line that copies seed and tick.\n832\t- **Balance:** every `game.bal.*` as a live slider with its value, each with a reset, and **Reset All**. Sliders work on the running game.\n833\t\n834\t### 11.6 Attract mode\n835\t\n836\tAfter **10 s with no input on the title or any menu screen**, start the bot on the live world, HUD visible, a pulsing banner saying to press any button. **Any input** (key, pointer move or press, wheel, pad button or stick, touch) exits to the title by `inspector.seed(seed)`. Saves are off.\n837\t\n838\tIt cheats freely: god mode, dev travel, forced drops. Loop, about 3 minutes, with a caption naming each feature as it appears: Evensong and the shops → Penitent on the Way → Sexton in the Undercroft with a Shriving Chest → an Exalted fight → a Reliquary shower → a Skills screen flip → Cantor in the Nave → a boss phase → a Vigil's Candle burning out → the Bell.\n839\t\n840\tThe bot is a pure function from world to intents (`bot/brain.ts`), which tests call directly with `engine.step(1, intents)` and attract feeds through `input.virtual`.\n841\t\n842\t### 11.7 Touch-only devices\n843\t\n844\tIf the device is touch-only and no pad is connected: **no touch controls** (set the engine's `touch` setting to `off`), show **\"Controller or keyboard required\"** and a Settings button that works by touch. Attract mode still runs, and a tap on the screen returns to that notice. A pad connecting at any time unlocks the normal title. Without WebGPU, show a plain notice saying the game needs a browser with WebGPU, not an engine error.\n845\t\n846\t---\n847\t\n848\t## 12. Multiplayer\n849\t\n850\t### 12.1 On its own\n851\t\n852\tThe full game works with no hub: `AIHub.active` is false, the session client does nothing, and storage is normal. **Couch co-op:** up to 4 local players. Press Options on an unused pad to drop in; choose a class in an overlay (modal, world paused); hold Options and Circle to leave.\n853\t\n854\t- Guests are temporary heroes at player 1's level with plain level-appropriate gear, kept for the page's life. Only player 1's save persists. A menu belongs to the seat that opened it, tinted in its colour."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b0d0401-1a79-4c2f-8a33-ba9239fdbfed","uuid":"d3bb5623-382a-4bbf-97b0-e9984b2382da","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:45:29.673Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211947__x8ab6bc/work/PLAN.md","content":"| Q1 | The Ninth Night | Wake in Evensong. Speak to Ilsabet. Tobias shouts that the bell is wrong. |\n| Q2 | The Penitents' Way | North along the road to the Hanging Field Bellpost. First Anointed pack. |\n| Q3 | Gallows-Tom | Kill him. The Minster doors open. |\n| Q4 | Down Among the Prayers | Undercroft: find 3 Knell-Stones (lever rooms) to open the Ossuary Choir. |\n| Q5 | The Unrung | Kill Prior Ansgar. He says too much, too late. **Vigils unlock.** |\n| Q6 | The Drowned Nave | Turn 2 sluice wheels to drain the way to the stairs, among waking statues. |\n| Q7 | The Gilt Advocate | Kill Serein, who wants the same silence you do. That should worry you. |\n| Q8 | Still the Bell | Belfry. Hold Interact for 3 s to cut the rope. All music dies. Silence. Then her voice. |\n| Q9 | The Lamps Go Out | Evensong burns. Hold the square through 3 waves. Tobias explains at volume. |\n| Q10 | Under the Song | Down through the Infirmary cellar into the Undersong. Recover 3 Stolen Notes. |\n| Q11 | The First Voice | Kill Mother Murmur. Take the heart. |\n| Q12 | Ring It | Hob casts the clapper. Belfry, last stand: monsters climb the tower. Ring the bell three times by holding the rope for 2 s. Each toll is a screen-clearing shockwave, in gold slow motion. Ending, then credits. Anguish and Hours 7 to 12 unlock. |\n\n### 8.4 Lines to use exactly\n\nThese set the voice. Write the rest to match.\n\n> **Chronicler, opening:** \"On the ninth night of the Long Vesper, Old Sorrow rang.\" / \"It had no clapper. It had not had a clapper in three hundred years.\" / \"Every soul in Evensong heard it anyway. By morning, so had the dead.\"\n\n> **Ilsabet, first meeting:** \"You came up the Penitents' Way on your own two feet. In this weather that makes you a saint or a fool, and we have buried all our saints.\" / \"That bell must be stilled, Unsung. Climb to the belfry of Saint Oriel and cut it down. I will keep the lamps lit for you. It is all I have ever done.\"\n\n> **Tobias:** \"WHAT? No. It's flat. FLAT! A bell tolling for the dead tolls down. This one tolls UP. Nobody ever listens to me. I barely listen to me.\" / \"Did I ever tell you about the founding of Saint Oriel? Of course I did. I tell everyone. They run.\"\n\n> **Hob:** \"Bring me iron. Bring me anything. I made a sword out of a church gate yesterday. The gate objected.\"\n\n> **Dame Agnes:** \"Every stone has a note. Yours is ugly. We can fix that.\"\n\n> **Pim:** \"Candles are six silver. Hope is extra.\"\n\n> **Prior Ansgar, on arrival:** \"Who climbs down into my choir? Another bright little candle. Come. I collect them.\" **Mid-fight:** \"Do you hear it, Unsung? That is the sound of everyone you have ever failed.\" **Dying:** \"You fool. You child. We were not ringing it to wake them. We were ringing it... to keep them... down...\"\n\n> **Serein:** \"Mortal noise. All of it. The High Choir has heard enough.\" / \"Silence is the last mercy, and I am merciful.\"\n\n> **Q8, rope cut. Chronicler:** \"And for the first time in three hundred years, the world was quiet.\" **Ilsabet's voice, from everywhere:** \"Thank you, child. Forty years I have kept those lamps. Do you know how heavy a lamp becomes?\" / \"I was the First Voice before your saints had tongues. Sing with me.\"\n\n> **Q9. Tobias:** \"IT WAS HOLDING THEM DOWN! THREE HUNDRED YEARS! I SAID IT WAS FLAT!\" **Hob:** \"You said it was flat. You did not say the world would end.\" **Tobias:** \"IT'S THE SAME THING!\"\n\n> **Mother Murmur:** \"Hush now. Hush. Everyone you lost is singing down here. They ask about you.\" / \"You cannot kill a Voice. You can only... interrupt.\" / \"Louder, then.\" **Dying:** \"Who will keep... the lamps...\"\n\n> **Ending. Chronicler:** \"They cast the new clapper from the heart of the First Voice, and the Unsung rang Old Sorrow with their own hands.\" / \"It was not a beautiful sound.\" / \"It was enough.\" **After the credits:** \"Far below, something answered.\"\n\n---\n\n## 9. Art direction and animation\n\n### 9.1 Look: the engine's native style, lit like a funeral\n\n**The base is the engine's native picture:** chunky pixels (at most 330 lines, nearest-neighbour upscaled; verified 480 × 270 at 1080p),\nlow-poly parts on rigid-skinned skeletons, procedural textures. This also keeps the game visually its own. Keep `gfx.resolution` on `auto`\nin every look, and offer Pixel, Balanced and Full in Settings.\n\n**Camera:** the custom view `cam=45,42,1.5,1,1`, orthographic. Verified: at 42° the floor reads far better than the `iso` preset's 30°.\nThe camera stands south-east, looking north-west. Zoom steps 1.25, 1.5, 2 from the wheel and R3. A hero stands about 30 chunky pixels tall.\n\n**Starting recipe (verified to read well):**\n\n```ts\ndefineSky('sky:crypt', { description: '…', background: '#06050b', pointLights: 1.6,\n  ambient: { sky: '#7a74a0', ground: '#3a3440', intensity: 9 },\n  fog: { color: '#06050b', start: 14, end: 60, amount: 1, floor: 0, ceiling: 1.2, height: 0.3 } });\ndefineLook('look:crypt', { description: '…', sky: 'sky:crypt', filters: {\n  bloom: { scope: 'all', strength: 0.55, threshold: 0.8 }, vignette: { scope: 'all', strength: 0.45 },\n  outline: { scope: 'characters+objects', width: 1, darken: 0.6 } } });\n```\n\n**Rules I learned from the renders:**\n\n- **Floors must be the brightest large surface** in a room (material colour around `#8a8798` with a texture map). Wall tops near black,\n  wall faces mid-dark. Otherwise the picture inverts and heroes vanish.\n- Near-black outside the walls makes rooms feel like islands of light. Keep it.\n- Colour per zone comes from sky ambient and `grade`: ash grey-orange, crypt blue-grey, nave cold with warm stained-glass pools, Undersong\n  red-black with wax yellow. Add `ao` and `air` halos as far as they look good: the budget is unlimited.\n- Heroes need one saturated colour each (Penitent red, Sexton bone and lantern gold, Cantor white and sky blue), so they read in a horde.\n- Check by `node x shot --png` only when the metrics (`LOOK_DARK`, `LOOK_FLAT`, `LOOK_LOW_CONTRAST`, ID-pass shares) can't answer the question.\n\n### 9.2 New art to make\n\nUse the engine's library (`prop:crate, barrel, brazier, chest, pillar, sconce, lantern, banner, table, bench, statue`) for generic props. Make\neverything that makes the world yours, as `defineGeometry`, `defineProp`, `defineTexture`, `defineMaterial`:\n\n- **Wall kits per biome:** tall and low, plain, buttress, arched, windowed (coloured glass light in the Nave), hung with banners or chains, sconce.\n- **Floors per biome:** 2 or 3 floor glyphs each (stone, cracked, wax or ash or water patches), to break up the surface.\n- **Signature pieces:** Old Sorrow (a huge bell, built from stacked `frustum`s and `ring`s, in the Belfry and on the title screen), small hanging bells,\n  gibbets, coffins, sarcophagi, pews, organ pipes, candle racks, wax pools, Bellposts (a post with a handbell), wheel sluices, altars.\n- **Bodies:** 3 hero classes × 3 tiers; 13 monster bodies; 4 boss bodies and 3 Warden forms; 5 NPCs on foot. Use the grammar's `cape`, `cone`, `blade`, `hair`, `ball`. A cowled hero\n  and a horned fiend each took about 15 lines and read clearly at 30 pixels.\n- **Loot:** a small pickup prop per slot, glowing by rarity; the Reliquary's ash pillar.\n- **Effects:** an emitter set per element (Ember, Rime, Blight, Toll, Physical) for hit, trail, explode and pool, plus level-up, Carnage, shrine and bell-toll\n  rings. Emitter `ring` makes shockwaves; `telegraph` makes warnings.\n\n### 9.3 Animation\n\nBase: the engine's animator, `Attack`, `Combo`, `defineMove`, `defineAction`, the reaction system, ragdolls, secondary chains, and the clip library (1,218\nclips; `node x anim find sword`, `… cast`, `… death`). If you import clips, ship only what you use: `node x anim cut` makes a smaller set, because the full set\nis 8.8 MB of text in the deliverable.\n\nMake new ones for what gives the game its feel:\n\n- **Moves (at least 10):** three-hit flail combo, flail spin, leap slam, spade swing, crossbow fire, cast and channel, bell strike, lid slam, noose lash, statue sweep.\n- **Actions:** leap with root motion, avatar transformation, hero ringing the bell (rope pull), kneeling at a Bellpost, boss phase changes.\n- **Monster gaits:** shamble with a limp (`stance` plus a thin build), scuttle, gliding Mourner, statue waking. Heavy secondary on capes, chains and censers.\n\nCheck with the tools: `animCheck`, `node x qa anim`, `node x sheet`.\n\n---\n\n## 10. Audio\n\n**All sound is code, with no audio files.** `defineSfx` and `defineSong` through `createAudio`, plus Web Audio for anything they can't do.\n\n- **Set `audio.volume('music', 0.1)` at start: music defaults to 10%**, and the Settings slider shows 10%. Master to 1, effects and voices near 0.8.\n- **The bell is the game's voice.** Write a good FM bell in `sfx` (`fm` voice, long release, inharmonic partials through layered voices), and use it for: Reliquary drop, level up,\n  Bellposts, boss arrival, the toll shockwave, Carnage. Old Sorrow's toll is the same bell pitched low and detuned, audibly *wrong* before Q12 and audibly *right* in the ending.\n- **Songs (at least 8, your own tunes):** title, Evensong, Way, Undercroft, Nave, Undersong, boss, ending, each in the tracker format with `intensity` layers: calm is pads, organ and a slow\n  bell; fighting adds pounding drums and a low choir pad. `audio.intensity` follows combat. In Q8, cut all music on the rope cut, and hold the silence for the Chronicler's line.\n- **Effects:** per element and weapon hit sets (with `variants` and `vary`), footsteps per surface, breakables, pickups by rarity (a chime rising with rarity), UI cues, per-boss stingers. Rooms set\n  reverb (`audio.room`); crypt and nave ring, the road is dry.\n- **Voices: Animalese/Simlish gibberish.** Each speaker gets a syllable bank of `defineSfx` entries: a pitched `saw` through two `bandpass` filters (two voices at the vowel's formants, `vib` for\n  age), a short noise onset for consonants. Five vowels × four onsets. A line maps its letters to syllables by a hash, so the same word always sounds alike; punctuation shapes the pitch contour; it plays\n  at the subtitle's typing speed. Pitch, formant shift, rate and filter define the speaker: the Chronicler slow and low, Tobias cracked and loud, Mother Murmur two voices an octave apart. Boss taunts and\n  hero barks use the same system.\n- **The first sound:** the engine's audio only starts at a key, click or touch; a pad press doesn't count. Have the title screen say \"Press any button\". If the last device is a pad and `audio.state` is\n  not `running`, show a small corner note: \"Sound starts at your first key press or click.\"\n- **`node x audio sfx:<id>`** renders a sound in Node as numbers; `node x qa audio` checks them. In a session, on `end`: stop music and mute.\n\n---\n\n## 11. UI and UX: 10-foot, controller first\n\nAll UI is your own HTML/CSS in `#ui`, on top of `engine.ui`, themed like iron and vellum, never a web page. Mark everything with `data-ui` and `data-id` so tests read the DOM. Scale by `min(vw/1920, vh/1080)`; keep\na 5% safe area; body text at least 28 px at 1080p. **No dense data screens:** few big things, one focused thing explained at a time.\n\n### 11.1 Controls\n\nDefine `actionMap:game` (`aimWith: 'pointer'`, no pointer lock). Keyboard and mouse must feel native, not like a controller stand-in.\n\n| Action | DualSense (standard mapping) | Keyboard and mouse |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Move | Left stick | Hold or click LMB on the floor (paths round walls), or WASD or arrows |\n| Aim | Right stick (else auto-target by facing) | Pointer |\n| Primary / interact when prompted | Cross `PadSouth` | LMB on a foe, or on a thing; E interacts |\n| Secondary | Square `PadWest` | RMB |\n| Skills 1, 2, 3, 4 | Triangle `PadNorth`, Circle `PadEast`, R1 `PadRightShoulder`, R2 `PadRightTrigger` | 1, 2, 3, 4 |\n| Wine; Dodge | L1 `PadLeftShoulder`; L2 `PadLeftTrigger` | Q; Space |\n| Stand still | n/a (aim with the right stick) | Shift |\n| Map; Journal; Skills; Homeward Bell | D-pad Up; Left; Right; Down (hold) | M or Tab; J; K; T |\n| Inventory | Create `PadSelect` | I or C |\n| Show item labels; Zoom | L3; R3 | Alt; wheel |\n| Pause | Options `PadStart` | Esc |\n| Menus | Stick or D-pad, Cross accept, Circle back, L1 and R1 change tab, Square and Triangle as prompted | Arrows, Enter, Esc, hover and click |\n\nRebinding: keys and pad through `input.bindingsFor`, `rebind` and `listen`, kept in the store. **Couch and hub note:** ignore Options while Create is held (the hub's combination).\n\n**Pointer in the world.** Each frame the page casts `screenRay` from the mouse (`input.mouse.pointer()`) against the capsules of nearby units and items, nearest the camera first, and the hit becomes the focus: nameplate, chevron and\nHP bar. The focused id goes to the sim as `game:target`. **Pad targeting:** a soft lock chooses by distance and angle from facing; the chevron shows it, and melee lunges up to 2 m to it.\n\n**Device tracking.** Track the last real device yourself from `keydown`, `pointermove`, `pointerdown` and pad polls. Don't read `input.lastDevice` alone: it reports `virtual` after your own `virtual.axis` calls.\n\n### 11.2 Prompts\n\nEvery prompt is a `<kbd data-action=\"primary\">` that follows the last device. **Pad:** drawn glyphs, PlayStation by default (✕ ○ □ △ L1 R1 L2 R2, in their colours), Xbox (A B X Y LB RB LT RT) by a Settings option.\n**Keyboard and mouse:** a keycap from the current binding, or a mouse icon. Test: press a key, then a stubbed pad button, then flip the setting, and read the DOM after each.\n\n### 11.3 HUD\n\nOriginal layout, bottom centre: a **bell of red wine** at left for life and a **censer** at right in the class colour for its resource, with the six skill tiles between, each showing its prompt and cooldown sweep, and the Wine beside. XP as a thin\ngold thread beneath. Top: boss bar with name and phase pips; focus plate for elites with affix names. Top right: minimap (2D canvas of explored tiles) and current objective in one line. Damage numbers (`engine.ui.damage`, restyled). Carnage banner.\nCouch and hub: a small plate per other player, in their seat colour, with name, life and class icon; names as text only.\n\n### 11.4 Screens\n\nEach is modal and focus-driven, with the pointer moving focus and clicks selecting. D-pad and stick move focus along a simple grid (write `ui/focus.ts`; `createPadCursor` is a fallback).\n\n- **Title:** title, subtitle, Old Sorrow tolling behind it. Continue, New Game, Settings, Controls, About. Idle → attract.\n- **Class select:** the three classes standing in the Chapel, camera pulled in, one big description at a time, difficulty choice, slot choice.\n- **Inventory:** paper doll with 8 big slots, a backpack of 20 big tiles per tab. Focus shows one card: name in rarity colour, one line of big ▲▼ change against what is equipped, up to 4 affix lines, flavour. Prompts for equip, sell, salvage.\n- **Skills:** six tiles; focusing one shows its three forms as three big cards with a short video-like live demo line. Passive slots.\n- **Map and travel:** full-screen explored map, Bellposts as a list.\n- **Journal:** quests, lore books (replay aloud), stats.\n- **Shops:** Smith, Bellfounder, Chandler, Poor Box, Candle Rack: two panes at most.\n- **Pause:** Resume, Settings, Controls, **Dev Mode**, Quit to Title. Solo pauses the sim (a Setting can turn this off). Couch pauses. In a hub session, it pauses nothing and offers Settings and Controls only.\n- **Controls:** one big diagram for the device in use, with the rebinding screen one press away.\n- **Settings:** volumes (Master, Music 10%, Effects, Voices, UI), Controller prompts (PlayStation or Xbox), rebinding, camera distance, picture (Pixel, Balanced, Full), screen shake, damage numbers, subtitle size, fullscreen, pause on menus, reset all.\n- **About and Credits:** every Source Information field, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback as TASK.md lists them, with Usage reading \"added on import\". Scrolls with stick or wheel. Fill it at the end from the same data as the exit interview.\n- **Dialogue:** a large subtitle band with the speaker's name; never blocks play except story beats; skippable.\n\n### 11.5 Dev mode\n\nFrom the pause menu, never in a session. Two tabs.\n\n- **Tools:** god mode, one-hit kills, free skills and no cooldowns, freeze AI (`freeze`), level set, add silver and materials, spawn any item by rarity, spawn any monster, elite with chosen affixes, or boss at the cursor, travel to any zone or Bellpost\n  (`travel`), set a quest step, unlock everything, reveal map, time scale, show colliders and target shapes as telegraphs, live counters (`__engine.stats()`, awake actors, entities, step ms), and a bug-report line that copies seed and tick.\n- **Balance:** every `game.bal.*` as a live slider with its value, each with a reset, and **Reset All**. Sliders work on the running game.\n\n### 11.6 Attract mode\n\nAfter **10 s with no input on the title or any menu screen**, start the bot on the live world, HUD visible, a pulsing banner saying to press any button. **Any input** (key, pointer move or press, wheel, pad button or stick, touch) exits to the title by `inspector.seed(seed)`. Saves are off.\n\nIt cheats freely: god mode, dev travel, forced drops. Loop, about 3 minutes, with a caption naming each feature as it appears: Evensong and the shops → Penitent on the Way → Sexton in the Undercroft with a Shriving Chest → an Exalted fight → a Reliquary shower → a Skills screen flip → Cantor in the Nave → a boss phase → a Vigil's Candle burning out → the Bell.\n\nThe bot is a pure function from world to intents (`bot/brain.ts`), which tests call directly with `engine.step(1, intents)` and attract feeds through `input.virtual`.\n\n### 11.7 Touch-only devices\n\nIf the device is touch-only and no pad is connected: **no touch controls** (set the engine's `touch` setting to `off`), show **\"Controller or keyboard required\"** and a Settings button that works by touch. Attract mode still runs, and a tap on the screen returns to that notice. A pad connecting at any time unlocks the normal title. Without WebGPU, show a plain notice saying the game needs a browser with WebGPU, not an engine error.\n\n---\n\n## 12. Multiplayer\n\n### 12.1 On its own\n\nThe full game works with no hub: `AIHub.active` is false, the session client does nothing, and storage is normal. **Couch co-op:** up to 4 local players. Press Options on an unused pad to drop in; choose a class in an overlay (modal, world paused); hold Options and Circle to leave.\n\n- Guests are temporary heroes at player 1's level with plain level-appropriate gear, kept for the page's life. Only player 1's save persists. A menu belongs to the seat that opened it, tinted in its colour.","numLines":215,"startLine":640,"totalLines":1023}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01KDEfVtCAbxjv2yn2pJ4nQ1","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
