{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjFaz3XuAbu9deuxnpfU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01C8RA9qBB53v1jRNCEpMiKy","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211947__x8ab6bc/work/PLAN.md","offset":350,"limit":60},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":926,"cache_read_input_tokens":679054,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":926},"output_tokens":72,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b0d0401-1a79-4c2f-8a33-ba9239fdbfed","uuid":"251a1899-eaf0-46de-914a-31cc32bbcb90","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:46:09.848Z","request_id":"req_011CgjFaygThwhTPipoBa4Ym","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01C8RA9qBB53v1jRNCEpMiKy":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211947__x8ab6bc/work/PLAN.md","offset":350,"limit":60}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01C8RA9qBB53v1jRNCEpMiKy","type":"tool_result","content":"350\t\n351\tThe rest of the game must be buildable later with ordinary designer tools, so content is data, never code:\n352\t\n353\t- Monsters, skills, skill forms, items, affixes, zones, quests, dialogue and chunks are table rows and text.\n354\t- A new chunk is a text map. A new zone is a row. A new monster is a row plus a body. A new skill form is a row. A quest\n355\t  is a list of steps with triggers.\n356\t- The runner, brains and generator read tables and never compare ids against code paths (\"ask the entry, never the id\").\n357\t- `labs/game/README.md` has a short **designer guide**: how to add each of those, with one worked example each, and the\n358\t  dev-mode tools that test it. `node x gallery body|prop|emitter|look` already shows entries as contact sheets.\n359\t\n360\t---\n361\t\n362\t## 4. Systems\n363\t\n364\t### 4.1 Hero numbers\n365\t\n366\t| Stat | Rule |\n367\t| --- | --- |\n368\t| Attributes | **Might** (Penitent), **Finesse** (Sexton), **Lore** (Cantor), **Vigor** (all). Main stat 10 + 3 per level; Vigor 9 + 2 per level; the other two 8 + 1 per level |\n369\t| Life | 40 + 4 × level + 6 × Vigor |\n370\t| Hit | `roll(weaponMin, weaponMax) × skill% × (1 + main/100) × (1 + sum of bonuses) × crit`. Crit: base 5% chance, +50% damage |\n371\t| Taking a hit | `× (1 − A/(A + 50m)) × (1 − R/(R + 5m))`, A armour, R the resist for that element, m monster level |\n372\t| Move | 5.4 m/s base. **Dodge:** 4.5 m dash in 0.25 s with invulnerability, 2 charges, 4 s recharge |\n373\t| Wine | heals 60% over 1 s, 30 s cooldown. **Wafers** drop from kills (15% chance), heal 15% and heal everyone within 6 m |\n374\t| Level | Cap 30. `xpToNext(L) = round(24 × L^1.9)`. A kill gives `4 + 2m` XP. Level-up heals fully, with a gold shaft of light and a bell |\n375\t| Devotion | After 30, every 20,000 XP gives a point: Zeal (+2 main), Flesh (+2 Vigor), Haste (+0.3% move, to 15%), Fortune (+0.5% find) |\n376\t| Carnage | 6 or more kills within 1.5 s pays XP bonus `10% × kills`, with a big banner and a sound |\n377\t\n378\t### 4.2 Monster numbers\n379\t\n380\t- Level `m` comes from the zone. `HP = base × 1.16^(m−1) × difficulty × (1 + 0.75 × (players − 1))`. `Damage = base × 1.12^(m−1) × difficulty`.\n381\t- Weapon damage at item level `i` averages `3.4 × 1.155^(i−1)`. Armour per piece `3 + 2.2i`. Affixes scale with `i`.\n382\t- **Difficulty (HP, damage, silver and XP, find):** Vespers 1, 1, 1, 1. Compline 1.6, 1.3, 1.25, 1.1. Matins 2.6, 1.7, 1.6, 1.25.\n383\t  Anguish I 4.5, 2.2, 2.1, 1.5. Anguish II 8, 2.9, 2.8, 1.8. Anguish III 14, 3.8, 3.6, 2.2. Anguish unlocks after the story.\n384\t- **Targets the balance test checks:** on-level gear at Vespers kills fodder in 1 to 3 primary hits, an Anointed pack in 12 to\n385\t  25 s, a boss in 90 to 150 s; fodder takes 15 or more hits to kill a hero, a boss's big hit takes 15 to 35% of life; a\n386\t  zone takes 8 to 12 minutes; the story ends near level 16 to 18.\n387\t\n388\t### 4.3 The combat pipeline (sim-side)\n389\t\n390\tOne path for all damage: **skill or attack releases a shape, shape finds targets, `applyHit` rolls and mitigates, then\n391\t`damage()` from the engine, statuses, `reactTo`, events.** Shapes: `arc, line, ring, cone, ground (delayed, with a telegraph),\n392\tprojectile, chain, self`. Every enemy attack has a telegraph (`defineTelegraph`) unless it is a fodder bite. Statuses: burn,\n393\tblight, chill, freeze, stun, root, slow, fear, vulnerable, shield, each with a duration in whole steps.\n394\t\n395\t**Feel, on every hit.** Event `hit` with `position`, `size` and `element` for emitter and sound; damage number (white, gold\n396\tcrit, element tint); flinch through `reactTo`; a small knockback; `requestHitStop` of 40 to 90 ms on big hits in solo and\n397\tcouch; trail ribbon on sweeps; screen shake scaled by hit size. In lockstep there is no hit-stop: shake and flash only, since\n398\tstopping time would stall every copy.\n399\t\n400\t**Kills.** Up to 6 simultaneous `handOff` ragdolls with a launch along the blow; other deaths play `deathBlown`,\n401\t`deathCrush`, `deathSpin` and so on from `data/anim/actions`. Corpses fade after 6 to 10 s. Crowd rigs use `killAgent`.\n402\t\n403\t### 4.4 Skills\n404\t\n405\tA single runner reads a table row: `{ id, slot, resource cost or gain, cooldown steps, wind-up and recovery (scaled by attack\n406\tspeed), move or action or clip to play, releases: [shape, percent, element, status, emitter, sfx], form overrides }`. Six\n407\tslots, all class skills: **Primary, Secondary, Skill 1 to 4**. Unlocks by level: 1, 2, 4, 6, 9, 12. Inflections unlock at\n408\tlevel 8 and level 14. Passive slots at 10 and 20. The player sets a skill's form and passives on the Skills screen, any\n409\ttime out of combat. Hub rounds start at level 12 with everything unlocked."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b0d0401-1a79-4c2f-8a33-ba9239fdbfed","uuid":"47b3f3a2-f764-418a-9097-0ebd270e5632","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:46:09.855Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211947__x8ab6bc/work/PLAN.md","content":"\nThe rest of the game must be buildable later with ordinary designer tools, so content is data, never code:\n\n- Monsters, skills, skill forms, items, affixes, zones, quests, dialogue and chunks are table rows and text.\n- A new chunk is a text map. A new zone is a row. A new monster is a row plus a body. A new skill form is a row. A quest\n  is a list of steps with triggers.\n- The runner, brains and generator read tables and never compare ids against code paths (\"ask the entry, never the id\").\n- `labs/game/README.md` has a short **designer guide**: how to add each of those, with one worked example each, and the\n  dev-mode tools that test it. `node x gallery body|prop|emitter|look` already shows entries as contact sheets.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Systems\n\n### 4.1 Hero numbers\n\n| Stat | Rule |\n| --- | --- |\n| Attributes | **Might** (Penitent), **Finesse** (Sexton), **Lore** (Cantor), **Vigor** (all). Main stat 10 + 3 per level; Vigor 9 + 2 per level; the other two 8 + 1 per level |\n| Life | 40 + 4 × level + 6 × Vigor |\n| Hit | `roll(weaponMin, weaponMax) × skill% × (1 + main/100) × (1 + sum of bonuses) × crit`. Crit: base 5% chance, +50% damage |\n| Taking a hit | `× (1 − A/(A + 50m)) × (1 − R/(R + 5m))`, A armour, R the resist for that element, m monster level |\n| Move | 5.4 m/s base. **Dodge:** 4.5 m dash in 0.25 s with invulnerability, 2 charges, 4 s recharge |\n| Wine | heals 60% over 1 s, 30 s cooldown. **Wafers** drop from kills (15% chance), heal 15% and heal everyone within 6 m |\n| Level | Cap 30. `xpToNext(L) = round(24 × L^1.9)`. A kill gives `4 + 2m` XP. Level-up heals fully, with a gold shaft of light and a bell |\n| Devotion | After 30, every 20,000 XP gives a point: Zeal (+2 main), Flesh (+2 Vigor), Haste (+0.3% move, to 15%), Fortune (+0.5% find) |\n| Carnage | 6 or more kills within 1.5 s pays XP bonus `10% × kills`, with a big banner and a sound |\n\n### 4.2 Monster numbers\n\n- Level `m` comes from the zone. `HP = base × 1.16^(m−1) × difficulty × (1 + 0.75 × (players − 1))`. `Damage = base × 1.12^(m−1) × difficulty`.\n- Weapon damage at item level `i` averages `3.4 × 1.155^(i−1)`. Armour per piece `3 + 2.2i`. Affixes scale with `i`.\n- **Difficulty (HP, damage, silver and XP, find):** Vespers 1, 1, 1, 1. Compline 1.6, 1.3, 1.25, 1.1. Matins 2.6, 1.7, 1.6, 1.25.\n  Anguish I 4.5, 2.2, 2.1, 1.5. Anguish II 8, 2.9, 2.8, 1.8. Anguish III 14, 3.8, 3.6, 2.2. Anguish unlocks after the story.\n- **Targets the balance test checks:** on-level gear at Vespers kills fodder in 1 to 3 primary hits, an Anointed pack in 12 to\n  25 s, a boss in 90 to 150 s; fodder takes 15 or more hits to kill a hero, a boss's big hit takes 15 to 35% of life; a\n  zone takes 8 to 12 minutes; the story ends near level 16 to 18.\n\n### 4.3 The combat pipeline (sim-side)\n\nOne path for all damage: **skill or attack releases a shape, shape finds targets, `applyHit` rolls and mitigates, then\n`damage()` from the engine, statuses, `reactTo`, events.** Shapes: `arc, line, ring, cone, ground (delayed, with a telegraph),\nprojectile, chain, self`. Every enemy attack has a telegraph (`defineTelegraph`) unless it is a fodder bite. Statuses: burn,\nblight, chill, freeze, stun, root, slow, fear, vulnerable, shield, each with a duration in whole steps.\n\n**Feel, on every hit.** Event `hit` with `position`, `size` and `element` for emitter and sound; damage number (white, gold\ncrit, element tint); flinch through `reactTo`; a small knockback; `requestHitStop` of 40 to 90 ms on big hits in solo and\ncouch; trail ribbon on sweeps; screen shake scaled by hit size. In lockstep there is no hit-stop: shake and flash only, since\nstopping time would stall every copy.\n\n**Kills.** Up to 6 simultaneous `handOff` ragdolls with a launch along the blow; other deaths play `deathBlown`,\n`deathCrush`, `deathSpin` and so on from `data/anim/actions`. Corpses fade after 6 to 10 s. Crowd rigs use `killAgent`.\n\n### 4.4 Skills\n\nA single runner reads a table row: `{ id, slot, resource cost or gain, cooldown steps, wind-up and recovery (scaled by attack\nspeed), move or action or clip to play, releases: [shape, percent, element, status, emitter, sfx], form overrides }`. Six\nslots, all class skills: **Primary, Secondary, Skill 1 to 4**. Unlocks by level: 1, 2, 4, 6, 9, 12. Inflections unlock at\nlevel 8 and level 14. Passive slots at 10 and 20. The player sets a skill's form and passives on the Skills screen, any\ntime out of combat. Hub rounds start at level 12 with everything unlocked.","numLines":60,"startLine":350,"totalLines":1025}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01C8RA9qBB53v1jRNCEpMiKy","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjFaz3XuAbu9deuxnpfU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Nnfw4GvTwrvYBgY8baRpDz","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211947__x8ab6bc/work/PLAN.md","offset":930,"limit":90},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":926,"cache_read_input_tokens":679054,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":926},"output_tokens":72,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b0d0401-1a79-4c2f-8a33-ba9239fdbfed","uuid":"737c271c-6667-4fbd-8c0b-789aacde968f","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:46:11.285Z","request_id":"req_011CgjFaygThwhTPipoBa4Ym","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Nnfw4GvTwrvYBgY8baRpDz":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211947__x8ab6bc/work/PLAN.md","offset":930,"limit":90}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Nnfw4GvTwrvYBgY8baRpDz","type":"tool_result","content":"930\tThe engine's one-file recipe aimed at your page. **Verified: 4 to 12 s, 6.7 MB, opens from `file://`.** Output goes to the deliverable beside the dev folder.\n931\t\n932\t```js\n933\t// labs/game/tools/build-one-file.mjs  <path to the deliverable>\n934\timport { build } from 'vite';\n935\timport { readFileSync, writeFileSync } from 'node:fs';\n936\timport { join, resolve } from 'node:path';\n937\tconst root = resolve('.');\n938\tconst result = await build({ root, configFile: false, logLevel: 'warn', base: './',\n939\t  resolve: { alias: [{ find: /^three$/, replacement: 'three/webgpu' }] },\n940\t  build: { write: false, modulePreload: false, cssCodeSplit: false, assetsInlineLimit: () => true, chunkSizeWarningLimit: Infinity,\n941\t    rollupOptions: { input: { game: join(root, 'labs/game/index.html') }, output: { inlineDynamicImports: true } } } });\n942\tconst files = {}; let html;\n943\tfor (const item of (Array.isArray(result) ? result : [result]).flatMap((o) => o.output)) {\n944\t  const text = item.type === 'chunk' ? item.code : typeof item.source === 'string' ? item.source : new TextDecoder().decode(item.source);\n945\t  if (item.fileName.endsWith('.html')) html = text; else files[item.fileName] = text;\n946\t}\n947\tconst find = (ref) => files[Object.keys(files).find((f) => ref.endsWith('/' + f) || ref === f || ref === './' + f)];\n948\tconst LOADED = /<script type=\"module\" crossorigin src=\"([^\"]+)\"><\\/script>|<link rel=\"stylesheet\" crossorigin href=\"([^\"]+)\">/g;\n949\tlet out = html.replace(LOADED, (_t, script, style) => {\n950\t  if (style) return `<style>${find(style)}</style>`;\n951\t  const code = find(script).replaceAll('</script', '<\\\\/script');\n952\t  if (code.includes('<!--')) throw new Error('inline script holds <!--: write it apart in the source');\n953\t  return `<script type=\"module\">${code}</script>`;\n954\t});\n955\tconst client = readFileSync('labs/game/vendor/aihub-session.txt', 'utf8');          // session.js, unmodified\n956\tout = out.replace('<meta charset=\"utf-8\" />', () => `<meta charset=\"utf-8\" />\\n<script>\\n${client}\\n</script>`);\n957\twriteFileSync(process.argv[2], out);\n958\t```\n959\t\n960\tGet the client once: `curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/session.js -o labs/game/vendor/aihub-session.txt`. Assert in the test: first `<script>` follows the charset; the client's banner is intact; no `src` or `href` outside data URLs. Also add `hub:source` and `hub:type` metas.\n961\t\n962\t---\n963\t\n964\t## 14. Testing\n965\t\n966\t**`npm run verify` (add the script to the game's `package.json`; it runs `labs/game/tools/verify.mjs`) runs everything and prints only failures and one line of counts.** Its parts: `npm run verify -- sim`, `net`, `full`, `browser`, `hub`. Rerun only the part covering what you changed.\n967\t\n968\t| Part | What it proves | Rough time |\n969\t| --- | --- | --- |\n970\t| `sim` | `npm run check`, then Vitest: replay goldens, capture and restore, formulas, every skill form hits or does what its row says, every monster spawns, attacks and dies, every affix, every boss phase changes, Reliquary powers fire, loot distribution over 100,000 rolls, 50 seeds of generator connectivity, quest graph reachable, save round trip, balance targets of §4.2 by a fast bot | 2 min |\n971\t| `net` | Four `createHeadless` copies running the lockstep driver over a fake hub, with random latency and a leave: `gameHash` equal at every checkpoint. The strongest net test, and cheap. Write the driver with its transport and stepper passed in, so the same code runs here. Software-rendered browsers can't get 3 or 4 copies warmed up in time here (a 3-player run left one copy at tick 0 with nothing to compare), so this one does that job | 1 min |\n972\t| `full` | **The scripted playthrough:** the bot plays the whole story for each class on 1 seed, Q1 to Q12 through the credits, plus one Vigil, in Node, with `game.bal` speeding it and dev travel between objectives; asserts each quest flag, boss death, level, gear, no softlock | 5 to 10 min |\n973\t| `browser` | The deliverable from `file://`, Playwright with the flags of §2 and `?quality=low&gfx.warmUp=asked`: boots, title, class select, play by keyboard and mouse, then by a stubbed pad; prompts follow device; Xbox setting; each screen opens and has content; dev sliders change a value and reset restores it; attract starts at 10 s and exits on input; phone profile shows the notice and its Settings; `pipelinesAfterWarmUp` 0; music bus at 0.1; `OfflineAudioContext` renders of a song and a voice line are non-silent; About has every field | 5 min |\n974\t| `hub` | Download `harness.html`, `bridge.js` and `round.js` from `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/` into `out/hub/` and copy the deliverable there as `game.html`; `python3 -u -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` there; open `harness.html?game=game.html&<scenario>&auto=1`; confirm the frame's page is your game; wait for `document.body.dataset.complete`; assert `window.__hubCheck.pass` for: `players=1`; `players=2`, `3` and `4`, each with `&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5`; `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&scenario=host-leave`; `players=2&scenario=server`. These are the hub's own test. Add `&play=60000` to a 2-player run and compare `__net.hashes` between frames. Then open the game alone | 3 min |\n975\t\n976\t**Stand-ins for what this machine lacks:** stub `navigator.getGamepads` with Playwright's `add_init_script` for a pad and for several; Playwright device profiles and `page.touchscreen` for touch; Web Audio renders for sound; two frames of the harness for a second player; 1920 × 1080 screenshots for the 10-foot view. Say in your feedback that real pads, a TV and ears weren't available.\n977\t\n978\tUse `node x replay labs/game/replays --browser sim` to hold Node and Chromium to the same hashes, and re-record only when play changes on purpose (`--update`), at milestones rather than every edit. `--bisect` when a hash moves by surprise. Screenshots only for what a script can't check: art, framing, layout.\n979\t\n980\t---\n981\t\n982\t## 15. Order of work\n983\t\n984\tKeep the game playing at each step, and `npm run verify -- sim` green.\n985\t\n986\t1. **Skeleton (prove every risky path first).** Workspace, title choice, one-file build, the starter's scene, bot and tests replaced by your own (keep the kinds of test it shows: golden replay, capture and restore, the bot wins on several seeds), `makeWorld` with one biome, walls as props, the crypt look, hero on seats, solo driver, lockstep driver, the hub card. Pass every `hub` scenario and open from `file://` **before writing gameplay**: these are the paths that are hardest to retrofit.\n987\t2. **Combat core.** Penitent, Shambler, Bonepicker, damage pipeline, hit feel, deaths, dodge, Wine, Wafers. Play it until the swing feels good, with sliders.\n988\t3. **All classes.** Every skill and form, resources, passives, Skills screen.\n989\t4. **Monsters.** All rows, elites, affixes, tokens, packs, zone streaming, destructibles, traps.\n990\t5. **Items.** Drops, rarity, affixes, Inventory, shops, Poor Box, sockets, Reliquaries, Vestments, visible gear.\n991\t6. **The story.** All zones and chunks, Evensong, quests, dialogue, voices, bosses, ending, music, credits. Scripted playthrough green.\n992\t7. **Long game.** Difficulties, Vigils, Devotion, three save slots.\n993\t8. **Together.** Full hub round, couch co-op, per-seat loot, revives. Node lockstep test green for the full game.\n994\t9. **Front end.** Settings, rebinding, prompts, Dev Mode, attract, touch notice, About.\n995\t10. **Polish.** Art pass per zone, sound pass, balance pass with the bot and sliders, full `npm run verify`.\n996\t11. **Finish.** Deliverable built; `ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md` honest; `labs/game/README.md` with the designer guide; About screen filled; the chat reply and exit interview as TASK.md asks (the Plan field is this file's name; in the catalogue fields: type Game, genre RPG, players 1–4, tags such as 3d, co-op, fantasy, boss fights). Remove test leftovers and stop your processes.\n997\t\n998\t---\n999\t\n1000\t## 16. Where TASK.md's asks are answered\n1001\t\n1002\t| TASK.md asks for | Here |\n1003\t| --- | --- |\n1004\t| Original game, source's themes and tone, not a recreation | §0, §1, §8 |\n1005\t| Genre and perspective | §1, §9.1 |\n1006\t| Title by a real random pick | §0 |\n1007\t| Research choice | §0 |\n1008\t| One HTML file, CDN optional | §13 |\n1009\t| The engine's full workspace, read-only | §2, §3 |\n1010\t| Art: native style, new assets, library for generic props | §9.1, §9.2 |\n1011\t| Animation: native system, new animations | §9.3 |\n1012\t| Audio in code, gibberish voices, music at 10% | §10 |\n1013\t| Online and multiplayer: hub, and the game on its own | §12 |\n1014\t| Dev folder, shared machine rules, ports and processes | §0, §2, §14 |\n1015\t| Performance unlimited | §0, §3 |\n1016\t| Headless tests, whole-game playthrough, one quiet command, no review subagents | §14, §0 |\n1017\t| Feature-complete vertical slice, infrastructure for the rest | §1, §3.11, §15 |\n1018\t| Dev mode, live sliders, reset | §3.10, §11.5 |\n1019\t| Attract mode at 10 s | §11.6 |"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b0d0401-1a79-4c2f-8a33-ba9239fdbfed","uuid":"15efb0a0-233d-4cc2-88ac-ea91907ba0f0","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:46:11.293Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211947__x8ab6bc/work/PLAN.md","content":"The engine's one-file recipe aimed at your page. **Verified: 4 to 12 s, 6.7 MB, opens from `file://`.** Output goes to the deliverable beside the dev folder.\n\n```js\n// labs/game/tools/build-one-file.mjs  <path to the deliverable>\nimport { build } from 'vite';\nimport { readFileSync, writeFileSync } from 'node:fs';\nimport { join, resolve } from 'node:path';\nconst root = resolve('.');\nconst result = await build({ root, configFile: false, logLevel: 'warn', base: './',\n  resolve: { alias: [{ find: /^three$/, replacement: 'three/webgpu' }] },\n  build: { write: false, modulePreload: false, cssCodeSplit: false, assetsInlineLimit: () => true, chunkSizeWarningLimit: Infinity,\n    rollupOptions: { input: { game: join(root, 'labs/game/index.html') }, output: { inlineDynamicImports: true } } } });\nconst files = {}; let html;\nfor (const item of (Array.isArray(result) ? result : [result]).flatMap((o) => o.output)) {\n  const text = item.type === 'chunk' ? item.code : typeof item.source === 'string' ? item.source : new TextDecoder().decode(item.source);\n  if (item.fileName.endsWith('.html')) html = text; else files[item.fileName] = text;\n}\nconst find = (ref) => files[Object.keys(files).find((f) => ref.endsWith('/' + f) || ref === f || ref === './' + f)];\nconst LOADED = /<script type=\"module\" crossorigin src=\"([^\"]+)\"><\\/script>|<link rel=\"stylesheet\" crossorigin href=\"([^\"]+)\">/g;\nlet out = html.replace(LOADED, (_t, script, style) => {\n  if (style) return `<style>${find(style)}</style>`;\n  const code = find(script).replaceAll('</script', '<\\\\/script');\n  if (code.includes('<!--')) throw new Error('inline script holds <!--: write it apart in the source');\n  return `<script type=\"module\">${code}</script>`;\n});\nconst client = readFileSync('labs/game/vendor/aihub-session.txt', 'utf8');          // session.js, unmodified\nout = out.replace('<meta charset=\"utf-8\" />', () => `<meta charset=\"utf-8\" />\\n<script>\\n${client}\\n</script>`);\nwriteFileSync(process.argv[2], out);\n```\n\nGet the client once: `curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/session.js -o labs/game/vendor/aihub-session.txt`. Assert in the test: first `<script>` follows the charset; the client's banner is intact; no `src` or `href` outside data URLs. Also add `hub:source` and `hub:type` metas.\n\n---\n\n## 14. Testing\n\n**`npm run verify` (add the script to the game's `package.json`; it runs `labs/game/tools/verify.mjs`) runs everything and prints only failures and one line of counts.** Its parts: `npm run verify -- sim`, `net`, `full`, `browser`, `hub`. Rerun only the part covering what you changed.\n\n| Part | What it proves | Rough time |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `sim` | `npm run check`, then Vitest: replay goldens, capture and restore, formulas, every skill form hits or does what its row says, every monster spawns, attacks and dies, every affix, every boss phase changes, Reliquary powers fire, loot distribution over 100,000 rolls, 50 seeds of generator connectivity, quest graph reachable, save round trip, balance targets of §4.2 by a fast bot | 2 min |\n| `net` | Four `createHeadless` copies running the lockstep driver over a fake hub, with random latency and a leave: `gameHash` equal at every checkpoint. The strongest net test, and cheap. Write the driver with its transport and stepper passed in, so the same code runs here. Software-rendered browsers can't get 3 or 4 copies warmed up in time here (a 3-player run left one copy at tick 0 with nothing to compare), so this one does that job | 1 min |\n| `full` | **The scripted playthrough:** the bot plays the whole story for each class on 1 seed, Q1 to Q12 through the credits, plus one Vigil, in Node, with `game.bal` speeding it and dev travel between objectives; asserts each quest flag, boss death, level, gear, no softlock | 5 to 10 min |\n| `browser` | The deliverable from `file://`, Playwright with the flags of §2 and `?quality=low&gfx.warmUp=asked`: boots, title, class select, play by keyboard and mouse, then by a stubbed pad; prompts follow device; Xbox setting; each screen opens and has content; dev sliders change a value and reset restores it; attract starts at 10 s and exits on input; phone profile shows the notice and its Settings; `pipelinesAfterWarmUp` 0; music bus at 0.1; `OfflineAudioContext` renders of a song and a voice line are non-silent; About has every field | 5 min |\n| `hub` | Download `harness.html`, `bridge.js` and `round.js` from `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/` into `out/hub/` and copy the deliverable there as `game.html`; `python3 -u -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` there; open `harness.html?game=game.html&<scenario>&auto=1`; confirm the frame's page is your game; wait for `document.body.dataset.complete`; assert `window.__hubCheck.pass` for: `players=1`; `players=2`, `3` and `4`, each with `&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5`; `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&scenario=host-leave`; `players=2&scenario=server`. These are the hub's own test. Add `&play=60000` to a 2-player run and compare `__net.hashes` between frames. Then open the game alone | 3 min |\n\n**Stand-ins for what this machine lacks:** stub `navigator.getGamepads` with Playwright's `add_init_script` for a pad and for several; Playwright device profiles and `page.touchscreen` for touch; Web Audio renders for sound; two frames of the harness for a second player; 1920 × 1080 screenshots for the 10-foot view. Say in your feedback that real pads, a TV and ears weren't available.\n\nUse `node x replay labs/game/replays --browser sim` to hold Node and Chromium to the same hashes, and re-record only when play changes on purpose (`--update`), at milestones rather than every edit. `--bisect` when a hash moves by surprise. Screenshots only for what a script can't check: art, framing, layout.\n\n---\n\n## 15. Order of work\n\nKeep the game playing at each step, and `npm run verify -- sim` green.\n\n1. **Skeleton (prove every risky path first).** Workspace, title choice, one-file build, the starter's scene, bot and tests replaced by your own (keep the kinds of test it shows: golden replay, capture and restore, the bot wins on several seeds), `makeWorld` with one biome, walls as props, the crypt look, hero on seats, solo driver, lockstep driver, the hub card. Pass every `hub` scenario and open from `file://` **before writing gameplay**: these are the paths that are hardest to retrofit.\n2. **Combat core.** Penitent, Shambler, Bonepicker, damage pipeline, hit feel, deaths, dodge, Wine, Wafers. Play it until the swing feels good, with sliders.\n3. **All classes.** Every skill and form, resources, passives, Skills screen.\n4. **Monsters.** All rows, elites, affixes, tokens, packs, zone streaming, destructibles, traps.\n5. **Items.** Drops, rarity, affixes, Inventory, shops, Poor Box, sockets, Reliquaries, Vestments, visible gear.\n6. **The story.** All zones and chunks, Evensong, quests, dialogue, voices, bosses, ending, music, credits. Scripted playthrough green.\n7. **Long game.** Difficulties, Vigils, Devotion, three save slots.\n8. **Together.** Full hub round, couch co-op, per-seat loot, revives. Node lockstep test green for the full game.\n9. **Front end.** Settings, rebinding, prompts, Dev Mode, attract, touch notice, About.\n10. **Polish.** Art pass per zone, sound pass, balance pass with the bot and sliders, full `npm run verify`.\n11. **Finish.** Deliverable built; `ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md` honest; `labs/game/README.md` with the designer guide; About screen filled; the chat reply and exit interview as TASK.md asks (the Plan field is this file's name; in the catalogue fields: type Game, genre RPG, players 1–4, tags such as 3d, co-op, fantasy, boss fights). Remove test leftovers and stop your processes.\n\n---\n\n## 16. Where TASK.md's asks are answered\n\n| TASK.md asks for | Here |\n| --- | --- |\n| Original game, source's themes and tone, not a recreation | §0, §1, §8 |\n| Genre and perspective | §1, §9.1 |\n| Title by a real random pick | §0 |\n| Research choice | §0 |\n| One HTML file, CDN optional | §13 |\n| The engine's full workspace, read-only | §2, §3 |\n| Art: native style, new assets, library for generic props | §9.1, §9.2 |\n| Animation: native system, new animations | §9.3 |\n| Audio in code, gibberish voices, music at 10% | §10 |\n| Online and multiplayer: hub, and the game on its own | §12 |\n| Dev folder, shared machine rules, ports and processes | §0, §2, §14 |\n| Performance unlimited | §0, §3 |\n| Headless tests, whole-game playthrough, one quiet command, no review subagents | §14, §0 |\n| Feature-complete vertical slice, infrastructure for the rest | §1, §3.11, §15 |\n| Dev mode, live sliders, reset | §3.10, §11.5 |\n| Attract mode at 10 s | §11.6 |","numLines":90,"startLine":930,"totalLines":1025}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Nnfw4GvTwrvYBgY8baRpDz","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
